        "tool_calls": [
          {
            "id": "toolu_013z1RfvAc1F9RYyrLHej4yF",
            "type": "function",
            "function": {
              "name": "edit",
              "arguments": "{\"path\": \"/home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator/.fractal-factory/domain-model.json\", \"old_str\": \"{\\n  \\\"version\\\": 1,\\n  \\\"lastUpdated\\\": null,\\n  \\\"subdomains\\\": [],\\n  \\\"invariants\\\": [],\\n  \\\"existingAssets\\\": [],\\n  \\\"exemplarPatterns\\\": []\\n}\", \"new_str\": \"{\\n  \\\"version\\\": 1,\\n  \\\"lastUpdated\\\": \\\"2026-03-15T19:00:19Z\\\",\\n  \\\"subdomains\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"SD-001\\\",\\n      \\\"name\\\": \\\"user-interaction\\\",\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Guide agent as sole user-facing entry point: gathers story idea, optional style samples, mood/tone, character sketches, world fragments, and constraints. Validates inputs, fills defaults, writes story-config.json, confirms with user, launches the autonomous pipeline, and reports results.\\\",\\n      \\\"sourceFiles\\\": [\\\".fractal-factory/domain-brief.md\\\"],\\n      \\\"complexity\\\": \\\"low\\\",\\n      \\\"estimatedAgentCount\\\": 1,\\n      \\\"crossCuttingConcerns\\\": [\\\"artifact-management\\\"],\\n      \\\"discoveredBy\\\": \\\"fractal-factory-domain-scanner\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"SD-002\\\",\\n      \\\"name\\\": \\\"concept-development\\\",\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Phase 1 of the creative pipeline: distills raw inputs into a crystallized story concept. Includes idea distillation (thematic core), theme extraction (2-3 thematic pillars), premise refinement (one-liner + paragraph hook), comparable title identification, and initial craft toolbox selection producing a Story Craft Profile.\\\",\\n      \\\"sourceFiles\\\": [\\\".fractal-factory/domain-brief.md\\\", \\\".fractal-factory/invariants.md\\\"],\\n      \\\"complexity\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\\n      \\\"estimatedAgentCount\\\": 2,\\n      \\\"crossCuttingConcerns\\\": [\\\"genre-compliance\\\", \\\"craft-toolbox-framework\\\", \\\"adversarial-quality-gates\\\"],\\n      \\\"discoveredBy\\\": \\\"fractal-factory-domain-scanner\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"SD-003\\\",\\n      \\\"name\\\": \\\"world-building\\\",\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Phase 2: constructs the complete fictional world in subcategorized artifacts. Covers geography/setting (maps, regions, climates, travel distances), magic system design (rules, costs, limitations per Sanderson's Laws), political/social structures (kingdoms, factions, class, religion), history/lore (key events, creation myths, legends), culture/daily life (customs, food, clothing, languages, festivals, taboos), and flora/fauna. Produces a consistency bible decomposed into typed subdirectories.\\\",\\n      \\\"sourceFiles\\\": [\\\".fractal-factory/domain-brief.md\\\"],\\n      \\\"complexity\\\": \\\"high\\\",\\n      \\\"estimatedAgentCount\\\": 4,\\n      \\\"crossCuttingConcerns\\\": [\\\"continuity-tracking\\\", \\\"series-knowledge-management\\\", \\\"adversarial-quality-gates\\\", \\\"artifact-management\\\"],\\n      \\\"discoveredBy\\\": \\\"fractal-factory-domain-scanner\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"SD-004\\\",\\n      \\\"name\\\": \\\"character-design\\\",\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Phase 3: creates full character profiles for romantic leads (backstory, psychological wounds, desires, flaws, strengths, voice patterns), designs the romance arc dynamic (attraction/obstacles/vulnerability/climax), builds supporting cast with mini-arcs, designs antagonist with comprehensible motivation, writes per-character voice guides with distinct speech patterns, and maps the full relationship web between all named characters.\\\",\\n      \\\"sourceFiles\\\": [\\\".fractal-factory/domain-brief.md\\\", \\\".fractal-factory/invariants.md\\\"],\\n      \\\"complexity\\\": \\\"high\\\",\\n      \\\"estimatedAgentCount\\\": 3,\\n      \\\"crossCuttingConcerns\\\": [\\\"genre-compliance\\\", \\\"continuity-tracking\\\", \\\"adversarial-quality-gates\\\", \\\"series-knowledge-management\\\"],\\n      \\\"discoveredBy\\\": \\\"fractal-factory-domain-scanner\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"SD-005\\\",\\n      \\\"name\\\": \\\"plot-architecture\\\",\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Phase 4: selects and applies a story structure framework (3-Act, Save the Cat, Hero's Journey, 7-Point, or Romance Arc), then produces a chapter-level scene-by-scene outline specifying POV, goal, conflict, disaster/resolution, emotional arc, romance beats, fantasy plot beats, and worldbuilding reveals per scene. Includes tension mapping (pacing chart), subplot tracking with intersection points, and the critical dual-arc interleave ensuring fantasy and romance beats reinforce each other.\\\",\\n      \\\"sourceFiles\\\": [\\\".fractal-factory/domain-brief.md\\\", \\\".fractal-factory/invariants.md\\\"],\\n      \\\"complexity\\\": \\\"high\\\",\\n      \\\"estimatedAgentCount\\\": 3,\\n      \\\"crossCuttingConcerns\\\": [\\\"genre-compliance\\\", \\\"craft-toolbox-framework\\\", \\\"adversarial-quality-gates\\\", \\\"continuity-tracking\\\"],\\n      \\\"discoveredBy\\\": \\\"fractal-factory-domain-scanner\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"SD-006\\\",\\n      \\\"name\\\": \\\"prose-style-development\\\",\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Phase 5: if reference stories are provided, analyzes them for abstract stylistic patterns (sentence length distribution, vocabulary register, metaphor density/type, dialogue-to-narration ratio, interior monologue style, paragraph rhythm). Produces a concrete style guide for the story and a tone palette mapping emotional tones to scene types (action=staccato/visceral, romantic=sensory/languid, political=precise/tense). Influence must be structural/tonal only, never substantive.\\\",\\n      \\\"sourceFiles\\\": [\\\".fractal-factory/domain-brief.md\\\", \\\".fractal-factory/invariants.md\\\"],\\n      \\\"complexity\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\\n      \\\"estimatedAgentCount\\\": 2,\\n      \\\"crossCuttingConcerns\\\": [\\\"originality-assurance\\\", \\\"adversarial-quality-gates\\\", \\\"series-knowledge-management\\\"],\\n      \\\"discoveredBy\\\": \\\"fractal-factory-domain-scanner\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"SD-007\\\",\\n      \\\"name\\\": \\\"chapter-drafting\\\",\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Phase 6: the core prose production engine. Writes each chapter sequentially following the outline, maintaining consistent character voice per POV, scene structure (goal/conflict/disaster), prose style adherence, worldbuilding consistency, romance arc pacing, and chapter hooks (opening hooks + closing cliffhangers). Chapters MUST be produced in order (N+1 only after N is complete with continuity recorded). Updates a running continuity document after each chapter.\\\",\\n      \\\"sourceFiles\\\": [\\\".fractal-factory/domain-brief.md\\\", \\\".fractal-factory/invariants.md\\\"],\\n      \\\"complexity\\\": \\\"high\\\",\\n      \\\"estimatedAgentCount\\\": 4,\\n      \\\"crossCuttingConcerns\\\": [\\\"continuity-tracking\\\", \\\"genre-compliance\\\", \\\"adversarial-quality-gates\\\", \\\"craft-toolbox-framework\\\"],\\n      \\\"discoveredBy\\\": \\\"fractal-factory-domain-scanner\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"SD-008\\\",\\n      \\\"name\\\": \\\"revision-editing\\\",\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Phase 7: exhaustive multi-pass self-editing. Developmental edit (plot holes, pacing, character motivation gaps, romance arc satisfaction, worldbuilding contradictions, theme reinforcement, structural problems). Line edit (prose quality, dialogue naturalism, overwriting/underwriting, repetitive usage, show vs. tell, cliché detection, POV consistency). Copy edit (grammar, naming consistency, timeline accuracy, factual accuracy within world rules). Every revision must cite what finding prompted it for full traceability.\\\",\\n      \\\"sourceFiles\\\": [\\\".fractal-factory/domain-brief.md\\\", \\\".fractal-factory/invariants.md\\\"],\\n      \\\"complexity\\\": \\\"high\\\",\\n      \\\"estimatedAgentCount\\\": 4,\\n      \\\"crossCuttingConcerns\\\": [\\\"continuity-tracking\\\", \\\"craft-toolbox-framework\\\", \\\"genre-compliance\\\"],\\n      \\\"discoveredBy\\\": \\\"fractal-factory-domain-scanner\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"SD-009\\\",\\n      \\\"name\\\": \\\"beta-reading-simulation\\\",\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Phase 8: deep multi-perspective simulated beta reading through 5 independent reviewer lenses. Romance Reader (relationship quality, romantic beats, chemistry, heat consistency, HEA/HFN). Fantasy Reader (worldbuilding immersion, magic consistency, stakes, fantasy-romance integration). Craft Reader (prose quality audit, voice consistency, POV violations, continuity, emotional authenticity, dialogue distinctness, pacing). Sensitivity Reader (representation, power dynamics, consent, cultural elements). Originality Reader (plagiarism detection, transformative influence verification). Each lens produces structured severity-rated findings.\\\",\\n      \\\"sourceFiles\\\": [\\\".fractal-factory/domain-brief.md\\\", \\\".fractal-factory/invariants.md\\\"],\\n      \\\"complexity\\\": \\\"high\\\",\\n      \\\"estimatedAgentCount\\\": 6,\\n      \\\"crossCuttingConcerns\\\": [\\\"genre-compliance\\\", \\\"originality-assurance\\\", \\\"continuity-tracking\\\"],\\n      \\\"discoveredBy\\\": \\\"fractal-factory-domain-scanner\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"SD-010\\\",\\n      \\\"name\\\": \\\"polish-delivery\\\",\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Phase 9: final proofread for typos/formatting/consistency, generation of one-paragraph chapter summaries, series knowledge base update (promoting canonical facts from the book into series-level artifacts), and assembly of the complete delivery package with all output artifacts organized and cross-referenced under the book directory.\\\",\\n      \\\"sourceFiles\\\": [\\\".fractal-factory/domain-brief.md\\\"],\\n      \\\"complexity\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\\n      \\\"estimatedAgentCount\\\": 2,\\n      \\\"crossCuttingConcerns\\\": [\\\"series-knowledge-management\\\", \\\"artifact-management\\\", \\\"continuity-tracking\\\"],\\n      \\\"discoveredBy\\\": \\\"fractal-factory-domain-scanner\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"SD-011\\\",\\n      \\\"name\\\": \\\"adversarial-quality-gates\\\",\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Cross-cutting system of adversarial consistency auditors that gate every creative phase (Phases 1-6). Each auditor receives phase output, actively tries to find contradictions/gaps/logic failures/weak spots, cross-references against ALL prior phase artifacts, produces severity-rated findings (critical/major/minor), and blocks phase completion if any criticals exist. Includes the 'Kill Your Darlings' mandate — hunting for beautiful-but-purposeless passages and elements. Phase-specific focus areas differ (concept coherence, worldbuilding physics, character motivation, plot logic, style consistency, draft quality).\\\",\\n      \\\"sourceFiles\\\": [\\\".fractal-factory/domain-brief.md\\\", \\\".fractal-factory/invariants.md\\\"],\\n      \\\"complexity\\\": \\\"high\\\",\\n      \\\"estimatedAgentCount\\\": 4,\\n      \\\"crossCuttingConcerns\\\": [\\\"continuity-tracking\\\", \\\"genre-compliance\\\", \\\"craft-toolbox-framework\\\"],\\n      \\\"discoveredBy\\\": \\\"fractal-factory-domain-scanner\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"SD-012\\\",\\n      \\\"name\\\": \\\"continuity-tracking\\\",\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Cross-cutting system for maintaining story consistency across chapters and books. Tracks character locations, timeline progression, what each character knows at each point, promises made to the reader (Chekhov's guns), physical descriptions, names/titles, and open plot threads. Updated after every chapter draft. For sequels, extends the series-level continuity tracker. Feeds into adversarial auditors and beta readers. Includes the character knowledge matrix and reader promises tracker.\\\",\\n      \\\"sourceFiles\\\": [\\\".fractal-factory/domain-brief.md\\\", \\\".fractal-factory/invariants.md\\\"],\\n      \\\"complexity\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\\n      \\\"estimatedAgentCount\\\": 2,\\n      \\\"crossCuttingConcerns\\\": [\\\"series-knowledge-management\\\", \\\"adversarial-quality-gates\\\", \\\"artifact-management\\\"],\\n      \\\"discoveredBy\\\": \\\"fractal-factory-domain-scanner\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"SD-013\\\",\\n      \\\"name\\\": \\\"series-knowledge-management\\\",\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Cross-cutting system for series production. Manages the series knowledge base lifecycle: creates series-level canonical directories from book-1 artifacts, merges each completed book's new facts into series-level resources (characters, world, timeline, magic, naming), tracks unresolved threads tagged by origin book, enforces cross-book consistency rules (append-mostly facts, no silent retcons, voice guide carryover, magic system expansion-not-contradiction), and provides the sequel input contract (series KB + summaries + unresolved threads).\\\",\\n      \\\"sourceFiles\\\": [\\\".fractal-factory/domain-brief.md\\\", \\\".fractal-factory/invariants.md\\\"],\\n      \\\"complexity\\\": \\\"high\\\",\\n      \\\"estimatedAgentCount\\\": 3,\\n      \\\"crossCuttingConcerns\\\": [\\\"continuity-tracking\\\", \\\"artifact-management\\\", \\\"world-building\\\", \\\"character-design\\\"],\\n      \\\"discoveredBy\\\": \\\"fractal-factory-domain-scanner\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"SD-014\\\",\\n      \\\"name\\\": \\\"artifact-management\\\",\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Cross-cutting system for organizing output artifacts per the subcategory decomposition rules. Enforces per-book directory isolation (book-1/, book-2/), typed subdirectories within each artifact type (world/geography/, world/magic/, etc.), self-contained subcategory files loadable independently, relative-path cross-references between subcategories, and the series-mirrors-book directory schema. Prevents monolithic files and ensures agents can load only the artifacts they need without context-window waste.\\\",\\n      \\\"sourceFiles\\\": [\\\".fractal-factory/domain-brief.md\\\", \\\".fractal-factory/invariants.md\\\"],\\n      \\\"complexity\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\\n      \\\"estimatedAgentCount\\\": 2,\\n      \\\"crossCuttingConcerns\\\": [\\\"series-knowledge-management\\\"],\\n      \\\"discoveredBy\\\": \\\"fractal-factory-domain-scanner\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"SD-015\\\",\\n      \\\"name\\\": \\\"genre-compliance\\\",\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Cross-cutting enforcement of romantic fantasy genre conventions. Ensures fantasy-first plot (quests, magical conflicts, political intrigue) with romance as emotional spine (not the reverse). Enforces slow-burn pacing through recognizable stages (awareness→attraction→tension→vulnerability→setback→deepening→commitment), HEA/HFN ending promise, dual-POV handling, popular trope execution, heat-level consistency with stated target, and both leads having equal development and agency. Prevents genre-promise violations.\\\",\\n      \\\"sourceFiles\\\": [\\\".fractal-factory/domain-brief.md\\\", \\\".fractal-factory/invariants.md\\\"],\\n      \\\"complexity\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\\n      \\\"estimatedAgentCount\\\": 2,\\n      \\\"crossCuttingConcerns\\\": [\\\"adversarial-quality-gates\\\", \\\"beta-reading-simulation\\\", \\\"character-design\\\", \\\"plot-architecture\\\"],\\n      \\\"discoveredBy\\\": \\\"fractal-factory-domain-scanner\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"SD-016\\\",\\n      \\\"name\\\": \\\"craft-toolbox-framework\\\",\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Cross-cutting two-tier quality system. Non-negotiable invariants (28 rules across narrative, structural, quality, originality, and process categories) apply to every story always. The craft toolbox (14 techniques: Scene-Sequel, value shifts, Five Commandments, try-fail cycles, tone contract, stakes escalation, Black Moment, internal romantic resistance, subtext, Sanderson's First Law, kill-your-darlings, dual-arc interleave, tension mapping, MRU) is selectively applied per-story during concept/plotting. Produces the Story Craft Profile artifact. Adversarial auditors verify against selected tools, not the full set.\\\",\\n      \\\"sourceFiles\\\": [\\\".fractal-factory/domain-brief.md\\\", \\\".fractal-factory/invariants.md\\\"],\\n      \\\"complexity\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\\n      \\\"estimatedAgentCount\\\": 2,\\n      \\\"crossCuttingConcerns\\\": [\\\"adversarial-quality-gates\\\", \\\"concept-development\\\", \\\"plot-architecture\\\"],\\n      \\\"discoveredBy\\\": \\\"fractal-factory-domain-scanner\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"SD-017\\\",\\n      \\\"name\\\": \\\"originality-assurance\\\",\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Cross-cutting system ensuring all output is entirely original. Enforces zero-tolerance plagiarism rules: no directly quotable or closely paraphraseable content from existing works. When style samples are provided, ensures only abstract stylistic patterns are extracted (sentence rhythm, vocabulary register, metaphor density) — never specific content, metaphors, character archetypes, plot sequences, or world elements. Includes the dedicated originality reader lens in beta reading and the originality self-audit invariant.\\\",\\n      \\\"sourceFiles\\\": [\\\".fractal-factory/domain-brief.md\\\", \\\".fractal-factory/invariants.md\\\"],\\n      \\\"complexity\\\": \\\"low\\\",\\n      \\\"estimatedAgentCount\\\": 1,\\n      \\\"crossCuttingConcerns\\\": [\\\"beta-reading-simulation\\\", \\\"prose-style-development\\\", \\\"chapter-drafting\\\"],\\n      \\\"discoveredBy\\\": \\\"fractal-factory-domain-scanner\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"invariants\\\": [],\\n  \\\"existingAssets\\\": [],\\n  \\\"exemplarPatterns\\\": []\\n}\"}"
