2026-03-15T19:03:00.857Z [INFO] Custom agent "fractal-factory-invariant-extractor" invoked with prompt: You are the Fractal Factory Invariant Extractor. Execute your task now.

**Working directory**: /home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator
**Factory root**: .fractal-factory/

**Your inputs**:
- `.fractal-factory/context.json` — factory configuration
- `.fractal-factory/domain-brief.md` — comprehensive domain brief (~31KB) for a romantic fantasy fiction writer agent system
- `.fractal-factory/invariants.md` — contains 28 explicit invariants (INV-001 through INV-028) plus 14 Craft Toolbox items that define the creative and quality constraints for the system
- `.fractal-factory/domain-model.json` — already populated by the domain scanner with 17 subdomains. You must ADD invariants to this file without removing the existing subdomain data.

**Your job**:
1. Read `.fractal-factory/invariants.md` thoroughly — it contains numbered invariants (INV-001 through INV-028) organized into categories (Structural, Behavioral, Quality, Workflow) plus 14 Craft Toolbox items
2. Also read `.fractal-factory/domain-brief.md` for any additional implicit invariants not in the invariants file
3. Extract ALL invariants and add them to the `invariants` array in `.fractal-factory/domain-model.json` — each invariant needs: id, text, category (structural/behavioral/quality/workflow), severity (must/should/may), appliesTo (which subdomain IDs), source
4. Map each invariant to the subdomains it applies to using the subdomain IDs already in domain-model.json (SD-001 through SD-017)
5. Write your status to `.fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory-invariant-extractor/status.json`

The invariants cover things like:
- Genre compliance (romantic fantasy conventions)
- Quality gates (adversarial review requirements)
- Continuity tracking requirements
- Series bible management
- Prose quality standards
- Craft toolbox techniques
- Workflow sequencing rules

Be thorough — capture every invariant from both sources. These invariants will be enforced throughout the agent system.
