\n\\n# Source breakdown\\nlines.append(\\"## Source Breakdown\\")\\nlines.append(\\"\\")\\nexplicit_count = sum(1 for inv in invs if 'invariants.md' in inv['source'] and 'domain-brief' not in inv['source'])\\nimplicit_count = sum(1 for inv in invs if 'domain-brief.md' in inv['source'])\\nlines.append(f\\"- **From invariants.md (explicit)**: {explicit_count} invariants (INV-001 through INV-046)\\")\\nlines.append(f\\"  - 31 core invariants (I1–I28 including I14a, I14b, I14c)\\")\\nlines.append(f\\"  - 1 craft toolbox framework rule\\")\\nlines.append(f\\"  - 14 craft toolbox technique definitions (T1–T14)\\")\\nlines.append(f\\"- **From domain-brief.md (implicit)**: {implicit_count} invariants (INV-047 through INV-064)\\")\\nlines.append(f\\"  - Architectural constraints, series management rules, quality expectations\\")\\nlines.append(\\"\\")\\n\\n# Full invariant table\\nlines.append(\\"## Full Invariant Table\\")\\nlines.append(\\"\\")\\nlines.append(\\"| ID | Description | Classification | Confidence | Source |\\")\\nlines.append(\\"|---|---|---|---|---|\\")\\nfor inv in invs:\\n    desc = inv['description'][:120] + \\"...\\" if len(inv['description']) > 120 else inv['description']\\n    lines.append(f\\"| {inv['id']} | {desc} | {inv['classification']} | {inv['confidence']} | {inv['source'].split(',')[0]} |\\")\\nlines.append(\\"\\")\\n\\n# Invariants flagged for verification (none < 0.5)\\nlines.append(\\"## Invariants Flagged for User Verification\\")\\nlines.append(\\"\\")\\nlow_conf = [inv for inv in invs if inv['confidence'] < 0.5]\\nif low_conf:\\n    for inv in low_conf:\\n        lines.append(f\\"- **{inv['id']}** ({inv['confidence']}): {inv['description']}\\")\\nelse:\\n    lines.append(\\"No invariants below confidence 0.5. All extracted invariants are either explicitly stated (0.9–1.0) or strongly implied by multiple passages (0.7–0.8).\\")\\nlines.append(\\"\\")\\n\\n# Coverage analysis\\nlines.append(\\"## Subdomain Coverage\\")\\nlines.append(\\"\\")\\nlines.append(\\"| Subdomain | ID | Invariants Applied |\\")\\nlines.append(\\"|---|---|---|\\")\\nfor sd in model['subdomains']:\\n    count = sum(1 for inv in invs if sd['id'] in inv['affectedSubdomains'])\\n    lines.append(f\\"| {sd['name']} | {sd['id']} | {count} |\\")\\nlines.append(\\"\\")\\n\\nlines.append(\\"## Key Observations\\")\\nlines.append(\\"\\")\\nlines.append(\\"1. **Highest-coverage subdomains**: chapter-drafting (SD-007), revision-editing (SD-008), beta-reading-simulation (SD-009), and adversarial-quality-gates (SD-011) — these are the execution and quality enforcement cores of the system.\\")\\nlines.append(\\"2. **The craft toolbox creates a two-tier quality system**: 31 non-negotiable invariants that always apply + 14 selectable techniques that become binding per-story. The framework rule (INV-032) bridges the two tiers.\\")\\nlines.append(\\"3. **Originality is deeply embedded**: 3 explicit invariants (INV-023–025) plus the originality reader lens (INV-053) create a multi-layered plagiarism defense.\\")\\nlines.append(\\"4. **Series production is a first-class concern**: 6 invariants (INV-031, INV-049, INV-051, INV-056, INV-057, INV-059) govern cross-book consistency, making sequel production architecturally safe.\\")\\nlines.append(\\"5. **Adversarial quality gates are pervasive**: INV-026, INV-052, INV-062 ensure every creative phase is stress-tested before advancing, with critical findings as hard blockers.\\")\\n\\noutput_text = \\"\\\\n\\".join(lines)\\n\\nwith open('.fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory-invariant-extractor/output.md', 'w') as f:\\n    f.write(output_text)\\n\\nprint(\\"Output report written.\\")\\n\\n# Write status\\nstatus = {\\n    \\"agent\\": \\"fractal-factory-invariant-extractor\\",\\n    \\"task_id\\": \\"pass1/invariant-extraction\\",\\n    \\"status\\": \\"completed\\",\\n    \\"result\\": \\"extracted\\",\\n    \\"summary\\": f\\"Extracted {len(invs)} invariants ({class_counts.get('behavioral',0)} behavioral, {class_counts.get('structural',0)} structural, {class_counts.get('quality',0)} quality, {class_counts.get('workflow',0)} workflow). {conf_bands['0.9–1.0 (explicit)']} high-confidence, {conf_bands['0.7–0.8 (strongly implied)']} medium-confidence. 0 need verification.\\",\\n    \\"artifacts\\": [\\"domain-model.json\\", \\"agents/fractal-factory-invariant-extractor/output.md\\"],\\n    \\"next_hint\\": \\"fractal-factory-asset-auditor\\",\\n    \\"iteration\\": 1\\n}\\n\\nwith open('.fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory-invariant-extractor/status.json', 'w') as f:\\n    json.dump(status, f, indent=2)\\n\\nprint(\\"Status written.\\")\\n\\n# Update manifest\\nwith open('.fractal-factory/manifest.json', 'r') as f:\\n    manifest = json.load(f)\\n\\nmanifest.insert(0, {\\n    \\"timestamp\\": datetime.now(timezone.utc).strftime(\\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ\\"),\\n    \\"agent\\": \\"fractal-factory-invariant-extractor\\",\\n    \\"artifacts\\": [\\"domain-model.json\\", \\"agents/fractal-factory-invariant-extractor/output.md\\"],\\n    \\"status\\": \\"completed\\",\\n    \\"result\\": \\"extracted\\",\\n    \\"iteration\\": 1\\n})\\n\\nwith open('.fractal-factory/manifest.json', 'w') as f:\\n    json.dump(manifest, f, indent=2)\\n\\nprint(\\"Manifest updated.\\")\\nprint(\\"\\\\nDone. All artifacts written successfully.\\")\\nPYEOF","description":"Write status, output report, and manifest","initial_wait":30}`,
