      'gen_ai.tool.call.result': '1. ## Source Code References in Comments\n' +
        '2. \n' +
        '3. When citing Xperience source code in JIRA comments or handoff files, include navigable links to the source browser so reviewers can click through and verify.\n' +
        '4. \n' +
        '5. ### URL format\n' +
        '6. \n' +
        '7. ```\n' +
        '8. https://app-xbyk-source-prod.azurewebsites.net/#<Namespace/Path/ClassName.cs>,<LineNumber>\n' +
        '9. ```\n' +
        '10. \n' +
        "11. The URL path uses the **fully-qualified .NET namespace** from the source file's `namespace` declaration, not the filesystem path. The line number is optional but recommended. **Critical:** The namespace almost always starts with `CMS.`\n" +
        '12. \n' +
        '13. Example:\n' +
        '14. - File on disk: `CMSSolution/DbDataManager/Installation/SqlInstallationHelper.cs`\n' +
        '15. - Namespace in file: `namespace CMS.DbDataManager.Installation`\n' +
        '16. - Correct URL: `https://app-xbyk-source-prod.azurewebsites.net/#CMS.DbDataManager/Installation/SqlInstallationHelper.cs,222`\n' +
        '17. - Wrong URL: `https://app-xbyk-source-prod.azurewebsites.net/#DbDataManager/Installation/SqlInstallationHelper.cs,222` (missing `CMS.` prefix)\n' +
        '18. \n' +
        '19. Post as a JIRA link: `[ClassName.cs:L222|<url>]`'
    },
