        '2. name: devralph-build-verification\n' +
        '3. description: "Build verification and error troubleshooting reference. Covers primary build commands (npm run build, npm run serve, npx gulp rspec_tests), common failure patterns across Jekyll/Liquid, Ruby gems, Webpack, Less/Tailwind CSS, and the Gulp pipeline, plus diagnosis strategies for each. Use this skill before committing any changes, when any build step fails, when you see unfamiliar error output, or when you need the verification checklist for your type of change — the build pipeline has 5 sequential stages where errors in one stage often masquerade as problems in another, so understanding the pipeline order matters for diagnosis."\n' +
        '4. ---\n' +
        '5. {% raw %}\n' +
        '6. \n' +
        '7. # Build Verification\n' +
        '8. \n' +
        '9. ## Primary Build Commands\n' +
        '10. \n' +
        '11. Run these to verify your changes work:\n' +
        '12. \n' +
        '13. | Command | What it checks | When to run |\n' +
        '14. |---------|---------------|-------------|\n' +
        '15. | `npm run build` | Full site: config merge → dependencies → assets (Less, Tailwind, Webpack) → Jekyll build + validation | After every change, before committing |\n' +
        '16. | `npx gulp rspec_tests` | RSpec tests for all Ruby gems (kentico-core, liquid-kfm, learn-portal, etc.) | After modifying any gem in `gems/` |\n' +
        '17. | `npm run codesamples:build` (or `cd src/_code && dotnet build`) | .NET code sample compilation | After modifying any `.cs` files in `src/_code/` |\n' +
        '18. \n' +
        '19. ## Build Pipeline Order\n' +
        '20. \n' +
        '21. ```\n' +
        '22. 1. Config merge (jekyll merge_configs)\n' +
        '23. 2. Dependency generation (jekyll generate_dependencies → pagetrees, search/404 pages)\n' +
        '24. 3. Assets\n' +
        '25.    a. Delete old CSS/JS → rebuild Less → rebuild Tailwind → copy to build/\n' +
        '26.    b. Webpack bundle JS → copy vendor JS → copy to build/\n' +
        '27.    c. Copy fonts, images, SVGs\n' +
        '28. 4. Jekyll build (--source src/ --destination src/_site/)\n' +
        '29.    → Liquid rendering (all custom tags run here)\n' +
        '30.    → Pandoc markdown conversion\n' +
        '31.    → Validation (infrastructure + markdown checks)\n' +
        '32. 5. Output → src/_site/\n' +
        '33. ```\n' +
        '34. \n' +
        '35. ## Common Build Failures\n' +
        '36. \n' +
        '37. ### Jekyll / Liquid Tag Errors\n' +
        '38. \n' +
        '39. **Broken page_link identifier**\n' +
        '40. ```\n' +
        '41. identifier "unknownID" not found\n' +
        '42. ```\n' +
        '43. Fix: Check for typos in the identifier. If the target page was removed, update or remove the link.\n' +
        '44. \n' +
        '45. **Missing anchor**\n' +
        '46. ```\n' +
        '47. anchor "myAnchor" not defined in current page\n' +
        '48. ```\n' +
        '49. Fix: Add `{% anchor myAnchor %}` at the target location, or fix the typo.\n' +
        '50. \n' +
        '51. **Unknown tag parameter**\n' +
        '52. ```\n' +
        '53. Unknown parameter "badParam" for tag "image"\n' +
        '54. ```\n' +
        "55. Fix: Check the tag's `SUPPORTED_PARAMS` in its Ruby class. Remove the unsupported parameter.\n" +
        '56. \n' +
        '57. **Duplicate identifier**\n' +
        '58. ```\n' +
        '59. duplicate identifier "ABCDE" found in collection\n' +
        '60. ```\n' +
        "61. Fix: Each page's `identifier` frontmatter value must be unique within the collection.\n" +
        '62. \n' +
        '63. ### Ruby Gem Errors\n' +
        '64. \n' +
        '65. **Gem load failure**\n' +
        '66. ```\n' +
        '67. cannot load such file -- kentico-core (LoadError)\n' +
        '68. ```\n' +
        '69. Fix: Run `bundle install` in the project root. If a specific gem fails, check its `gemspec` dependencies.\n' +
        '70. '
    },
