      'gen_ai.tool.call.result': '1. ---\n' +
        '2. name: code-typescript-review\n' +
        '3. description: Perform comprehensive code reviews for TypeScript projects, analyzing type safety, best practices, performance, security, and code quality with actionable feedback\n' +
        '4. ---\n' +
        '5. \n' +
        '6. # TypeScript Code Review Skill\n' +
        '7. \n' +
        '8. Perform thorough, professional code reviews for TypeScript code with focus on type safety, best practices, performance, security, and maintainability.\n' +
        '9. \n' +
        '10. ## Review Process\n' +
        '11. \n' +
        '12. When reviewing TypeScript code, follow this structured approach:\n' +
        '13. \n' +
        '14. ### 1. Initial Assessment\n' +
        "15. - Understand the code's purpose and context\n" +
        '16. - Identify the scope (single file, module, feature, or entire codebase)\n' +
        '17. - Note the TypeScript version and configuration (check `tsconfig.json`)\n' +
        '18. - Review any relevant documentation or comments\n' +
        '19. \n' +
        '20. ### 2. Core Review Categories\n' +
        '21. \n' +
        '22. #### Type Safety\n' +
        '23. - **Strict mode compliance**: Verify `strict: true` in tsconfig.json and adherence\n' +
        '24. - **Type annotations**: Check for proper type annotations, avoid implicit `any`\n' +
        '25. - **Type narrowing**: Ensure proper use of type guards and narrowing\n' +
        '26. - **Generic types**: Review generic usage for flexibility without sacrificing safety\n' +
        '27. - **Union and intersection types**: Verify correct usage and handling\n' +
        '28. - **Type assertions**: Flag unnecessary or dangerous type assertions (`as`, `!`)\n' +
        '29. - **Null/undefined handling**: Check for proper optional chaining (`?.`) and nullish coalescing (`??`)\n' +
        '30. - **Return types**: Ensure all functions have explicit return types\n' +
        '31. - **Discriminated unions**: Verify proper exhaustiveness checking\n' +
        '32. \n' +
        '33. #### Code Quality & Best Practices\n' +
        '34. - **Naming conventions**: Check for clear, descriptive names (camelCase for variables/functions, PascalCase for types/classes)\n' +
        '35. - **Function length**: Flag functions longer than ~50 lines or with high complexity\n' +
        '36. - **Single responsibility**: Ensure functions and classes have one clear purpose\n' +
        '37. - **DRY principle**: Identify duplicate code that should be extracted\n' +
        '38. - **Magic numbers/strings**: Flag hardcoded values that should be constants\n' +
        '39. - **Error handling**: Review try-catch usage, error types, and error messages\n' +
        '40. - **Async/await**: Check for proper async handling, avoid mixing callbacks/promises\n' +
        '41. - **Immutability**: Prefer `const` over `let`, check for array/object mutations\n' +
        '42. - **Enums vs unions**: Recommend const enums or union types over regular enums when appropriate\n' +
        '43. \n' +
        '44. #### Modern TypeScript Features\n' +
        '45. - **Optional chaining**: Suggest using `?.` for nested property access\n' +
        '46. - **Nullish coalescing**: Recommend `??` over `||` for default values\n' +
        '47. - **Template literal types**: Check for opportunities to use template literals\n' +
        '48. - **Utility types**: Suggest `Partial`, `Pick`, `Omit`, `Record`, etc. where appropriate\n' +
        '49. - **Const assertions**: Recommend `as const` for literal types\n' +
        '50. - **Type predicates**: Use for custom type guards\n' +
        '51. - **`satisfies` operator**: Use instead of type assertions when validating types\n' +
        '52. \n' +
        '53. #### Performance\n' +
        '54. - **Unnecessary re-renders**: In React/frameworks, check for memo usage, dependency arrays\n' +
        '55. - **Large bundle imports**: Flag entire library imports when tree-shaking is possible\n' +
        '56. - **Inefficient algorithms**: Identify O(n²) or worse when better options exist\n' +
        '57. - **Memory leaks**: Check for cleanup in event listeners, subscriptions, timers\n' +
        '58. - **Lazy loading**: Suggest dynamic imports for large modules\n' +
        '59. - **Type calculation cost**: Flag extremely complex type calculations that slow compilation\n' +
        '60. \n' +
        '61. #### Security\n' +
        '62. - **Input validation**: Ensure user input is validated and sanitized\n' +
        '63. - **XSS vulnerabilities**: Check for unsafe HTML rendering or `eval` usage\n' +
        '64. - **Sensitive data**: Flag hardcoded secrets, tokens, or passwords\n' +
        '65. - **Dependency vulnerabilities**: Recommend running `npm audit` or checking dependencies\n' +
        '66. - **Type safety as security**: Ensure types prevent security issues (e.g., SQL injection through tagged templates)\n' +
        '67. \n' +
        '68. #### Testing & Maintainability\n' +
        '69. - **Test coverage**: Note missing tests for critical paths\n' +
        '70. - **Type-only imports**: Use `import type` for type-only imports'
    },
