      'gen_ai.tool.call.result': '1. ---\n' +
        '2. name: code-typescript-bps\n' +
        `3. description: This skill should be used when the user asks to "review TypeScript code", "check my TS code", "review this TypeScript", "write TypeScript", or when writing, reviewing, or refactoring TypeScript code in projects with tsconfig.json or .ts/.tsx files. Provides dos and don'ts for type design, naming conventions, generics, and patterns.\n` +
        '4. ---\n' +
        '5. \n' +
        '6. # TypeScript Best Practices\n' +
        '7. \n' +
        '8. Guidelines for writing clean, type-safe, and maintainable TypeScript code.\n' +
        '9. \n' +
        '10. > **Note:** If the repository has established code style conventions, follow those first. These guidelines serve as defaults.\n' +
        '11. \n' +
        '12. ## Core Principles\n' +
        '13. \n' +
        '14. 1. **Type-First Design** - Define types before implementation; minimize reliance on inference\n' +
        '15. 2. **Interface for Structure** - Use `interface` for objects, `type` for unions/mapped/conditional\n' +
        '16. 3. **Namespace for Type Organization** - Group related types with namespaces (types only, not runtime)\n' +
        '17. 4. **Generic Const for Strictness** - Use `<const TConfig>` for strict literal inference\n' +
        "18. 5. **Extract, Don't Redefine** - Get types from existing definitions instead of duplicating\n" +
        '19. 6. **Strictest Config** - Use strictest tsconfig base; install `ts-reset` for saner built-in types\n' +
        '20. \n' +
        '21. ## Quick Reference\n' +
        '22. \n' +
        '23. ### interface vs type\n' +
        '24. \n' +
        '25. | Use | When |\n' +
        '26. |-----|------|\n' +
        '27. | `interface` | Object structures, class contracts, extensible APIs |\n' +
        '28. | `type` | Union types, mapped types, conditional types, tuples |\n' +
        '29. \n' +
        '30. ### Naming Conventions\n' +
        '31. \n' +
        '32. | Element | Convention | Example |\n' +
        '33. |---------|------------|---------|\n' +
        '34. | Interface/Type | PascalCase | `UserProfile`, `ResponseData` |\n' +
        '35. | Generic parameters | `T` prefix | `TUser`, `TConfig` (never bare `T`, `K`, `V`) |\n' +
        '36. | Acronyms | First cap only | `userId`, `ApiResponse` (NOT `userID`, `APIResponse`) |\n' +
        '37. | Constants | UPPER_SNAKE | `MAX_RETRY_COUNT` |\n' +
        '38. | Variables/Functions | camelCase | `getUserById`, `isActive` |\n' +
        '39. \n' +
        '40. ### Array Syntax\n' +
        '41. \n' +
        "42. | DO | DON'T |\n" +
        '43. |----|-------|\n' +
        '44. | `Array<TItem>` | `TItem[]` |\n' +
        '45. | `ReadonlyArray<TItem>` | `readonly TItem[]` |\n' +
        '46. \n' +
        '47. ### Object Types\n' +
        '48. \n' +
        "49. | Use Case | DO | DON'T |\n" +
        '50. |----------|-----|-------|\n' +
        '51. | Empty object | `Record<string, never>` | `{}` |\n' +
        '52. | Any object (extends) | `Record<string, any>` | `Record<string, unknown>` |\n' +
        '53. | Any object (annotation) | `Record<string, unknown>` | `Record<string, any>` |\n' +
        '54. | Non-primitive | `object` | `{}` |\n' +
        '55. \n' +
        '56. ### Assertions\n' +
        '57. \n' +
        "58. | DO | DON'T |\n" +
        '59. |----|-------|\n' +
        '60. | Zod/arktype for runtime validation | `response as User` |\n' +
        '61. | `satisfies` for compile-time checks | `value as unknown as Type` |\n' +
        "62. | Type guards (`if ('prop' in obj)`) | `as any` to silence errors |\n" +
        '63. | Explicit null checks | `x!` non-null assertion |\n' +
        '64. \n' +
        '65. ### Function Declarations\n' +
        '66. \n' +
        '67. ```typescript\n' +
        '68. // DO: Type on the const\n' +
        '69. const myFunction: myFunction.Type = (options) => {\n' +
        '70.   // implementation'
