      'gen_ai.tool.call.result': '1. ---\n' +
        '2. name: ralph-build-errors\n' +
        '3. description: "Troubleshooting guide for common npm run build errors in the Xperience docs site. Use this skill when the build fails and you need to diagnose the cause — covers broken page_link identifiers, missing anchors, duplicate identifiers, code blocks missing lang parameter, circular redirects, URI path conflicts, and frontmatter issues. Read this before spending cycles debugging build failures manually."\n' +
        '4. ---\n' +
        '5. {% raw %}\n' +
        '6. \n' +
        '7. # Build Error Troubleshooting\n' +
        '8. \n' +
        "9. `npm run build` runs the Jekyll build with validation. When it fails, the error message tells you exactly what's wrong. Here's how to fix each type.\n" +
        '10. \n' +
        '11. ## Broken page_link identifier\n' +
        '12. \n' +
        '13. **Error:** `identifier "unknownID" not found`\n' +
        '14. \n' +
        "15. **Cause:** A `{% page_link unknownID %}` references an identifier that doesn't exist.\n" +
        '16. \n' +
        '17. **Fix:**\n' +
        '18. 1. Check for typos in the identifier\n' +
        '19. 3. If the page was removed, update or remove the link\n' +
        '20. \n' +
        '21. ## Missing anchor reference\n' +
        '22. \n' +
        '23. **Error:** `anchor "myAnchor" not defined in current page`\n' +
        '24. \n' +
        '25. **Cause:** An `{% inpage_link "myAnchor" %}` exists but no matching `{% anchor myAnchor %}` is defined on the same page.\n' +
        '26. \n' +
        '27. **Fix:**\n' +
        '28. 1. Add `{% anchor myAnchor %}` at the target location on the page\n' +
        '29. 2. Or fix the typo in either the anchor definition or the inpage_link reference\n' +
        '30. 3. Anchor IDs are case-sensitive\n' +
        '31. \n' +
        '32. ## Duplicate identifier\n' +
        '33. \n' +
        '34. **Error:** `Duplicate identifier "myID" in pagetree`\n' +
        '35. \n' +
        '36. **Cause:** Two pages use the same `identifier` value.\n' +
        '37. \n' +
        '38. **Fix:**\n' +
        '39. 1. Grep for the identifier: `grep -r "identifier: myID" src/_data/ src/_documentation/`\n' +
        '40. 2. Rename one of the duplicates — if you created it, change yours\n' +
        '41. 3. Update all `page_link` references to use the new identifier\n' +
        '42. \n' +
        '43. ## Code block missing lang\n' +
        '44. \n' +
        "45. **Error:** `required parameter 'lang' is missing`\n" +
        '46. \n' +
        '47. **Cause:** A `{% code %}` or `{% code_link %}` tag without the `lang` parameter.\n' +
        '48. \n' +
        '49. **Fix:** Add the language parameter:\n' +
        '50. ```liquid\n' +
        '51. {% code lang=csharp %}\n' +
        '52. ```\n' +
        '53. Common values: `csharp`, `xml`, `json`, `javascript`, `html`, `css`, `sql`, `powershell`, `bash`\n' +
        '54. \n' +
        '55. ## Circular redirect\n' +
        '56. \n' +
        '57. **Error:** `Circular redirect detected`\n' +
        '58. \n' +
        '59. **Cause:** Page A has `redirect_from` pointing to B, and B has `redirect_from` pointing to A (or a longer chain).\n' +
        '60. \n' +
        '61. **Fix:**\n' +
        '62. 1. Decide which page is canonical\n' +
        '63. 2. Remove the `redirect_from` entry from the canonical page that creates the cycle\n' +
        '64. 3. Redirects should always point FROM old paths TO the current page\n' +
        '65. \n' +
        '66. ## URI path conflict\n' +
        '67. \n' +
        '68. **Error:** `Multiple pages resolve to the same URL`\n' +
        '69. \n' +
        '70. **Cause:** Two pages generate the same URL path (same filename in same directory, or conflicting `redirect_from`).'
    },
