      'gen_ai.tool.call.arguments': '{"path":"/home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator/shared/skills/domain/devralph-ruby-gems/SKILL.md","view_range":[1,70]}',
      'gen_ai.tool.call.result': '1. ---\n' +
        '2. name: devralph-ruby-gems\n' +
        '3. description: "Architecture reference for the 8 custom Ruby gems under gems/. Covers kentico-core (DI container, tag base classes, validation), liquid-kfm (42 custom Liquid tags), jekyll-algolia (search indexing), jekyll-learn-portal (learning modules/paths), and supporting gems. Use this skill whenever you touch Ruby code under gems/, encounter Liquid tag rendering errors, need to add or modify a tag, debug DI container registration, fix Learn Portal module/path behavior, or work with Algolia search indexing — even for seemingly simple tag changes, because the tag system has subtle coupling through the DI container and shared base classes that this skill maps."\n' +
        '4. ---\n' +
        '5. {% raw %}\n' +
        '6. \n' +
        '7. # Ruby Gems Architecture\n' +
        '8. \n' +
        '9. The docs site uses 8 custom gems under `gems/`. All gems use `kentico-core` as a foundation.\n' +
        '10. \n' +
        '11. ## Gem Overview\n' +
        '12. \n' +
        '13. | Gem | Purpose | Key integration |\n' +
        '14. |-----|---------|-----------------|\n' +
        '15. | **kentico-core** | Shared base: tag base classes, DI container, validation, logging | Foundation for all other gems |\n' +
        '16. | **liquid-kfm** | 42 custom Liquid tags (links, admonitions, tables, grids, code, assets) | Liquid rendering phase |\n' +
        '17. | **jekyll-algolia** | Algolia search indexing (forked/customized) | `jekyll algolia` CLI command |\n' +
        '18. | **jekyll-learn-portal** | Learning paths + modules system | `:site, :post_read` hook |\n' +
        '19. | **jekyll-kentico-customizations** | Pandoc converter, URL generation, validators, generators | Multiple Jekyll hooks |\n' +
        '20. | **jekyll-redirect-from** | URL redirect support | Redirect pages |\n' +
        '21. | **jekyll-sitemap** | Sitemap generation | `:site, :post_write` |\n' +
        '22. | **jekyll-changelog** | Changelog/release notes | `jekyll changelog` CLI |\n' +
        '23. \n' +
        '24. ## kentico-core (Foundation)\n' +
        '25. \n' +
        '26. **Location:** `gems/kentico-core/`\n' +
        '27. \n' +
        '28. ### DI System\n' +
        '29. \n' +
        '30. Uses `dry-container` + `dry-auto_inject`:\n' +
        '31. \n' +
        '32. ```ruby\n' +
        '33. # Register a service\n' +
        '34. Core::ServiceContainer.register_implementation(InterfaceName, ClassName, singleton: true)\n' +
        '35. \n' +
        '36. # Resolve in a class\n' +
        '37. class MyService\n' +
        '38.   include Core::ServiceResolver[:url_resolver, :validator]\n' +
        '39. end\n' +
        '40. ```\n' +
        '41. \n' +
        '42. ### Tag Base Classes\n' +
        '43. \n' +
        '44. All custom Liquid tags inherit from these:\n' +
        '45. \n' +
        '46. - `KenticoTagBase` → extends `Liquid::Tag` (inline tags like `{% image %}`)\n' +
        '47. - `KenticoBlockTagBase` → extends `Liquid::Block` (block tags like `{% code %}...{% endcode %}`)\n' +
        '48. - `KenticoLinkTagBase` → extends `KenticoTagBase` (link tags like `{% page_link %}`)\n' +
        '49. \n' +
        '50. **Key shared module:** `KenticoSharedBaseLogic` provides:\n' +
        '51. - Parameter parsing via `Liquid::Tag::Parser` (`@params[:key]`, `@params[:argv1]`)\n' +
        '52. - `SUPPORTED_PARAMS` constant for validation\n' +
        '53. - Collection/context helpers\n' +
        '54. \n' +
        '55. ### Creating a New Liquid Tag\n' +
        '56. \n' +
        '57. 1. Create class in `gems/liquid-kfm/lib/` under appropriate subdirectory\n' +
        '58. 2. Inherit from the right base class\n' +
        '59. 3. Define `SUPPORTED_PARAMS` constant\n' +
        '60. 4. Implement `render(context)` (inline) or `render_block(context, content)` (block)\n' +
        "61. 5. Register with `Liquid::Template.register_tag('tag_name', ClassName)`\n" +
        '62. 6. The tag auto-loads because `liquid-kfm.rb` requires all `.rb` files under `lib/`\n' +
        '63. \n' +
        '64. ### Parameter Handling Pattern\n' +
        '65. \n' +
        '66. ```ruby\n' +
        '67. class MyTag < KenticoTagBase\n' +
        '68.   SUPPORTED_PARAMS = %i[param1 param2 optional_flag].freeze\n' +
        '69. \n' +
        '70.   def render(context)'
    },
