      'gen_ai.tool.call.result': '1. ---\n' +
        '2. name: ralph-new-page-creation\n' +
        `3. description: "Rules for creating new Markdown documentation pages including frontmatter schema, identifiers, persona assignment, ordering, and licensing. Use this skill whenever creating a new documentation page, adding a new file to the docs site, setting up YAML frontmatter for a new page, or when the task mentions adding new content that doesn't have an existing page."\n` +
        '4. ---\n' +
        '5. \n' +
        '6. # New Page Creation Skill\n' +
        '7. \n' +
        '8. Rules for creating new Markdown documentation pages for the Xperience by Kentico docs site.\n' +
        '9. \n' +
        '10. ## Documentation Page Creation Rules\n' +
        '11. \n' +
        '12. **Context:** Creating new Markdown documentation pages for the Xperience by Kentico solution.\n' +
        '13. **Format:** Jekyll-based Markdown with YAML Frontmatter.\n' +
        '14. \n' +
        '15. ### File Naming Conventions\n' +
        '16. \n' +
        '17. - **Source:** `~/src/_documentation/<audience>/<filename>.md`\n' +
        '18. - **Slug Logic:** The filename determines the URL slug.\n' +
        '19. - **Syntax:**\n' +
        '20.   - Must reflect the page title.\n' +
        '21.   - Must use hyphens (`-`) as word separators (kebab-case).\n' +
        '22.   - Example: Title "Business user pages" -> Filename `business-user-pages.md`.\n' +
        '23. \n' +
        '24. ### Frontmatter Schema (YAML)\n' +
        '25. \n' +
        '26. The following properties must appear at the top of the `.md` file between triple dashes (`---`).\n' +
        '27. \n' +
        '28. | Property | Required | Type | Valid Values / Constraints |\n' +
        '29. | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n' +
        '30. | `title` | **Yes** | String | The display title of the page. |\n' +
        '31. | `persona` | **Yes** | String/List | Target audience. Comma-separated for multiple. **Enums:** `developer`, `admin`, `business`, `architect`, `all`. |\n' +
        '32. | `identifier` | **Yes** | String | Unique ID. Syntax: `{code_name}_{collection_suffix}`. |\n' +
        '33. | `order` | **Yes** | Integer | Hierarchy sorting index. Start at 100. |\n' +
        '34. | `license` | **Conditional** | String/Int | Tier level. Default is `1` (Standard). Mandatory for `_documentation` and `_guides`. |\n' +
        '35. | `redirect_from` | **Yes** | List | Legacy links. Must include `x/<identifier>`. |\n' +
        '36. | `searchable` | No | Boolean | `true` or `false`. Defaults to true if omitted. |\n' +
        '37. \n' +
        '38. ### Identifier Logic\n' +
        '39. \n' +
        '40. - **Structure:** A unique code name followed by a collection suffix.\n' +
        '41. - **Formatting:** Snake_case.\n' +
        '42. - **Suffixes:** `_guides`, `_xp` depending on target collection.\n' +
        '43. - **Example:** For a "Website Channels" page in the guides collection, use `website_channels_guides`.\n' +
        '44. - **Constraint:** Must be unique across the help service.\n' +
        '45. \n' +
        '46. **Legacy identifiers** (opaque hashes like `H5jWCQ`, `DgqiCQ`) exist from Confluence migration — never create new ones in this format. Always use the modern descriptive format.\n' +
        '47. \n' +
        '48. Identifiers connect the page frontmatter and every `page_link` referencing the page.\n' +
        '49. \n' +
        "50. Before choosing an identifier, verify it's not already taken:\n" +
        '51. ```bash\n' +
        '52. grep -r "identifier: my_proposed_id" src/_documentation/\n' +
        '53. ```\n' +
        '54. \n' +
        '55. ### Persona Assignment Strategy\n' +
        '56. \n' +
        '57. - **General/All:** Use `all`.\n' +
        '58. - **Developer Guides:** `developer` (add `admin`, `architect` if relevant).\n' +
        '59. - **Business Guides:** `business` (add `architect` if relevant).\n' +
        '60. - **Architecture:** `architect` (add `admin`, `developer` if relevant).\n' +
        '61. - **Config/User Roles:** `admin`, `developer`.\n' +
        '62. \n' +
        '63. ### Order (Sorting) Logic\n' +
        '64. \n' +
        '65. - **New Subtrees:** Start at `100`, increment by 100 (`100`, `200`, `300`).\n' +
        '66. - **Insertions:** Use the mathematical midpoint.\n' +
        '67.   - *Example:* Inserting between 500 and 600 -> `550`.\n' +
        '68.   - *Collision:* If `550` exists, split to `533` and `566`, or `525` and `575`.\n' +
        '69. \n' +
        '70. ### Licensing Features'
    },
