      'gen_ai.tool.call.result': '1. ---\n' +
        '2. name: devralph-jekyll-site\n' +
        `3. description: "Jekyll site structure reference covering collections (7 active + legacy archives), layouts (8 templates), includes (component hierarchy), data files (pagetree YAML), frontmatter conventions, content organization, and the multi-file config overlay system. Use this skill whenever you modify layouts or includes under src/_layouts/ or src/_includes/, change navigation or pagetree data, add or reorganize collections, edit frontmatter conventions, or need to understand identifier-based cross-referencing — the site's component hierarchy and collection metadata drive both navigation and rendering, so changes to one layer often require coordinated updates in another."\n` +
        '4. ---\n' +
        '5. {% raw %}\n' +
        '6. \n' +
        '7. # Jekyll Site Structure\n' +
        '8. \n' +
        '9. Content lives under `src/` following Jekyll conventions with a custom `collections_dir`.\n' +
        '10. \n' +
        '11. ## Configuration\n' +
        '12. \n' +
        '13. ### Multi-File Config Overlay\n' +
        '14. \n' +
        '15. The site uses **multiple YAML config files** merged at build time:\n' +
        '16. \n' +
        '17. - `src/_configs/_config_primary.yml` (445 lines) — main config\n' +
        '18. - `src/_configs/_config_development.yml` — local dev overrides\n' +
        '19. - `src/_configs/infrastructure/` — mode-specific configs (serve, test, algolia, AIRA, validation)\n' +
        '20. - `src/_jekyllConfigFinal.yml` — auto-generated merged output\n' +
        '21. \n' +
        '22. Key settings:\n' +
        '23. - **Markdown converter:** `KenticoPandoc` (custom, from `jekyll-kentico-customizations` gem)\n' +
        '24. - **Default layout:** `page`\n' +
        '25. - **Permalink:** `/:collection/:path`\n' +
        '26. - **Collections dir:** `_documentation`\n' +
        '27. - **Learn portal:** enabled per-collection via `learn_portal: true`\n' +
        '28. \n' +
        '29. ## Collections\n' +
        '30. \n' +
        '31. All collections live under `src/_documentation/`.\n' +
        '32. \n' +
        '33. ### Active Collections\n' +
        '34. \n' +
        '35. | Collection | Pages | Purpose |\n' +
        '36. |------------|-------|---------|\n' +
