      'gen_ai.tool.call.result': '1. ---\n' +
        '2. name: ralph-documentation-syntax\n' +
        '3. description: "Complete reference for all Liquid tags, formatting, and components available in the Xperience by Kentico Jekyll documentation site. Use this skill whenever writing or editing documentation pages, inserting Liquid tags (admonitions, code blocks, images, page links, tables, columns, cards), adding assets, creating anchors, or using any documentation-specific component. This is the authoritative syntax reference — consult it instead of guessing tag syntax."\n' +
        '4. ---\n' +
        '5. {% raw %}\n' +
        '6. # Documentation Syntax Skill\n' +
        '7. \n' +
        '8. Reference for all Liquid tags, formatting, and components available in the Xperience by Kentico Jekyll documentation site.\n' +
        '9. \n' +
        '10. ## Front Matter\n' +
        '11. \n' +
        '12. Every page starts with YAML between `---` lines. For the full frontmatter schema (required fields, identifier logic, persona assignment, ordering, licensing), see the **ralph-new-page-creation** skill.\n' +
        '13. \n' +
        '14. ## Related Skills\n' +
        '15. \n' +
        '16. Read these skills when the task requires the corresponding operation:\n' +
        '17. \n' +
        '18. - **ralph-callout-selection** — choosing the correct admonition type (tip, info, note, warning) for each situation\n' +
        '19. - **ralph-cross-version-linking** — cross-collection `page_link` and `card` tag syntax (read when linking between documentation, guides, and api collections)\n' +
        '20. - **ralph-page-removal** — checklist for removing or replacing pages without leaving broken links (read when removing or deprecating pages)\n' +
        '21. - **ralph-build-errors** — troubleshooting guide for `npm run build` failures (read when the build fails — covers broken page_link identifiers, missing anchors, duplicate identifiers, code blocks missing lang)\n' +
        '22. \n' +
        '23. ## Formatting\n' +
        '24. \n' +
        '25. - Indentation: 4 spaces, no tabs or 2-space indents.\n' +
        '26. \n' +
        '27. ## Liquid Tags\n' +
        '28. \n' +
        '29. ### Admonitions\n' +
        '30. \n' +
        '31. ### Code Blocks\n' +
        '32. \n' +
        '33. **Inline code block** — content directly in the tag:\n' +
        '34. ```liquid\n' +
        '35. {% code lang=csharp title="Example.cs" highlight="4-7,10" linenumbers=true %}\n' +
        '36. // code\n' +
        '37. {% endcode %}\n' +
        '38. ```\n' +
        '39. \n' +
        '40. - Params: `lang`, `title`, `highlight`, `linenumbers`, `header` (true by default).\n' +
        '41. - Supported `lang`: bash, bicep, c, css, csharp, cshtml, git, graphql, js, java, json, jsx, html, markdown, nginx, powershell, tsx, regex, sql, typescript, yaml.\n' +
        '42. - Use `lang=text` for no highlighting.\n' +
        '43. - If code contains Liquid-like syntax (`{%` or `{{`), wrap the code content with raw/endraw tags to prevent Liquid interpretation.\n' +
        '44. \n' +
        '45. **Linked code block** — pulls from the CodeSamples project:\n' +
        '46. ```liquid\n' +
        '47. {% code_link source="CodeSamples/FeatureArea/ClassName.cs" lang=csharp title="Title" id="section-id" exclude="inner" %}\n' +
        '48. ```\n' +
        '49. - `source` (required) — path relative to `src/_code/src/`\n' +
        '50. - `lang` (required) — language\n' +
        '51. - `id` (optional) — extract only the region between `//Include:section-id` and `//EndInclude:section-id` markers in the source file\n' +
        '52. - `exclude` (optional) — exclude a nested region within the included section\n' +
        '53. - `title`, `highlight`, `linenumbers` — same as `{% code %}`\n' +
        '54. \n' +
        '55. ### Assets\n' +
        '56. \n' +
        '57. - Images: `{% image filename.png title="..." width=500 border=true %}`\n' +
        '58.   - Path: `src/_docsassets/<collection>/<pagefilename>/`.\n' +
        '59.   - Use `border=true` for UI/screenshot images.\n' +
        '60. - Files: `{% file filename.pdf linkText="..." disposition=download %}`\n' +
        '61.   - Path: `src/_docsassets/<collection>/<pagefilename>/`.\n' +
        '62.   - `disposition`: `download` (default) or `open`.\n' +
        '63. - Video: `{% video "https://www.youtube.com/embed/ID" height=300 width=500 %}` or `{% video "local.mp4" width=500 %}`\n' +
        '64.   - YouTube must use `/embed/` URLs.\n' +
        '65. - Arcade demo: `{% arcade https://demo.arcade.software/ID title="Demo Title" mobile=inline desktop=inline %}`\n' +
        '66.   - `mobile`, `desktop`: `inline` or `tab`.\n' +
        '67. \n' +
        '68. ### Anchors and Links\n' +
        '69. \n' +
        '70. - Anchors: `{% anchor my-id %}`'
    },
