      'gen_ai.tool.call.arguments': '{"path":"/home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator/shared/skills/domain/ralph-cross-version-linking/SKILL.md","view_range":[1,70]}',
      'gen_ai.tool.call.result': '1. ---\n' +
        '2. name: ralph-cross-version-linking\n' +
        '3. description: "How to link across documentation collections (documentation, guides, api) using the collection parameter on page_link and card tags. Use this skill when a page in one collection needs to reference a page in a different collection — cross-collection links require the collection parameter or the build silently generates a broken link."\n' +
        '4. ---\n' +
        '5. {% raw %}\n' +
        '6. \n' +
        '7. # Cross-Collection Linking\n' +
        '8. \n' +
        "9. The docs site has multiple Jekyll collections, each with its own page tree. Links between collections require the `collection` parameter — without it, page_link only searches the current collection's tree.\n" +
        '10. \n' +
        '11. ## Collections in use\n' +
        '12. \n' +
        '13. | Collection | Path prefix | Pagetree file | Content scope |\n' +
        '14. |------------|-------------|---------------|---------------|\n' +
        '15. | `documentation` | `/documentation/` | `documentation.yml` | Main Xperience by Kentico docs |\n' +
        '16. | `guides` | `/guides/` | `guides.yml` | Training guides and tutorials |\n' +
        '17. | `api` | `/api/` | `api.yml` | API reference and code examples |\n' +
        '18. \n' +
        '19. Legacy collections (K8, K9, K10, K11, K12SP, 13, 13api, 13tutorial) also exist but new docs pages target the main three.\n' +
        '20. \n' +
        '21. ## Linking across collections\n' +
        '22. \n' +
        '23. **From documentation → guides:**\n' +
        '24. ```liquid\n' +
        '25. {% page_link setup_guide_identifier collection="guides" linkText="Getting started guide" %}\n' +
        '26. ```\n' +
        '27. \n' +
        '28. **From guides → api:**\n' +
        '29. ```liquid\n' +
        '30. {% page_link api_example_identifier collection="api" linkText="See API example" %}\n' +
        '31. ```\n' +
        '32. \n' +
        '33. **Card linking across collections:**\n' +
        '34. ```liquid\n' +
        '35. {% card link=guide_identifier collection="guides" title="Related Guide" %}\n' +
        '36. Check out the getting started guide.\n' +
        '37. {% endcard %}\n' +
        '38. ```\n' +
        '39. \n' +
        '40. ## When collection is required\n' +
        '41. \n' +
        "42. - **Same collection:** No `collection` parameter needed — page_link resolves within the current collection's tree automatically.\n" +
        "43. - **Different collection:** `collection` parameter is **required**. Without it, the identifier won't be found in the current collection's tree and the build produces an error.\n" +
        '44. \n' +
        '45. ## How to determine the collection\n' +
        '46. \n' +
        "47. Look at where the target page's `.md` file lives:\n" +
        '48. - `src/_documentation/_documentation/` → collection `documentation`\n' +
        '49. - `src/_documentation/_guides/` → collection `guides`\n' +
        '50. - `src/_documentation/_api/` → collection `api`\n' +
        '51. \n' +
        '52. Or check which pagetree YAML file contains the target identifier.\n' +
        '53. \n' +
        '54. ## Common mistake\n' +
        '55. \n' +
        "56. Forgetting the `collection` parameter when linking from a guide page to the main documentation. The link renders but may point to the wrong page or produce a build error if the identifier isn't found.\n" +
        '57. {% endraw %}'
    },
