      'gen_ai.tool.call.arguments': '{"path":"/home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator/shared/skills/domain/ralph-page-removal/SKILL.md","view_range":[1,70]}',
      'gen_ai.tool.call.result': '1. ---\n' +
        '2. name: ralph-page-removal\n' +
        '3. description: "Checklist for removing or deprecating documentation pages without leaving broken links. Use this skill whenever a task requires deleting a page, merging pages, or replacing one page with another. Covers removing from documentation.yml, setting up redirects, cleaning up orphaned page_link references, updating related_pages arrays, and removing orphaned images."\n' +
        '4. ---\n' +
        '5. {% raw %}\n' +
        '6. \n' +
        '7. # Page Removal Checklist\n' +
        '8. \n' +
        '9. Removing a page incorrectly breaks links across the site. Follow this checklist in order.\n' +
        '10. \n' +
        '11. ## 1. Identify all references to the page\n' +
        '12. \n' +
        "13. Find every place the page's identifier is used:\n" +
        '14. ```bash\n' +
        '15. grep -r "IDENTIFIER" src/_documentation/ src/_data/\n' +
        '16. ```\n' +
        '17. \n' +
        '18. ## 2. Update or remove page_link references\n' +
        '19. \n' +
        '20. For each `{% page_link IDENTIFIER %}` found:\n' +
        "21. - If there's a replacement page, update to the new identifier\n" +
        '22. - If the content is being merged into another page, link to that page with an appropriate anchor\n' +
        '23. - If the content is being removed entirely, remove the link and rewrite the surrounding text\n' +
        '24. \n' +
        '25. ## 3. Set up redirects\n' +
        '26. \n' +
        '27. If the page had traffic or external links, add `redirect_from` to the replacement page:\n' +
        '28. ```yaml\n' +
        '29. redirect_from:\n' +
        '30.   - /documentation/path/to/old-page\n' +
        '31.   - x/OLD_IDENTIFIER\n' +
        '32. ```\n' +
        '33. \n' +
        '34. If no replacement exists, consider whether a redirect to the parent section is appropriate.\n' +
        '35. \n' +
        '36. ## 4. Update related_pages arrays\n' +
        '37. \n' +
        '38. Search for the identifier in `related_pages` frontmatter fields:\n' +
        '39. ```bash\n' +
        '40. grep -r "IDENTIFIER" src/_documentation/ --include="*.md" -l\n' +
        '41. ```\n' +
        '42. \n' +
        '43. Remove the identifier from any `related_pages` arrays.\n' +
        '44. \n' +
        '45. ## 5. Clean up orphaned assets\n' +
        '46. \n' +
        '47. If the page referenced images that no other page uses:\n' +
        '48. ```bash\n' +
        '49. # Find images referenced only by the deleted page\n' +
        '50. grep -r "image_filename.png" src/_documentation/ --include="*.md"\n' +
        '51. ```\n' +
        '52. \n' +
        '53. If no other page references the image, delete it from `src/_assets/img/`.\n' +
        '54. \n' +
        '55. ## 6. Validate\n' +
        '56. \n' +
        '57. Run `npm run build` to confirm no broken references remain.\n' +
        '58. {% endraw %}'
    },
