      'gen_ai.tool.call.result': '1. ---\n' +
        '2. name: ralph-research-guide\n' +
        '3. description: "Complete research guide for the ralph-researcher sub-agent. Covers research order, techniques for exploring existing docs, Xperience C# source code, and external references, plus the report template and validation checklist. Read this skill and its reference files before starting any research task."\n' +
        '4. ---\n' +
        '5. \n' +
        '6. # Research Guide\n' +
        '7. \n' +
        '8. Complete research guide for the ralph-researcher sub-agent. Read the reference files listed below before starting your research — they contain the techniques, patterns, and checklists you need.\n' +
        '9. \n' +
        '10. ## Reference Files\n' +
        '11. \n' +
        '12. Read these from your folder:\n' +
        '13. \n' +
        '14. | File | What it covers |\n' +
        '15. |---|---|\n' +
        '16. | `references/existing-docs.md` | How to navigate the docs site structure, find sibling pages, check frontmatter |\n' +
        '17. | `references/source-code.md` | How to search the Xperience C# codebase for classes, APIs, enums, defaults |\n' +
        '18. | `references/external-docs.md` | When and how to use `microsoft_docs_search` and `web_fetch` |\n' +
        '19. | `references/report-template.md` | Report template and validation checklist — structure your output using this |\n' +
        '20. \n' +
        '21. ## Research Order\n' +
        '22. \n' +
        '23. 1. **Check Ralphchives** — search for prior work on this component or feature area using the **ralph-ralphchives** skill. Past observations, gotchas, and failed approaches save you from repeating mistakes.\n' +
        '24. 2. **Explore existing documentation** — find related pages, understand current coverage, identify gaps. See `references/existing-docs.md`.\n' +
        '25. 3. **Explore the Xperience source code** — verify technical claims, find accurate API signatures, class hierarchies, configuration options, enum values, default settings. See `references/source-code.md`.\n' +
        '26. 4. **Cross-reference external documentation** — when source code findings need clarification or the task involves .NET/ASP.NET concepts. See `references/external-docs.md`.\n' +
        '27. 5. **Assemble your report** — follow the template in `references/report-template.md`. Run the validation checklist before returning.\n' +
        '28. \n' +
        '29. ## Rules\n' +
        '30. \n' +
        '31. - **Read-only** — do NOT create, edit, or delete any files\n' +
        '32. - **Source code is ground truth.** When existing docs contradict the source, trust the source and flag the discrepancy.\n' +
        '33. - **Be specific** — include file paths, class names, method signatures, line numbers\n' +
        "34. - **Extract, don't summarize** — provide actual code snippets and content the meta-agent can use directly\n" +
        '35. - **Search gitignored paths** — the Xperience source at `resources/repositories/xperience` is gitignored; always use `includeIgnoredFiles: true` when searching it\n' +
        "36. - **Note what you couldn't find.** If you searched for something and it doesn't exist, say so explicitly — that's useful information."
    },
