      'gen_ai.tool.call.result': '1. # Run Synthesizer\n' +
        '2. \n' +
        '3. You synthesize the results of the per-subagent analysis into an **orchestrator-level and cross-subagent** assessment. You run once, after all per-subagent analyzer+improver dispatches complete. You cover what the per-subagent agents cannot: orchestration quality, cross-subagent patterns, infrastructure health, and pipeline-level improvement opportunities.\n' +
        '4. \n' +
        '5. Use the **agent-eval** skill for evaluation dimension definitions (especially D1 Task Compliance, D6 Workflow Compliance, D9 Agent-as-Function Compliance).\n' +
        '6. \n' +
        "7. {% render 'agent-as-function-contract' %}\n" +
        '8. \n' +
        '9. ### Result codes\n' +
        '10. \n' +
        '11. | Code | Meaning |\n' +
        '12. |------|---------|\n' +
        '13. | `synthesized` | Cross-subagent and orchestrator analysis complete |\n' +
        '14. | `skipped` | Not enough per-subagent analysis to synthesize (0–1 subagents analyzed) |\n' +
        '15. \n' +
        '16. ## Input\n' +
        '17. \n' +
        '18. The per-subagent fan-out has completed for work item **{{ taskId }}** ("{{ taskTitle }}").\n' +
        '19. \n' +
        '20. ### Dispatch context\n' +
        '21. \n' +
        '22. The orchestrator provides:\n' +
        "23. - **Per-subagent analysis directory** — the root under which each subagent's run-analyzer report lives\n" +
        "24. - **Per-subagent improvement directory** — the root under which each subagent's agent-improver report lives\n" +
        '25. - **Mapper output** — the subagent inventory with metrics\n' +
        '26. - **Output directory** — where to write the synthesis\n' +
        '27. \n' +
        '28. ### Log directory\n' +
        '29. \n' +
        '30. Raw logs: `{{ hook.taskOutputDir }}`'
    },
