      'gen_ai.tool.call.result': '1. ---\n' +
        '2. name: ralph-codesamples-verification\n' +
        '3. description: "Functionally verify the ASP.NET Core codesamples application after implementing changes. Start the server, use playwright-cli to exercise the routes and interactions you implemented — browse pages, submit forms, trigger controller actions — and confirm the application behaves as expected. Use this skill whenever you modified controllers, services, views, or models in src/_code/src/."\n' +
        '4. ---\n' +
        '5. \n' +
        '6. # Code Samples Functional Verification\n' +
        '7. \n' +
        '8. After implementing changes to the codesamples ASP.NET Core project, verify that the application **works as expected** — routes respond, pages render, forms submit, services return correct data. Use `playwright-cli` to interact with the running application the way a user would.\n' +
        '9. \n' +
        '10. ## Prerequisites\n' +
        '11. \n' +
        '12. - `playwright-cli` must be available (run `playwright-cli open` to verify; if unavailable, use `npx playwright-cli`).\n' +
        '13. - Build must pass before verification:\n' +
        '14. \n' +
        '15. ```bash\n' +
        '16. npm run codesamples:build\n' +
        '17. ```\n' +
        '18. \n' +
        '19. - Start the application if not already running. Keep it running only for the duration of verification:\n' +
        '20. \n' +
        '21. ```bash\n' +
        '22. if ! curl -sf http://localhost:666 >/dev/null; then\n' +
        '23. \tnpm run codesamples:serve > /tmp/codesamples-serve.log 2>&1 &\n' +
        '24. \tSERVER_PID=$!\n' +
        `25. \ttrap 'if [[ -n "$SERVER_PID" ]]; then kill "$SERVER_PID" 2>/dev/null || true; fi' EXIT\n` +
        '26. \tfor i in $(seq 1 30); do\n' +
        '27. \t\tcurl -sf http://localhost:666 >/dev/null && break\n' +
        '28. \t\tsleep 2\n' +
        '29. \tdone\n' +
        '30. fi\n' +
        '31. ```\n' +
        '32. \n' +
        '33. Wait until the application responds on `localhost:666` before proceeding. If startup fails, inspect `/tmp/codesamples-serve.log`.\n' +
        '34. \n' +
        '35. ## What to Verify\n' +
        '36. \n' +
        '37. Focus on the **features you implemented or modified**. Walk through them as a user would:\n' +
        '38. \n' +
        '39. - If you added a **controller action** — navigate to its route and confirm it returns the expected page or redirect\n' +
        '40. - If you added a **form** — fill it out and submit it, verify the response (success page, validation errors for bad input, redirect)\n' +
        '41. - If you added a **service** — exercise it through the controller that consumes it, verify the data appears correctly on the page\n' +
        '42. - If you modified **views** — navigate to the page and verify the UI reflects your changes (elements present, data displayed, layout correct)\n' +
        '43. - If you added **DI registrations** — verify the application starts without dependency injection errors\n' +
        '44. \n' +
        '45. ## Verification Workflow\n' +
        '46. \n' +
        '47. ### 1. Open the application\n' +
        '48. \n' +
        '49. ```bash\n' +
        '50. playwright-cli open http://localhost:666\n' +
        '51. playwright-cli resize 1366 900\n' +
        '52. ```\n' +
        '53. \n' +
        '54. ### 2. Exercise the routes you implemented\n' +
        '55. \n' +
        '56. Navigate to each route your changes affect:\n' +
        '57. \n' +
        '58. ```bash\n' +
        '59. playwright-cli goto http://localhost:666/<route>\n' +
        '60. playwright-cli snapshot\n' +
        '61. ```\n' +
        '62. \n' +
        '63. For each page, use `snapshot` to inspect the DOM. Verify:\n' +
        '64. - The page loads (no 500 error page, no blank response)\n' +
        '65. - Expected content is present (headings, data, form fields)\n' +
        '66. - Dynamic data renders correctly (lists populated, values calculated)\n' +
        '67. \n' +
        '68. Capture screenshots when the task involves visible UI changes, admin UI interactions, or evidence worth attaching to the handoff:\n' +
        '69. \n' +
        '70. ```bash'
    },
