        '2. name: ralph-codegraph\n' +
        '3. description: "Query Xperience source code structure using the CodeGraphContext MCP tools — call chains, class hierarchies, dead code, complexity metrics, and raw Cypher queries against an indexed graph of the codebase. Use this skill when you need structural answers about the source code that grep and file search cannot efficiently answer."\n' +
        '4. ---\n' +
        '5. \n' +
        '6. # Code Graph Queries\n' +
        '7. \n' +
        '8. Use the CodeGraphContext (CGC) MCP tools to answer **structural** questions about the Xperience source code. The graph is pre-indexed on container startup — you do not need to index manually.\n' +
        '9. \n' +
        '10. ## When to Use This vs. File Search\n' +
        '11. \n' +
        '12. | Use CGC | Use grep / file search |\n' +
        '13. |---|---|\n' +
        '14. | "What calls `ProcessPayment`?" | "Find TODO comments" |\n' +
        '15. | "Show the class hierarchy for `PageBuilderComponent`" | "Find files matching `*.cs`" |\n' +
        '16. | "Is `OldHelper` used anywhere?" (dead code) | "Search for string `API_KEY`" |\n' +
        '17. | "What does `Initialize` call under the hood?" | Content/pattern matching |\n' +
        '18. | "Trace from `Register` down to `SaveToDatabase`" | "Find files containing `using CMS.Core`" |\n' +
        '19. \n' +
        '20. **Rule:** structural questions → CGC tools. Content/pattern questions → text search.\n' +
        '21. \n' +
        '22. ## Verify the Index\n' +
        '23. \n' +
        '24. Before your first query, confirm the repo is indexed:\n' +
        '25. \n' +
        '26. ```\n' +
        '27. Tool: list_indexed_repositories\n' +
        '28. ```\n' +
        '29. \n' +
        '30. If the Xperience repo is missing, index it:\n' +
        '31. \n' +
        '32. ```\n' +
        '33. Tool: add_code_to_graph\n' +
        '34. Args: { "directory_path": "resources/repositories/xperience" }\n' +
        '35. ```\n' +
        '36. \n' +
        '37. Then poll until done:\n' +
        '38. \n' +
        '39. ```\n' +
        '40. Tool: check_job_status\n' +
        '41. Args: { "job_id": "<id>" }\n' +
        '42. ```\n' +
        '43. \n' +
        '44. ### Useful patterns\n' +
        '45. \n' +
        '46. **All classes implementing an interface:**\n' +
        '47. ```cypher\n' +
        "48. MATCH (c:Class)-[:INHERITS]->(i:Class {name: 'IPageBuilderComponent'})\n" +
        '49. RETURN c.name, c.path\n' +
        '50. ```\n' +
        '51. \n' +
        '52. **Hub functions (refactoring targets):**\n' +
        '53. ```cypher\n' +
        '54. MATCH (f:Function)\n' +
        '55. OPTIONAL MATCH (f)-[:CALLS]->(callee:Function)\n' +
        '56. OPTIONAL MATCH (caller:Function)-[:CALLS]->(f)\n' +
        '57. WITH f, count(DISTINCT callee) AS out, count(DISTINCT caller) AS inc\n' +
        '58. ORDER BY (out + inc) DESC LIMIT 10\n' +
        '59. RETURN f.name, f.path, inc, out\n' +
        '60. ```\n' +
        '61. \n' +
        '62. **Cross-namespace calls:**\n' +
        '63. ```cypher\n' +
        '64. MATCH (caller:Function)-[:CALLS]->(callee:Function)\n' +
        "65. WHERE caller.path CONTAINS 'CMS/ContentEngine' AND callee.path CONTAINS 'CMS/DataEngine'\n" +
        '66. RETURN caller.name, callee.name\n' +
        '67. ```\n' +
        '68. \n' +
        '69. ## Graph Model Reference\n' +
        '70. '
