      'gen_ai.tool.call.result': '1. ---\n' +
        '2. name: ralph-screenshots\n' +
        '3. description: "Instructions for capturing clean admin UI screenshots using playwright-cli for the Xperience by Kentico documentation. Use this skill whenever a task requires taking screenshots of the admin interface, documenting UI elements visually, capturing visual references for documentation pages, or when the JIRA issue mentions screenshots, images, or visual documentation."\n' +
        '4. ---\n' +
        '5. \n' +
        '6. # Screenshots Skill\n' +
        '7. \n' +
        '8. Instructions for capturing clean admin UI screenshots using `playwright-cli` for the Xperience by Kentico documentation.\n' +
        '9. \n' +
        '10. ## Prerequisites\n' +
        '11. \n' +
        '12. - `playwright-cli` must be available (run `playwright-cli open` to verify; if unavailable, use `npx playwright-cli`).\n' +
        '13. - The Xperience admin application must be running (typically on `http://localhost:666/admin`). If not running, use `npm run codesamples:serve`. Login is administrator:admin.\n' +
        '14. \n' +
        '15. ## Standard Capture Workflow\n' +
        '16. \n' +
        '17. ### 1. Open browser and navigate\n' +
        '18. \n' +
        '19. ```bash\n' +
        '20. playwright-cli open http://localhost:666/admin\n' +
        '21. # Resize to standard documentation width\n' +
        '22. playwright-cli resize 1366 900\n' +
        '23. ```\n' +
        '24. \n' +
        '25. ### 2. Log in (if needed)\n' +
        '26. \n' +
        '27. ```bash\n' +
        '28. playwright-cli snapshot\n' +
        '29. # Use refs from snapshot to fill login form\n' +
        '30. playwright-cli fill <email-ref> "administrator"\n' +
        '31. playwright-cli fill <password-ref> "admin"\n' +
        '32. playwright-cli click <login-button-ref>\n' +
        '33. ```\n' +
        '34. \n' +
        '35. ### 3. Navigate to the target page\n' +
        '36. \n' +
        '37. ```bash\n' +
        '38. playwright-cli goto http://localhost:666/admin/<path>\n' +
        '39. playwright-cli snapshot\n' +
        '40. ```\n' +
        '41. \n' +
        '42. ### 4. Capture screenshot with run-code\n' +
        '43. \n' +
        '44. Use `playwright-cli run-code` for every screenshot. The script must:\n' +
        '45. \n' +
        '46. 1. **Hide the AIRA panel** (`display: none`)\n' +
        '47. 2. **Add red highlight outlines** if needed (`outline: 3px solid red`)\n' +
        '48. 3. **Calculate a clip region** that excludes the left sidebar and crops dead space at the bottom\n' +
        '49. 4. **Take the screenshot** with the calculated clip\n' +
        '50. \n' +
        '51. ```bash\n' +
        '52. playwright-cli run-code "async page => {\n' +
        '53.   // 1. Hide AIRA\n' +
        '54.   await page.evaluate(() => {\n' +
        `55.     const aira = document.querySelector('[class*=\\"aira___\\"]');\n` +
        "56.     if (aira) aira.style.display = 'none';\n" +
        '57.   });\n' +
        '58. \n' +
        '59.   // 2. Add highlights (optional)\n' +
        '60.   await page.evaluate(() => {\n' +
        "61.     document.querySelectorAll('button').forEach(btn => {\n" +
        "62.       if (btn.textContent.trim() === 'Save') {\n" +
        "63.         btn.style.outline = '3px solid red';\n" +
        "64.         btn.style.outlineOffset = '3px';\n" +
        "65.         btn.style.borderRadius = '4px';\n" +
        '66.       }\n' +
        '67.     });\n' +
        '68.   });\n' +
        '69. \n' +
        '70.   // 3. Calculate clip (exclude sidebar, crop bottom dead space)'
    },
