      'gen_ai.tool.call.result': '1. ---\n' +
        '2. name: ralph-source-references\n' +
        '3. description: "URL format for citing Xperience by Kentico source code in JIRA comments and handoff files using the source browser. Use this skill whenever referencing source code, linking to specific classes or methods from the Xperience codebase, or including source browser URLs in comments or documentation."\n' +
        '4. ---\n' +
        '5. \n' +
        '6. # Source Code References Skill\n' +
        '7. \n' +
        '8. Instructions for citing Xperience by Kentico source code in JIRA comments and handoff files.\n' +
        '9. \n' +
        '10. ## Source Code References in Comments\n' +
        '11. \n' +
        '12. When citing Xperience source code in JIRA comments or handoff files, include navigable links to the source browser so reviewers can click through and verify.\n' +
        '13. \n' +
        '14. ### URL format\n' +
        '15. \n' +
        '16. ```\n' +
        '17. https://app-xbyk-source-prod.azurewebsites.net/#<Namespace/Path/ClassName.cs>,<LineNumber>\n' +
        '18. ```\n' +
        '19. \n' +
        "20. The URL path uses the **fully-qualified .NET namespace** from the source file's `namespace` declaration, not the filesystem path. The line number is optional but recommended. **Critical:** The namespace almost always starts with `CMS.`\n" +
        '21. \n' +
        '22. ### Example\n' +
        '23. \n' +
        '24. - File on disk: `CMSSolution/DbDataManager/Installation/SqlInstallationHelper.cs`\n' +
        '25. - Namespace in file: `namespace CMS.DbDataManager.Installation`\n' +
        '26. - Correct URL: `https://app-xbyk-source-prod.azurewebsites.net/#CMS.DbDataManager/Installation/SqlInstallationHelper.cs,222`\n' +
        '27. - Wrong URL: `https://app-xbyk-source-prod.azurewebsites.net/#DbDataManager/Installation/SqlInstallationHelper.cs,222` (missing `CMS.` prefix)\n' +
        '28. \n' +
        '29. Post as a JIRA link: `[ClassName.cs:L222|<url>]`'
    },
