        '- [ ] Are there scope creep additions not covered by the issue?\n' +
        '\n' +
        '#### B. Architecture Compliance\n' +
        '\n' +
        "The extension has **rigid patterns**. Verify they're followed:\n" +
        '\n' +
        '- [ ] **Definition-driven pattern** — new tags/attributes use declarative definitions, not ad-hoc logic in providers\n' +
        '- [ ] **TagNames enum** — new tags added to `src/constants.ts` `TagNames` enum (not bare strings)\n' +
        '- [ ] **Definition registration** — new definitions registered in `definitionInit.ts` (tags) or `headerDefinition.ts` (header attrs)\n' +
        '- [ ] **Folder structure** — tag definitions in `src/definitions/tags/<category>/<tag>/`, header in `src/definitions/header/<attr>/`\n' +
        '- [ ] **File naming** — `<tag>.types.ts` for definition, `<tag>Snippet.ts` for snippet provider, `validate*.rule.ts` for rules\n' +
        '- [ ] **Grammar sync** — if a new tag or attribute was added, the TextMate grammar (`grammars/injections/kfmarkdown.json`) was updated to match\n' +
        '- [ ] **Event system** — new VS Code event listeners go through the internal event emitter, not registered ad-hoc\n' +
        '- [ ] **Disposal** — new disposables added to `context.subscriptions` or `pluginDispose.ts`; new timers have `clearAll*` cleanup\n' +
        '\n' +
        '#### C. TypeScript & Code Quality\n' +
        '\n' +
        '- [ ] **Strict TypeScript** — no `any` type leakage without justification; the project uses `strict: true`\n' +
        '- [ ] **Type interfaces** — `TagDefinition`, `TagAttribute`, `HeaderAttribute` interfaces implemented correctly with all required fields\n' +
        '- [ ] **Enum usage** — `TagNames`, `AttributeDataType`, `Scope`, `DocumentContext` enums used instead of bare strings\n' +
        '- [ ] **Import paths** — no barrel re-exports; direct imports from source modules\n' +
        '- [ ] **No `vscode` namespace misuse** — extension APIs used correctly (disposable management, event subscriptions, configuration reads)\n' +
        '- [ ] **Async correctness** — promises properly awaited; no fire-and-forget in activation path\n' +
        '- [ ] **ESLint compliance** — camelCase/PascalCase naming, semicolons, curly braces, strict equality\n' +
        '- [ ] **JSDoc** — public methods and interfaces have JSDoc documentation\n' +
        '\n' +
