      'gen_ai.tool.call.result': '1. ---\n' +
        '2. name: ralph-codesamples\n' +
        '3. description: "Complete reference for the Xperience by Kentico codesamples .NET project — solution structure, feature-folder organization, code_link integration, build workflow, and coding conventions. Use this skill whenever working with files in src/_code/src/, creating or modifying C# code samples, adding code_link tags to documentation pages, or when the JIRA issue mentions code examples, API usage, or .NET snippets."\n' +
        '4. ---\n' +
        '5. \n' +
        '6. # Code Samples Skill\n' +
        '7. \n' +
        '8. Complete reference for the codesamples .NET project — structure, integration, and workflow.\n' +
        '9. \n' +
        '10. ## Solution Structure\n' +
        '11. \n' +
        "12. The codesamples project at `src/_code/src/` is a working Xperience by Kentico implementation used to source compilable, verified code snippets for documentation. The documentation build pipeline extracts regions marked with `//Include:` / `//EndInclude:` comments and embeds them into pages via {% raw %}`{% code_link %}`{% endraw %} Liquid tags. Because the code lives in a real, buildable project, API changes are caught at compile time — **if the code doesn't build, the docs don't render**.\n" +
        '13. \n' +
        '14. The solution (`Solution.slnx`) contains two projects:\n' +
        '15. \n' +
        '16. | Project | Type | Role |\n' +
        '17. |---------|------|------|\n' +
        '18. | **CodeSamples** | Razor Class Library (`Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Razor`) | All sample code — controllers, services, models, views, generated content types, and standalone snippets. |\n' +
        '19. | **Website** | ASP.NET Core Web App (`Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Web`) | Thin entry point. References the CodeSamples DLL, wires up DI and Kentico services. Contains almost no domain logic. |\n' +
        '20. \n' +
        '21. The Website registers CodeSamples via `AddApplicationPart` (controllers) and a custom `AddCodeSamplesViews()` extension (Razor views).\n' +
        '22. \n' +
        '23. ### Directory Layout\n' +
        '24. \n' +
        '25. ```\n' +
        '26. src/_code/src/\n' +
        '27.   Solution.slnx                    — Solution file (CodeSamples + Website projects)\n' +
        '28.   CodeSamples/                     — Main code samples library\n' +
        '29.     CodeSamples.csproj.sample      — Project file template (copy → .csproj, restore NuGet)\n' +
        '30.     DigitalCommerce/               — Feature area: digital commerce services, stock, pricing\n' +
        '31.     Membership/                    — Feature area: auth, registration, user management\n' +
        '32.     Views/                         — Razor views referenced by code samples\n' +
        '33.     Generated/                     — Auto-generated content types (do NOT edit — run codegen)\n' +
        '34.   Website/                         — ASP.NET host project that references CodeSamples\n' +
        '35.     Website.csproj.sample          — Project file template\n' +
        '36. ```\n' +
        '37. \n' +
        '38. ### Feature-Folder Organization\n' +
        '39. \n' +
        '40. Each functional domain gets its own top-level folder inside the CodeSamples project. When adding a new feature area, create a new top-level folder following the same pattern. Each feature folder typically contains:\n' +
        '41. \n' +
        '42. - **Controllers/** — ASP.NET MVC controllers\n' +
        '43. - **Services/** — Business logic and Xperience API integration\n' +
        '44. - **Models/** — View models and DTOs\n' +
        '45. - **Extensions/** — `IServiceCollection` extension methods for DI registration\n' +
        '46. - **StandaloneSamples/** — Self-contained example files demonstrating isolated API usage (not wired into the running Website). Use `//Include:` / `//EndInclude:` markers to demarcate extractable regions.\n' +
        '47. \n' +
        '48. ### Generated Content Types\n' +
        '49. \n' +
        '50. The `Generated/` folder contains auto-generated C# classes produced by the Xperience code generator. Run `npm run codesamples:codegen` to regenerate. **Never edit these files manually.**\n' +
        '51. \n' +
        '52. ## code_link Integration\n' +
        '53. \n' +
        '54. Documentation pages reference compiled code via the {% raw %}`{% code_link %}`{% endraw %} tag:\n' +
        '55. \n' +
        '56. ```liquid\n' +
        '57. {% raw %}\n' +
        '58. {% code_link source="CodeSamples/FeatureArea/ClassName.cs" lang=csharp title="Title" id="section-id" exclude="inner" %}\n' +
        '59. {% endraw %}\n' +
        '60. ```\n' +
        '61. \n' +
        '62. - `source` (required) — path **relative to `src/_code/src/`**\n' +
        '63. - `lang` (required) — language\n' +
        '64. - `id` (optional) — extract only the region between `//Include:section-id` and `//EndInclude:section-id` markers in the source file\n' +
        '65. - `exclude` (optional) — exclude a nested region within the included section\n' +
        '66. - `title`, `highlight`, `linenumbers` — same as {% raw %}`{% code %}`{% endraw %}\n' +
        '67. \n' +
        '68. ## CI Repository and Object Codenames\n' +
        '69. \n' +
        "70. The codesamples project uses Xperience's [Continuous Integration](https://docs.kentico.com/documentation/developers-and-admins/ci-cd/configure-ci-cd-repositories) feature to persist database objects as XML files in `src/_code/src/Website/App_Data/CIRepository/`."
    },
