      'gen_ai.tool.call.result': '1. ---\n' +
        '2. name: ralph-codesamples-bootstrap\n' +
        '3. description: "Bootstrap a working Xperience by Kentico codesamples project from scratch — version installation, NuGet restore, database creation, CI restore, and verification. Use this skill when the task requires setting up a fresh codesamples environment, running codesamples:setversion, troubleshooting NuGet or database setup, or when the trigger includes an xpversion parameter."\n' +
        '4. ---\n' +
        '5. \n' +
        '6. # Codesamples Bootstrap Skill\n' +
        '7. \n' +
        '8. How to bootstrap a working Xperience by Kentico codesamples project from scratch. This is the foundational setup that enables later code sample writing, testing, and admin UI interaction.\n' +
        '9. \n' +
        '10. ## Prerequisites\n' +
        '11. \n' +
        '12. Before bootstrapping, verify these prerequisites are met:\n' +
        '13. \n' +
        "14. - **`license.txt`** must exist at `src/_code/license.txt` — manual setup, not the agent's job. If missing, the script fails early with a clear error.\n" +
        '15. - **`ADO_PAT_XPERIENCE`** env var must be set — required for private NuGet feed authentication and for resolving PR/build URLs via the ADO API. The PAT needs **Code (Read)**, **Packaging (Read)**, and **Build (Read)** scopes on the `kenticoxperience` Azure DevOps org.\n' +
        '16. - **MSSQL server** available at `DB_HOST:DB_PORT` — provided by the `db` Docker service. Verify accessibility with `sqlcmd` before proceeding:\n' +
        '17. \n' +
        '18. ```bash\n' +
        '19. sqlcmd -S "$DB_HOST,$DB_PORT" -U sa -P "$MSSQL_SA_PASSWORD" -C -Q "SELECT 1"\n' +
        '20. ```\n' +
        '21. \n' +
        '22. If this command cannot connect, do not continue with bootstrap.\n' +
        '23. \n' +
        '24. ## Pre-bootstrapped Project Detection\n' +
        '25. \n' +
        '26. Before running `setversion`, check if the project is already bootstrapped:\n' +
        '27. \n' +
        '28. ```bash\n' +
        '29. # Extract the current version from a csproj file\n' +
        `30. CURRENT=$(grep -oPm1 'Include="Kentico\\.Xperience\\..*?" Version="\\K[^"]+' src/_code/src/Website/Website.csproj)\n` +
        '31. ```\n' +
        '32. \n' +
        '33. Compare `CURRENT` against the requested version:\n' +
        '34. \n' +
        '35. - **Exact match** — skip `setversion` entirely. Proceed directly to restore → build → database → smoke test.\n' +
        '36. - **Different version or wildcard (`*`)** — run `setversion` with the requested version. Do NOT reuse the existing build artifacts.\n' +
        '37. - **No version found** — fresh project, run `setversion` as normal.\n' +
        '38. \n' +
        '39. > **Only an exact version match qualifies as pre-bootstrapped.** If the csproj has `31.2.2` but the task requests a PR URL or a different semver, always run the full `setversion` flow — the PR may contain unreleased API changes that the task depends on.\n' +
        '40. \n' +
        '41. ## Version Installation\n' +
        '42. \n' +
        '43. Run the version installation script with the target version:\n' +
        '44. \n' +
        '45. ```bash\n' +
        '46. npm run codesamples:setversion -- <version>\n' +
        '47. ```\n' +
        '48. \n' +
        '49. ### Supported version formats\n' +
        '50. \n' +
        '51. | Format | Example | Description |\n' +
        '52. |--------|---------|-------------|\n' +
        '53. | Public NuGet semver | `31.0.0` | Released version from nuget.org |\n' +
        '54. | Kentico.Private feed | `31.1.0-<hash>` | Pre-release from private ADO feed |\n' +
        '55. | ADO PR URL | `https://dev.azure.com/kenticoxperience/CMS/_git/xperience/pullrequest/24735` | Resolves artifacts from a pull request |\n' +
        '56. | ADO build URL | `https://dev.azure.com/kenticoxperience/CMS/_build/results?buildId=550290` | Resolves artifacts from a specific build |\n' +
        '57. \n' +
        '58. ### What the script does\n' +
        '59. \n' +
        '60. 1. Initializes `nuget.config` (uses `$ADO_PAT_XPERIENCE` for private feed auth)\n' +
        '61. 2. Updates `.csproj` files with the pinned version\n' +
        '62. 3. Installs `kentico.xperience.dbmanager` tool\n' +
        '63. 4. Restores NuGet packages and builds the solution\n' +
        '64. 5. Creates database `codesamples-<version>`\n' +
        '65. 6. Generates `appsettings.local.json` with connection string\n' +
        '66. 7. Enables CI and restores `CIRepository/` XML files\n' +
        '67. 8. Runs data seeders (MemberSeeder, CustomerSeeder, OrderSeeder)\n' +
        '68. \n' +
        '69. ## Pre-release Packages and `--ci-migrate`\n' +
        '70. '
    },
