      'gen_ai.tool.call.result': '1. ---\n' +
        '2. name: ralph-codesamples-adminui\n' +
        '3. description: "Interact with the Xperience by Kentico admin UI via Playwright for creating and managing objects that cannot be created via code alone — promotions, taxonomies, shipping methods, order statuses, content items. Use this skill when the task requires creating admin-managed objects, the trigger includes an adminui parameter, or when objects must be persisted via CI store."\n' +
        '4. ---\n' +
        '5. \n' +
        '6. # Codesamples Admin UI Skill\n' +
        '7. \n' +
        '8. How to interact with the Xperience by Kentico admin UI via Playwright for creating and managing objects.\n' +
        '9. \n' +
        '10. The admin UI is a **React SPA** with client-side routing. All pages load asynchronously — you will see a "Preparing your Xperience" splash before the real content renders. Always wait for `networkidle` + a short timeout after navigation.\n' +
        '11. \n' +
        '12. ## Strategy: Explore First, Then Act\n' +
        '13. \n' +
        '14. **Always screenshot before interacting.** The admin UI has many conditional fields, dynamic sections, and context-specific controls. Before filling any form:\n' +
        '15. \n' +
        '16. 1. Navigate to the target page\n' +
        '17. 2. Wait for load (`networkidle` + `waitForTimeout(3000)`)\n' +
        "18. 3. Screenshot to see what's on the page\n" +
        '19. 4. Read the accessibility snapshot to identify exact element roles, labels, and structure\n' +
        '20. 5. Only then interact with elements using the exact selectors from the snapshot\n' +
        '21. \n' +
        "22. **Never hard-code selectors you haven't verified.** Even this skill document may not cover every edge case — always confirm with a screenshot.\n" +
        '23. \n' +
        '24. ## Evidence Screenshots\n' +
        '25. \n' +
        '26. **Save a screenshot to `/tmp/mcp-attachments/` after every key interaction.** These are attached to the JIRA issue during handoff as visual evidence of admin UI work.\n' +
        '27. \n' +
        '28. Use sequential numbering with a descriptive suffix:\n' +
        '29. \n' +
        '30. ```bash\n' +
        '31. playwright-cli screenshot --filename=/tmp/mcp-attachments/adminui-01-login.png\n' +
        '32. playwright-cli screenshot --filename=/tmp/mcp-attachments/adminui-02-discount-form.png\n' +
        '33. playwright-cli screenshot --filename=/tmp/mcp-attachments/adminui-03-discount-saved.png\n' +
        '34. ```\n' +
        '35. \n' +
        '36. **When to screenshot:**\n' +
        '37. - After successful login (dashboard visible)\n' +
        '38. - After navigating to a target section (list view loaded)\n' +
        '39. - After filling a form (before clicking Save/Continue)\n' +
        '40. - After saving/creating an object (success state)\n' +
        '41. - After any verification step (e.g., confirming object appears in the list)\n' +
        '42. \n' +
        '43. The handoff workflow automatically attaches all files from `/tmp/mcp-attachments/` to JIRA.\n' +
        '44. \n' +
        '45. ## Access\n' +
        '46. \n' +
        '47. - **URL:** `localhost:666/admin`\n' +
        '48. - **Login:** `administrator` / `admin`\n' +
        '49. - **Prerequisite:** The codesamples server must be running (`npm run codesamples:serve`)\n' +
        '50. \n' +
        '51. ## Login Flow\n' +
        '52. \n' +
        '53. ```\n' +
        '54. Navigate to localhost:666/admin → redirects to /admin/logon\n' +
        '55. Fill textbox "User name"  → administrator\n' +
        '56. Fill textbox "Password"   → admin\n' +
        '57. Click button "Sign in"\n' +
        '58. Wait for networkidle + 3s → dashboard loads at /admin/dashboard\n' +
        '59. ```\n' +
        '60. \n' +
        '61. ## Admin Navigation\n' +
        '62. \n' +
        "63. The left sidebar has 5 category buttons. Clicking one expands its sub-application list. Use direct URL navigation instead — it's faster and more reliable.\n" +
        '64. \n' +
        '65. | Section | URL | Sidebar Category |\n' +
        '66. |---------|-----|-----------------|\n' +
        '67. | Dashboard | `/admin/dashboard` | — |\n' +
        '68. | Content hub | `/admin/content-hub` | Content management |\n' +
        '69. | Content types | `/admin/content-types/list` | Configuration |\n' +
        '70. | Taxonomies | `/admin/taxonomy/list` | Configuration |'
    },
