      'gen_ai.tool.call.result': '1. ---\n' +
        '2. name: malph-workflow-handoff\n' +
        '3. description: "Malph review workflow Phase 6 — the final phase. Read this skill after dispatching the verdict agent. Covers attaching the review handoff to JIRA, posting to ralphchives, and printing the ralph-result exit block."\n' +
        '4. ---\n' +
        '5. \n' +
        '6. # Phase 6: Handoff & Exit\n' +
        '7. \n' +
        '8. ## Before you begin\n' +
        '9. \n' +
        '10. 1. **Read `state.md`** at `.ralph/tasks/{{ taskId }}/state.md`\n' +
        "11. 2. This skill is for **Phase 6: Handoff & Exit**. If you've already completed this phase, you should have already printed the exit block.\n" +
        '12. 3. **Check the verdict** in `state.md` — confirm Phase 5 is complete and `malph-verdict` has returned.\n' +
        '13. \n' +
        '14. ## Instructions\n' +
        '15. \n' +
        '16. ### 1. Attach the review handoff to JIRA\n' +
        '17. \n' +
        '18. The `malph-verdict` agent has already written the review handoff to `/tmp/mcp-attachments/review-handoff.md`.\n' +
        '19. \n' +
        '20. Attach the file to **{{ taskId }}** using the `jira_add_attachment` tool with file name `review-handoff.md`.\n' +
        '21. \n' +
        '22. ### 2. Report to ralphchives\n' +
        '23. \n' +
        "24. Use the verdict summary from `malph-verdict`'s `status.json` to report:\n" +
        '25. \n' +
        '26. 1. Search for an existing thread: `search_ralphchives` with query `{{ taskId }}`\n' +
        "27. 2. If a thread exists (Ralph's task report) → use `reply_to_thread` to add the review verdict as a reply\n" +
        '28. 3. Only if no thread exists → use `post_task_report` to create one\n' +
        '29. \n' +
        '30. Keep the ralphchives report brief — the verdict and issue count from `status.json` is sufficient.\n' +
        '31. \n' +
        '32. ### 3. Return result\n' +
        '33. \n' +
        '34. Output your result in this exact format:\n' +
        '35. \n' +
        '36. ```\n' +
        '37. <ralph-result>\n' +
        '38. status: completed\n' +
        '39. summary: Reviewed PR for {{ taskId }}. Verdict: APPROVED | NEEDS REVISION (N issues found).\n' +
        '40. </ralph-result>\n' +
        '41. ```\n' +
        '42. \n' +
        '43. Use `completed` for both approvals and revision requests — Malph always completes successfully. Derive the verdict and issue count from the `malph-verdict` status.json `result` and `summary` fields.'
    },
