      'gen_ai.tool.call.result': '1. ---\n' +
        '2. name: devralph-workflow\n' +
        '3. description: "Router for the Stacky fullstack development workflow — both standard (9 phases) and revision (4 phases). Read this skill at the start of every task and at every phase transition. Use when starting a new task, when state.md shows any phase, when the agent needs phase-specific instructions, or when transitioning between phases."\n' +
        '4. ---\n' +
        '5. \n' +
        '6. # Stacky Development Workflow\n' +
        '7. \n' +
        '8. This is the **single entry point** for the Stacky fullstack development workflow. It routes to phase-specific reference files based on whether this is a standard or revision task.\n' +
        '9. \n' +
        "10. **Your `state.md` file at `.ralph/tasks/{{ taskId }}/state.md` is your single source of truth.** Read it before every phase. It tells you where you are, what you've done, and which reference files to read next.\n" +
        '11. \n' +
        '12. {%- if isRevision %}\n' +
        '13. \n' +
        '14. ## Revision Workflow\n' +
        '15. \n' +
        "16. This is a **revision** — you're fixing defects found in a previous implementation for **{{ taskId }}**.\n" +
        '17. \n' +
        '18. Execute the following phases **in order**. Before each phase, read the corresponding reference file for detailed instructions. After each phase, update `state.md` with your progress and the reference file for the next phase.\n' +
        '19. \n' +
        '20. | Phase | Reference file | Summary |\n' +
        '21. |-------|---------------|---------|\n' +
        '22. | 1. Setup | `references/r1-setup.md` | Review previous handoff, extract defects, plan fixes |\n' +
        '23. | 2. Fix & Verify | `references/r2-fix.md` | Dispatch stacky-coder for fixes, full verification gauntlet |\n' +
        '24. | 3. Commit | `references/r3-commit.md` | Commit with `fix(TASKID)` prefix, push to update PR |\n' +
        '25. | 4. Handoff & Exit | `references/r4-handoff.md` | Update handoff, report to JIRA, print exit block |\n' +
        '26. \n' +
        '27. {%- else %}\n' +
        '28. \n' +
        '29. ## Standard Workflow\n' +
        '30. \n' +
        '31. Execute the following phases **in order**. Before each phase, read the corresponding reference file for detailed instructions. After each phase, update `state.md` with your progress and the reference file for the next phase.\n' +
        '32. \n' +
        '33. | Phase | Reference file | Summary |\n' +
        '34. |-------|---------------|---------|\n' +
        '35. | 1. Setup | `references/1-setup.md` | Branch, scratchpad, ralphchives search, component identification |\n' +
        '36. | 2. Research | `references/2-research.md` | Dispatch stacky-analyst to produce the implementation plan |\n' +
        '37. | 3. Implement | `references/3-implement.md` | Dispatch stacky-coder to execute changes and validate builds |\n' +
        '38. | 4. Test | `references/4-test.md` | Write unit/integration tests (delegate to stacky-test-writer) |\n' +
        '39. | 5. E2E | `references/5-e2e.md` | Write Playwright E2E tests for UI changes (delegate to stacky-e2e-playwright) |\n' +
        '40. | 6. Review | `references/6-review.md` | Code review gate (stacky-reviewer + stacky-bug-auditor) |\n' +
        '41. | 7. Commit | `references/7-commit.md` | Pre-commit checks, commit, push |\n' +
        '42. | 8. PR | `references/8-pr.md` | Create ADO pull request |\n' +
        '43. | 9. Handoff & Exit | `references/9-handoff.md` | Write handoff, report to JIRA, print exit block |\n' +
        '44. \n' +
        '45. {%- endif %}\n' +
        '46. \n' +
        '47. ## How to Use\n' +
        '48. \n' +
        '49. 1. Read `state.md` to determine your current phase\n' +
        '50. 2. Read the reference file listed in the workflow table above for that phase\n' +
        "51. 3. Follow the reference file's instructions\n" +
        "52. 4. Update `state.md` as directed by the reference file's transition section\n" +
        '53. 5. Repeat from step 1'
    },
