      'gen_ai.tool.call.result': '1. ---\n' +
        '2. name: malph-workflow-investigate\n' +
        '3. description: "Malph review workflow Phase 2. Read this skill after descending on the issue. Dispatch the malph-scout sub-agent to map the PR, capture requirement-coverage risks, and run the docs build before the panel review begins."\n' +
        '4. ---\n' +
        '5. \n' +
        '6. # Phase 2: Investigate\n' +
        '7. \n' +
        '8. ## Before you begin\n' +
        '9. \n' +
        '10. 1. **Read `state.md`** at `.ralph/tasks/{{ taskId }}/state.md`\n' +
        "11. 2. This skill is for **Phase 2: Investigate**. If you've already completed this phase, skip to the next.\n" +
        '12. \n' +
        '13. ## Instructions\n' +
        '14. \n' +
        '15. 1. **You are already on the correct branch.**{% if triggerParams.branch %} The branch is `{{ triggerParams.branch }}`.{% endif %}\n' +
        '16. 2. **Dispatch `malph-scout`** with the task-id and a one-line directive (e.g. "Scout the PR for {{ taskId }}"). The scout reads the PR context, changed files, and build status on its own.\n' +
        '17. 3. After the scout returns, read its `status.json` at `.ralph/tasks/{{ taskId }}/artifacts/malph-scout/status.json`.\n' +
        '18. 4. If the scout returns `blocked`, record the `summary` in `state.md` and stop.\n' +
        '19. 5. If the scout returns `build-broken`, note the build failure in `state.md` — the verdict agent will handle it.\n' +
        '20. \n' +
        '21. Do **not** read `scout-findings.json` or `output.md`. Downstream subagents read scout artifacts directly from the filesystem.\n' +
        '22. \n' +
        '23. ## Before moving to Phase 3\n' +
        '24. \n' +
        '25. Update `state.md`:\n' +
        '26. - Set "Current Phase" to `Phase 3: Verify Technical Claims`\n' +
        '27. - Set "Skills for this phase" to:\n' +
        '28.   - malph-workflow-verify\n' +
        '29. - Add Phase 2 to "Completed Phases" — note the scout\'s `result` and `summary` from `status.json`\n' +
        '30. - Record the scout\'s `result` and `summary` under "Scout Status" in `state.md`'
    },
