        '2. name: malph-vscode-workflow-aggregate\n' +
        '3. description: "VS Code extension review orchestrator Phase 4. Aggregate reviewer verdicts and findings, then post a unified review comment to JIRA."\n' +
        '4. ---\n' +
        '5. \n' +
        '6. # Phase 4: Aggregate & Deliver\n' +
        '7. \n' +
        '8. ## Before you begin\n' +
        '9. \n' +
        '10. 1. **Read `state.md`** at `.ralph/tasks/{{ taskId }}/state.md`\n' +
        '11. 2. **Verify the current phase** — this skill is for Phase 4.\n' +
        '12. 3. **Review completed phases** — confirm Phase 3 (Review Panel) is done.\n' +
        '13. \n' +
        '14. ## Instructions\n' +
        '15. \n' +
        '16. ### 1. Read all reviewer artifacts\n' +
        '17. \n' +
        '18. For each reviewer that completed successfully, read:\n' +
        '19. - `.ralph/tasks/{{ taskId }}/artifacts/malph-reviewer-opus/status.json`\n' +
        '20. - `.ralph/tasks/{{ taskId }}/artifacts/malph-reviewer-opus/jira-findings.json`\n' +
        '21. - `.ralph/tasks/{{ taskId }}/artifacts/malph-reviewer-gpt/status.json`\n' +
        '22. - `.ralph/tasks/{{ taskId }}/artifacts/malph-reviewer-gpt/jira-findings.json`\n' +
        '23. - `.ralph/tasks/{{ taskId }}/artifacts/malph-reviewer-gemini/status.json`\n' +
        '24. - `.ralph/tasks/{{ taskId }}/artifacts/malph-reviewer-gemini/jira-findings.json`\n' +
        '25. \n' +
        '26. Skip any reviewer whose `status.json` shows `status: failed`.\n' +
        '27. \n' +
        '28. ### 2. Determine panel verdict\n' +
        '29. \n' +
        '30. Apply the **unanimous approval rule**:\n' +
        '31. - ANY reviewer verdict of `needs-revision` → overall **NEEDS REVISION**\n' +
        '32. - Only unanimous `approved` → overall **APPROVED**\n' +
        '33. - If all successful reviewers approved but one failed, treat the panel verdict as the majority\n' +
        '34. \n' +
        '35. ### 3. Aggregate findings\n' +
        '36. \n' +
        '37. Merge findings from all `jira-findings.json` files:\n' +
        '38. - Deduplicate by issue code + file + line — if multiple reviewers flag the same issue at the same location, keep the most detailed description and note which reviewers agreed\n' +
        '39. - Group by severity: Critical (must fix) → Style (should fix) → Suggestions (optional)\n' +
        '40. - Preserve the `code`, `file`, `line`, `detail`, and `correction` fields from each finding\n' +
        '41. \n' +
        '42. ### 4. Post unified JIRA comment\n' +
        '43. \n' +
        '44. Post a single rich comment on **{{ taskId }}** with the panel verdict:\n' +
        '45. \n' +
        '46. ```\n' +
        '47. ## Review Panel Verdict: APPROVED | NEEDS REVISION\n' +
        '48. \n' +
        '49. **Panel:** 3 reviewers (Opus 4.6, GPT 5.4, Gemini Pro)\n' +
        '50. **Scout:** Build PASS | FAIL\n' +
        '51. \n' +
        '52. ### Reviewer Verdicts\n' +
        '53. | Reviewer | Verdict | Findings |\n' +
        '54. |---|---|---|\n' +
        '55. | malph-reviewer-opus | approved / needs-revision / failed | N findings |\n' +
        '56. | malph-reviewer-gpt | approved / needs-revision / failed | N findings |\n' +
        '57. | malph-reviewer-gemini | approved / needs-revision / failed | N findings |\n' +
        '58. \n' +
        '59. ### Aggregated Findings\n' +
        '60. \n' +
        '61. #### Critical (must fix)\n' +
        '62. - **[ARCH-001]** `file:line` — description *(flagged by: opus, gpt)*\n' +
        '63. \n' +
        '64. #### Style (should fix)\n' +
        '65. - **[TS-003]** `file:line` — description *(flagged by: gemini)*\n' +
        '66. \n' +
        '67. #### Suggestions\n' +
        '68. - **[SUG-001]** description *(flagged by: opus)*\n' +
        '69. \n' +
        '70. ### Summary'
    },
