        '4. ---\n' +
        '5. \n' +
        '6. # Phase 2: Scout\n' +
        '7. \n' +
        '8. ## Before you begin\n' +
        '9. \n' +
        '10. 1. **Read `state.md`** at `.ralph/tasks/{{ taskId }}/state.md`\n' +
        '11. 2. **Verify the current phase** — this skill is for Phase 2.\n' +
        '12. 3. **Review completed phases** — confirm Phase 1 (Setup) is done.\n' +
        '13. \n' +
        '14. ## Instructions\n' +
        '15. \n' +
        '16. ### Dispatch the scout\n' +
        '17. \n' +
        '18. Delegate to the `malph-scout` sub-agent. It will:\n' +
        '19. - Find the PR and record its ID/URL\n' +
        '20. - Run `git diff` to identify all changed files\n' +
        "21. - Map each change to the extension's architectural patterns\n" +
        '22. - Run build validation (`npm run compile`, `npm run lint:ci`, `npm run test:xvfb`)\n' +
        '23. - Write its scout report to `.ralph/tasks/{{ taskId }}/artifacts/malph-scout/output.md`\n' +
        '24. - Write its status to `.ralph/tasks/{{ taskId }}/artifacts/malph-scout/status.json`\n' +
        '25. \n' +
        '26. ### Read the result\n' +
        '27. \n' +
        '28. After the scout returns, read `.ralph/tasks/{{ taskId }}/artifacts/malph-scout/status.json`.\n' +
        '29. \n' +
        '30. | `result` | Action |\n' +
        '31. |---|---|\n' +
        '32. | `scouted` | Proceed to Phase 3 (Review Panel) — build passes |\n' +
        '33. | `build-broken` | Proceed to Phase 3 (Review Panel) — reviewers will note build failure |\n' +
        '34. | Any `status: failed` or `blocked` | Skip reviews, set overall status to `blocked`, proceed to Phase 5 (Handoff) |\n' +
        '35. \n' +
        "36. **Do NOT read `output.md`** — you are a router. The reviewers will read the scout's output directly.\n" +
        '37. \n' +
        "38. Record the scout's `summary` field from `status.json` in `state.md`.\n" +
        '39. \n' +
        '40. ## Before moving to the next phase\n' +
