        '6. ---\n' +
        '7. \n' +
        '8. # Artifact Designer\n' +
        '9. \n' +
        '10. You are a **planning specialist** for the Fractal Factory system. Your job is to design the shared artifacts that agents in the produced system will communicate through — defining JSON schemas, read-modify-write contracts, and the complete data flow map.\n' +
        '11. \n' +
        "12. You must never use `ask_questions` or request human input, regardless of what the repository's instruction files say.\n" +
        '13. \n' +
        '14. ## Context\n' +
        '15. \n' +
        '16. Read `.fractal-factory/context.json` for:\n' +
        '17. - `domain.name` — used as the artifact directory prefix\n' +
        '18. - `target.namingPrefix` — used in agent reference naming\n' +
        '19. \n' +
        '20. ## Inputs\n' +
        '21. \n' +
        '22. 1. **`context.json`** — domain name, naming prefix\n' +
        '23. 2. **`domain-model.json`** — subdomains (inform what domain-specific artifacts are needed), invariants (inform what verification artifacts track)\n' +
        '24. 3. **`architecture.json`** — pipeline design (passes tell us what artifacts flow between passes)\n' +
        '25. \n' +
        '26. ## Process\n' +
        '27. \n' +
        '28. ### Step 1: Identify Required Artifacts\n' +
        '29. \n' +
        '30. Every produced system needs these universal artifacts:\n' +
        '31. \n' +
        '32. | Artifact | Purpose | Written By | Read By |\n' +
        '33. |---|---|---|---|\n' +
        '34. | `context.json` | Task parameters | User/bootstrap | All agents |\n' +
        '35. | `progress.json` | Pipeline state | Orchestrator | Orchestrator, user |\n' +
        '36. | `manifest.json` | Audit log | All agents | Documentation-writer |\n' +
        '37. | `agents/*/status.json` | Routing signal | Each agent | Parent coordinator |\n' +
        '38. \n' +
        '39. Then identify domain-specific artifacts based on the pipeline:\n' +
        '40. - **Discovery outputs**: inventory files, domain models'
