      'gen_ai.tool.call.result': '1. ---\n' +
        '2. name: xperience\n' +
        '3. description: A router skill for working with Xperience by Kentico source code and product internals. Use this skill whenever you need to orient yourself in the CMSSolution codebase, identify which subsystem owns a feature, map documentation topics to source roots, or find the right product area before doing deeper research. Use it for source-structure questions even when the user only mentions a feature name and not the repository layout explicitly.\n' +
        '4. ---\n' +
        '5. \n' +
        '6. # Xperience by Kentico Source Map\n' +
        '7. \n' +
        '8. This skill maps the major source-code areas under `./resources/repositories/xperience/CMSSolution/`.\n' +
        '9. \n' +
        '10. Use it to answer questions like:\n' +
        '11. \n' +
        '12. - which subsystem owns this feature\n' +
        '13. - where a documentation topic maps into product source code\n' +
        '14. - which root directories matter before doing detailed code search\n' +
        '15. - how product surfaces relate to each other at a high level\n' +
        '16. \n' +
        '17. For documentation-tree orientation rather than source-tree orientation, use the companion `xperience-documentation` skill.\n' +
        '18. \n' +
        '19. ## Solution and Platform Structure\n' +
        '20. \n' +
        '21. - [Solution foundations](references/source-solution-foundations.md) — solution-level build/config anchors plus the shared platform roots such as `Base`, `Core`, `Helpers`, and `Modules`\n' +
        '22. - [Data, security, and operations](references/source-data-security-operations.md) — `DataEngine`, `DbDataManager`, `DataProtection`, `MacroEngine`, `Scheduler`, `ContinuousIntegration`, `WebFarmSync`, and other horizontal runtime services\n' +
        '23. - [Integrations and storage](references/source-integrations-and-storage.md) — external integration packages plus the internal file/storage abstraction layer in `IO`\n' +
        '24. - [Tooling, samples, and tests](references/source-tooling-samples-tests.md) — analyzers, templates, internal tools, samples, and subsystem-oriented test projects\n' +
        '25. \n' +
        '26. ## Product Surfaces\n' +
        '27. \n' +
        '28. - [Content and channels](references/source-content-and-channels.md) — `ContentEngine`, `Websites`, `Headless`, `MediaLibrary`, workflow, sync, and workspaces\n' +
        '29. - [Admin and web runtime](references/source-admin-and-runtime.md) — `Admin`, `Mvc`, `Routing.Web`, `Membership`, and `AIRA`\n' +
        '30. - [Marketing and engagement](references/source-marketing-and-engagement.md) — activities, contacts, automation, journeys, email, forms, and online marketing\n' +
        '31. - [Commerce](references/source-commerce.md) — customers, carts, orders, pricing, promotions, payments, and shipping\n' +
        '32. \n' +
        '33. ## Deep Topic References\n' +
        '34. \n' +
        '35. - [Page permissions](references/page-permissions.md) — the website page permission model: application access, page ACLs, workflow roles, the Read prerequisite rule, and operation-to-permission mapping'
    },
