              "arguments": "{\"command\": \"cat > /tmp/skills-inventory.txt << 'EOF'\\n# COMPREHENSIVE SKILLS INVENTORY — ralph-orchestrator\\n\\n## DOMAIN SKILLS (20 skills)\\nCode review, testing, documentation, and build-related domain expertise for the Xperience by Kentico docs project.\\n\\n### Domain - Code & Development\\n1. code-typescript-bps\\n   Path: shared/skills/domain/code-typescript-bps/\\n   Domain: Code Quality / TypeScript Best Practices\\n   Description: Guidelines for writing clean, type-safe, and maintainable TypeScript code. Covers type-first design, naming conventions, generics patterns, and type assertion best practices.\\n\\n2. code-typescript-review\\n   Path: shared/skills/domain/code-typescript-review/\\n   Domain: Code Review\\n   Description: Perform comprehensive code reviews for TypeScript projects, analyzing type safety, best practices, performance, security, and code quality with actionable feedback.\\n\\n### Domain - Build & Deployment\\n3. devralph-build-verification\\n   Path: shared/skills/domain/devralph-build-verification/\\n   Domain: Build & Deployment\\n   Description: Build verification and error troubleshooting reference. Covers primary build commands, pipeline stages, and diagnosis strategies across Jekyll, Ruby gems, Webpack, CSS, and Gulp.\\n\\n4. ralph-build-errors\\n   Path: shared/skills/domain/ralph-build-errors/\\n   Domain: Build Troubleshooting\\n   Description: Troubleshooting guide for common npm run build errors including broken page_link identifiers, missing anchors, duplicate identifiers, and code block issues.\\n\\n### Domain - Documentation & Content\\n5. ralph-documentation-syntax\\n   Path: shared/skills/domain/ralph-documentation-syntax/\\n   Domain: Documentation Authoring\\n   Description: Complete reference for all Liquid tags, formatting, and components available in the Jekyll documentation site including admonitions, code blocks, images, anchors, and cross-references.\\n\\n6. ralph-new-page-creation\\n   Path: shared/skills/domain/ralph-new-page-creation/\\n   Domain: Documentation Authoring\\n   Description: Rules for creating new Markdown documentation pages including frontmatter schema, identifiers, persona assignment, ordering, and licensing.\\n\\n7. ralph-page-removal\\n   Path: shared/skills/domain/ralph-page-removal/\\n   Domain: Documentation Maintenance\\n   Description: Checklist for removing or deprecating documentation pages without leaving broken links, including redirect setup, reference cleanup, and validation.\\n\\n8. ralph-callout-selection\\n   Path: shared/skills/domain/ralph-callout-selection/\\n   Domain: Documentation Style\\n   Description: Semantic guide for choosing the correct admonition type (tip, info, note, warning, key) to avoid desensitizing readers and maintaining consistent severity.\\n\\n9. ralph-cross-version-linking\\n   Path: shared/skills/domain/ralph-cross-version-linking/\\n   Domain: Documentation Navigation\\n   Description: How to link across documentation collections (documentation, guides, api) using collection parameters on page_link and card tags.\\n\\n10. ralph-style-guide-review\\n    Path: shared/skills/domain/ralph-style-guide-review/\\n    Domain: Documentation Style\\n    Description: Writing standards for self-reviewing documentation — UI interaction verbs, formatting rules, tone, voice, sentence structure, and callout usage.\\n\\n11. ralph-research-guide\\n    Path: shared/skills/domain/ralph-research-guide/\\n    Domain: Documentation Research\\n    Description: Complete research guide covering research order, techniques for exploring docs, source code, and external references, plus report template and validation.\\n\\n### Domain - Frontend\\n12. devralph-frontend\\n    Path: shared/skills/domain/devralph-frontend/\\n    Domain: Frontend Development\\n    Description: Frontend architecture reference covering JavaScript (ES modules, Webpack, 4 bundles), jQuery patterns, Tailwind v4, Less styling, and third-party library integration.\\n\\n13. devralph-gulp-pipeline\\n    Path: shared/skills/domain/devralph-gulp-pipeline/\\n    Domain: Build Orchestration\\n    Description: Build pipeline reference for Gulp 5 orchestration layer covering task architecture, asset pipeline, Jekyll integration, BrowserSync, and config overlay system.\\n\\n14. devralph-jekyll-site\\n    Path: shared/skills/domain/devralph-jekyll-site/\\n    Domain: Site Structure\\n    Description: Jekyll site structure reference covering collections, layouts, includes, data files, frontmatter conventions, and the multi-file config overlay system.\\n\\n15. devralph-ruby-gems\\n    Path: shared/skills/domain/devralph-ruby-gems/\\n    Domain: Ruby Development\\n    Description: Architecture reference for 8 custom Ruby gems covering DI container, tag base classes, validation, Liquid tag system, and Learn Portal.\\n\\n### Domain - VSCode Extension\\n16. vscode-extension-performance\\n    Path: shared/skills/domain/vscode-extension-performance/\\n    Domain: VSCode Extension Performance\\n    Description: Guidance for keeping VS Code extensions fast to activate, cheap to load, and lightweight — covers activation events, bundling, and performance profiling.\\n\\n17. vscode-grammar-and-scopes\\n    Path: shared/skills/domain/vscode-grammar-and-scopes/\\n    Domain: VSCode Grammar & Syntax\\n    Description: Guidance for changing VS Code TextMate grammars, injection grammars, syntax highlighting, embedded languages, and scope naming.\\n\\n### Domain - Testing\\n18. test-behavior-testing\\n    Path: shared/skills/domain/test-behavior-testing/\\n    Domain: Testing Strategy\\n    Description: Guide for writing tests that verify behavior and outputs rather than implementation details, avoiding brittle tests that break on refactoring.\\n\\n19. test-mocking-strategy\\n    Path: shared/skills/domain/test-mocking-strategy/\\n    Domain: Testing Strategy\\n    Description: Guide for when and how to mock dependencies in tests — choosing between mocks, fakes, and real collaborators at architectural boundaries.\\n\\n20. test-structure-patterns\\n    Path: shared/skills/domain/test-structure-patterns/\\n    Domain: Testing Strategy\\n    Description: Guide for structuring test files, naming tests, using Given/When/Then, organizing tests by behavior, and understanding observable output.\\n\\n\\n## INTEGRATION SKILLS (6 skills)\\nIntegration with external systems, code samples, and knowledge bases.\\n\\n1. ralph-ado-pr-workflow\\n   Path: shared/skills/integrations/ralph-ado-pr-workflow/\\n   Domain: Pull Request Management\\n   Description: Instructions for creating and managing pull requests in Azure DevOps including PR description formatting and change annotation.\\n\\n2. ralph-codegraph\\n   Path: shared/skills/integrations/ralph-codegraph/\\n   Domain: Code Analysis / Graph Queries\\n   Description: Query Xperience source code structure using CodeGraphContext MCP tools — call chains, class hierarchies, dead code detection, and complexity metrics via Cypher.\\n\\n3. ralph-codesamples-verification\\n   Path: shared/skills/integrations/ralph-codesamples-verification/\\n   Domain: Testing & Verification\\n   Description: Functionally verify ASP.NET Core codesamples application using playwright-cli to exercise routes, forms, and application behavior after implementation changes.\\n\\n4. ralph-ralphchives\\n   Path: shared/skills/integrations/ralph-ralphchives/\\n   Domain: Knowledge Management\\n   Description: Workflow for searching and posting to the Ralphchives persistent knowledge base — access prior work, post observations during work, and record task reports.\\n\\n5. ralph-screenshots\\n    Path: shared/skills/integrations/ralph-screenshots/\\n    Domain: Visual Documentation\\n    Description: Instructions for capturing clean admin UI screenshots using playwright-cli including workflow, element highlighting, and evidence attachment to JIRA.\\n\\n6. ralph-source-references\\n   Path: shared/skills/integrations/ralph-source-references/\\n   Domain: Code Reference\\n   Description: URL format for citing Xperience source code in JIRA comments and handoff files using the source browser with navigable links.\\n\\n\\n## TASK SKILLS (6 skills)\\nHigh-level task execution and project-specific workflows.\\n\\n1. ralph-codesamples\\n   Path: shared/skills/tasks/ralph-codesamples/\\n   Domain: Code Samples Management\\n   Description: Complete reference for the Xperience codesamples .NET project — solution structure, feature-folder organization, code_link integration, and build workflow.\\n\\n2. ralph-codesamples-adminui\\n   Path: shared/skills/tasks/ralph-codesamples-adminui/\\n   Domain: UI Interaction / Admin Testing\\n   Description: Interact with Xperience admin UI via Playwright for creating and managing objects (promotions, taxonomies, shipping, order statuses, content items).\\n\\n3. ralph-codesamples-bootstrap\\n   Path: shared/skills/tasks/ralph-codesamples-bootstrap/\\n   Domain: Project Setup\\n   Description: Bootstrap a working Xperience codesamples project from scratch — version installation, NuGet restore, database creation, CI restore, and verification.\\n\\n4. ralph-task-planning\\n   Path: shared/skills/tasks/ralph-task-planning/\\n   Domain: Project Planning\\n   Description: Core planning skill for turning research artifacts or revision feedback into ordered, machine-friendly task plans for headless execution.\\n\\n5. ralph-training-modules\\n   Path: shared/skills/tasks/ralph-training-modules/\\n   Domain: Learning Content\\n   Description: YAML schema and templates for creating structured training modules and learning paths including personas and module sequences.\\n\\n6. ralph-write-release-notes\\n   Path: shared/skills/tasks/ralph-write-release-notes/\\n   Domain: Release Documentation\\n   Description: Format and examples for writing release notes for Xperience features and changes — user-focused, capability-driven descriptions.\\n\\n\\n## WORKFLOW SKILLS (15 skills)\\nPhase-based orchestration skills for documentation and extension development workflows.\\n\\n### Documentation Workflow (8 skills)\\n1. ralph-workflow\\n   Path: shared/skills/workflow/docs/ralph-workflow/\\n   Domain: Documentation Workflow Orchestration\\n   Description: Router for the Ralph documentation workflow — both standard (8 phases) and revision (7 phases). Entry point for all phase transitions and instructions.\\n\\n2. devralph-workflow\\n   Path: shared/skills/workflow/docs/devralph-workflow/\\n   Domain: Fullstack Development Workflow\\n   Description: Router for the Stacky fullstack development workflow — standard (9 phases) and revision (4 phases). Directs to phase-specific reference files.\\n\\n3. malph-workflow-descend\\n   Path: shared/skills/workflow/docs/malph-workflow-descend/\\n   Domain: Review Workflow - Phase 1\\n   Description: Malph review workflow Phase 1. Covers reading JIRA issues, downloading handoffs, searching ralphchives, and creating state.md.\\n\\n4. malph-workflow-investigate\\n   Path: shared/skills/workflow/docs/malph-workflow-investigate/\\n   Domain: Review Workflow - Phase 2\\n   Description: Malph review workflow Phase 2. Dispatch malph-scout to map PR, capture risks, and run docs build before panel review.\\n\\n5. malph-workflow-verify\\n   Path: shared/skills/workflow/docs/malph-workflow-verify/\\n   Domain: Review Workflow - Phase 3\\n   Description: Malph review workflow Phase 3. Dispatch technical reviewer and record status.json result for technical accuracy verification.\\n\\n6. malph-workflow-review\\n   Path: shared/skills/workflow/docs/malph-workflow-review/\\n   Domain: Review Workflow - Phase 4\\n   Description: Malph review workflow Phase 4. Dispatch specialist reviewers and determine panel verdict mechanically from status.json results.\\n\\n7. malph-workflow-deliver\\n   Path: shared/skills/workflow/docs/malph-workflow-deliver/\\n   Domain: Review Workflow - Phase 5\\n   Description: Malph review workflow Phase 5. Dispatch malph-verdict to aggregate findings, post JIRA comment, and post PR threads.\\n\\n8. malph-workflow-handoff\\n   Path: shared/skills/workflow/docs/malph-workflow-handoff/\\n   Domain: Review Workflow - Phase 6\\n   Description: Malph review workflow Phase 6 — final phase. Attach review handoff to JIRA, post to ralphchives, and print exit block.\\n\\n### VSCode Extension Workflow (7 skills)\\n9. vscode-workflow\\n   Path: shared/skills/workflow/vscode/vscode-workflow/\\n   Domain: VSCode Extension Workflow Orchestration\\n   Description: Router for VS Code extension agent workflow — standard and revision modes. Entry point for phase transitions and reference file routing.\\n\\n10. malph-vscode-workflow-setup\\n    Path: shared/skills/workflow/vscode/malph-vscode-workflow-setup/\\n    Domain: Extension Review - Phase 1\\n    Description: VS Code extension review Phase 1. Read JIRA, download handoff, find PR, and create state.md for review tracking.\\n\\n11. malph-vscode-workflow-scout\\n    Path: shared/skills/workflow/vscode/malph-vscode-workflow-scout/\\n    Domain: Extension Review - Phase 2\\n    Description: VS Code extension review Phase 2. Dispatch malph-scout for diff mapping, pattern verification, and build validation.\\n\\n12. malph-vscode-workflow-review-panel\\n    Path: shared/skills/workflow/vscode/malph-vscode-workflow-review-panel/\\n    Domain: Extension Review - Phase 3\\n    Description: VS Code extension review Phase 3. Dispatch three independent reviewers (Opus, GPT, Gemini) sequentially for full review checklist.\\n\\n13. malph-vscode-workflow-aggregate\\n    Path: shared/skills/workflow/vscode/malph-vscode-workflow-aggregate/\\n    Domain: Extension Review - Phase 4\\n    Description: VS Code extension review Phase 4. Aggregate reviewer verdicts and findings, then post unified review comment to JIRA.\\n\\n14. malph-vscode-workflow-handoff\\n    Path: shared/skills/workflow/vscode/malph-vscode-workflow-handoff/\\n    Domain: Extension Review - Phase 5\\n    Description: VS Code extension review Phase 5. Write review handoff document and attach it to JIRA.\\n\\n15. malph-vscode-workflow-archive\\n    Path: shared/skills/workflow/vscode/malph-vscode-workflow-archive/\\n    Domain: Extension Review - Phase 6\\n    Description: VS Code extension review Phase 6 — final phase. Dispatch scribe to archive knowledge to Ralphchives, then print exit block.\\n\\n\\n## XPERIENCE PRODUCT SKILLS (2 skills)\\nProduct and documentation structure mapping for Xperience by Kentico.\\n\\n1. xperience\\n   Path: shared/skills/xperience/\\n   Domain: Product Source Map\\n   Description: Router skill for working with Xperience source code. Maps major source-code areas in CMSSolution, identifies subsystem ownership, and directs to detailed references.\\n\\n2. xperience-documentation\\n   Path: shared/skills/xperience-documentation/\\n   Domain: Documentation Map\\n   Description: Maps the structure of Xperience documentation — business users section and developers/admins section. Shows where topics are documented and corresponding source code.\\n\\n\\n## SKILLS-LOCK.json ENTRIES\\nExternal registered skills (from skills-lock.json):\\n- playwright-best-practices (source: currents-dev/playwright-best-practices-skill)\\n- playwright-cli (source: microsoft/playwright-cli)\\n\\n\\n## .GITHUB/SKILLS DIRECTORY\\nThe .github/skills/ directory contains 32 additional skill directories (agents/workflows):\\n- agent-as-function, agent-as-function-audit\\n- agent-creator, agent-eval, agent-fractal-orchestrator-architecture, agent-fractal-workflow-eval\\n- agent-skill-wiring, agent-subagent-wiring, agent-workflow-phase-editor\\n- behavior-testing, builder-workflow, cli-debug-log-analysis\\n- codebase-familiarization, codegraphcontext, dashboard-development\\n- doc-coauthoring, feature-implementation-workflow, feature-task-planning\\n- looper-planner, mcp-builder, mcp-deployment, nodebb-interaction\\n- planner-loop-wiring, playwright-best-practices, playwright-cli\\n- skill-consolidator, skill-creator, task-failure-diagnosis\\n- test-mocking-strategy, test-structure-patterns\\n\\nThese are primarily agent/workflow definitions rather than traditional \\\"skills\\\" in the shared/skills/ structure.\\n\\n\\n## SUMMARY BY DOMAIN\\n\\n### Code Quality & Reviews (3)\\n- code-typescript-bps, code-typescript-review, test-behavior-testing\\n\\n### Build & Deployment (3)\\n- devralph-build-verification, ralph-build-errors, devralph-gulp-pipeline\\n\\n### Documentation Authoring (6)\\n- ralph-documentation-syntax, ralph-new-page-creation, ralph-page-removal\\n- ralph-callout-selection, ralph-cross-version-linking, ralph-style-guide-review\\n\\n### Site Architecture (3)\\n- devralph-frontend, devralph-jekyll-site, devralph-ruby-gems\\n\\n### Testing (3)\\n- test-behavior-testing, test-mocking-strategy, test-structure-patterns\\n\\n### Integration & Tools (6)\\n- ralph-ado-pr-workflow, ralph-codegraph, ralph-codesamples-verification\\n- ralph-ralphchives, ralph-screenshots, ralph-source-references\\n\\n### Code Samples (3)\\n- ralph-codesamples, ralph-codesamples-adminui, ralph-codesamples-bootstrap\\n\\n### Workflow Orchestration (8)\\n- ralph-workflow, devralph-workflow, malph-workflow-* (6 phases)\\n\\n### VSCode Extension (8)\\n- vscode-workflow, vscode-extension-performance, vscode-grammar-and-scopes\\n- malph-vscode-workflow-* (6 phases)\\n\\n### Project & Product (3)\\n- ralph-task-planning, ralph-training-modules, ralph-write-release-notes\\n- xperience, xperience-documentation\\n\\n### Research & Planning (2)\\n- ralph-research-guide\\n\\n---\\nTOTAL: 50 shared skills + 32 .github/skills agent definitions + 2 external registrations\\nEOF\\ncat /tmp/skills-inventory.txt\\n\", \"description\": \"Generate comprehensive skills inventory\"}"
