        "content": "Excellent! Now I have all the information I need. Let me compile a comprehensive inventory:\n\n---\n\n# **COMPREHENSIVE INVENTORY: Ralph-Orchestrator Shared Resources**\n\n## 1. AGENT INCLUDES\n\n### Core Framework Files\n\n| File | Path | Purpose | Content (First 50 lines) |\n|------|------|---------|----------------------|\n| **agent-as-function-contract.md** | `shared/agent-includes/` | Defines the artifact contract and output structure for subagents | Specifies artifact directory, required files (`output.md`/`output-vN.md`), `status.json` structure with fields (status, result, task_id, summary, artifacts, next_hint, iteration) |\n| **rules.md** | `shared/agent-includes/` | Operational constraints and workflow rules | Only read `status.json` for routing; never push to default branch; wait for subagent return values; never emit empty responses |\n| **prompt-security.md** | `shared/agent-includes/` | Security and data handling guidelines | Data handling from untrusted task sources; prompt injection defense; credential prevention; issue/branch scope locks; no hallucinated URLs/endpoints |\n| **source-references.md** | `shared/agent-includes/` | URL format for linking Xperience source code in comments | Namespace-based URL format for .NET source browser (e.g., `https://app-xbyk-source-prod.azurewebsites.net/#CMS.DbDataManager.Installation/SqlInstallationHelper.cs,222`) |\n| **ralphchives.md** | `shared/agent-includes/` | Knowledge base integration guide | Search archive for prior work; post observations during work; post task reports after completion; max 5 tags per topic |\n| **ado-api.md** | `shared/agent-includes/` | Azure DevOps integration | Use ado MCP server for PR operations; handle 401/403 auth errors; document conflict/validation errors in handoff |\n| **ado-pr-format.md** | `shared/agent-includes/` | Pull request description template | Standard format: JIRA-KEY title; Changes list; Context section; Review Notes with rationale and decisions |\n\n### Personality Profiles\n\n| File | Path | Purpose |\n|------|------|---------|\n| **malph.md** | `shared/agent-includes/personality/` | Malph identity (🦇) — nocturnal reviewer persona with theatrically precise, dry wit delivery. Reviews code for Ralph. Never uses `ask_questions`. Catchphrase: \"I'm not the reviewer you want. I'm the reviewer you need.\" |\n| **ralph.md** | `shared/agent-includes/personality/` | Ralph identity (🔧) — technical explorer who enjoys digging into systems. Disciplined, terse writer. Uses 🔧 prefix in PR threads. Genuine vim and vigor in interactions. |\n\n### Post-Task Hooks (Analysis & Improvement)\n\n**Directory:** `shared/agent-includes/post-hooks/` (4 files)\n\n| File | Purpose | Dispatch Trigger |\n|------|---------|------------------|\n| **agent-improver.md** (lines 1-30) | Improves Ralph templates, skills, and MCP server configs based on execution analysis | Once per subagent (after run-analyzer completes). Result codes: `improved` \\| `no-action` |\n| **run-analyzer.md** (lines 1-30) | Analyzes agent execution quality, failure patterns, improvement opportunities | Dispatched once per subagent found in run (or infra-failure mode if CLI crashed). Uses agent-eval skill. Result codes: `analyzed` \\| `skipped` |\n| **run-synthesizer.md** (lines 1-30) | Synthesizes per-subagent analysis into orchestrator-level assessment | Runs once after all per-subagent analyzer+improver complete. Covers orchestration quality, cross-subagent patterns, infrastructure health. Result codes: `synthesized` \\| `skipped` |\n| **subagent-mapper.md** (lines 1-30) | Maps all subagent invocations, extracts telemetry & artifacts, produces structured inventory | Post-task hook. Analyzes `cli-debug.log`, `summary.json`, `pre-tool.log`, `audit.jsonl`, `state.md`. Result codes: `mapped` \\| `skipped` |\n\n### Ralph Documentation Workflows (ralph-docs)\n\n**Directory:** `shared/agent-includes/ralph-docs/` (14 files, 7 workflows + code samples)\n\n#### Standard & Revision Workflows\n- **ralph-standard-workflow.md** — 9-phase workflow (Setup → Research → Implement → Test → E2E → Review → Commit → PR → Handoff)\n- **ralph-revision-workflow.md** — 4-phase workflow (Setup → Fix & Verify → Commit → Handoff) for defect fixes\n- **devralph-standard-workflow.md** — Developer-focused variant (similar 9-phase)\n- **devralph-revision-workflow.md** — Developer defect-fix workflow (4-phase)\n\n#### Malph Review Workflow\n- **malph-review-workflow.md** — 6-phase review panel (Descend → Investigate → Verify → Review → Deliver → Handoff)\n\n#### Code Samples Integration (5 role-specific files)\n- **ralph-codesamples.md** — Full project structure, feature folders, `code_link` tags, `//Include:` markers, CI repository, codename prefixing\n- **ralph-codesamples-coder.md** — Bootstrap .NET codesamples, version setup, build verification, admin UI testing\n- **ralph-codesamples-researcher.md** — Analyze existing samples, find `code_link` usage, identify gaps, check API signatures\n- **ralph-codesamples-reviewer.md** — Verify API correctness, `code_link` accuracy, build status, namespace patterns, codename prefix (`codesamples.`)\n- **ralph-codesamples-validator.md** — Validate code sample paths, build passes, inclusion markers, namespace conventions, functional verification\n- **ralph-codesamples-writer.md** — Create/update .cs files, add `{% code_link %}` tags, manage CI objects, build & test\n\n### VS Code Extension Workflows (ralph-vscode)\n\n**Directory:** `shared/agent-includes/ralph-vscode/` (4 files)\n\n| File | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| **ralph-standard-workflow.md** | Routing to vscode-workflow skill (single entry point for full workflow) |\n| **ralph-revision-workflow.md** | Revision mode detection & routing to vscode-workflow skill |\n| **malph-review-workflow.md** | 6-phase VS Code review (Setup → Scout → Review Panel → Aggregate → Handoff → Archive) |\n| **malph-review-checklist.md** | **Detailed review checklist** for VS Code extension (70+ items): Requirements Coverage, Architecture Compliance (definition-driven patterns, TagNames enum, folder structure, grammar sync, event system, disposal), TypeScript & Code Quality, File Operations, Scope Validation, Compatibility, etc. |\n\n---\n\n## 2. MCP SERVERS\n\n**Location:** `shared/mcp-servers/` (9 servers)\n\n### Server Manifests & Tool Inventory\n\n| Server | Port | Type | Command | Tools | Required Config |\n|--------|------|------|---------|-------|-----------------|\n| **ado** | 9101 | custom | `node dist/bundle.js` | `ado_create_pull_request`, `ado_list_pull_requests`, `ado_list_pull_request_threads`, `ado_create_pull_request_thread`, `ado_reply_to_comment`, `ado_push_progress` | `ADO_PROJECT`, `ADO_REPO`; Env: `ADO_PAT` |\n| **codegraphcontext** | 9108 | npm | `cgc mcp start` | **26 tools**: `find_code`, `analyze_code_relationships`, `calculate_cyclomatic_complexity`, `find_most_complex_functions`, `find_dead_code`, `add_code_to_graph`, `add_package_to_graph`, `monitor_directory`, `list_watched_paths`, `unwatch_directory`, `list_indexed_repositories`, `get_repository_stats`, `list_jobs`, `check_job_status`, `search_registry_bundles`, `load_bundle`, `execute_cypher_query`, `visualize_graph_query` | Init: `init.sh` |\n| **discord-hitl** | 9102 | custom | `node dist/bundle.mjs` | `discord_ask` | Env: `DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN`, `DISCORD_CHANNEL_ID`; Optional: `DISCORD_TASK_CONTEXT` |\n| **jira-kentico** | 9100 | custom | `node dist/bundle.js` | `jira_add_comment`, `jira_add_attachment` | `JIRA_ISSUE_KEY`; Env: `JIRA_PAT_KENTICO_JIRA`, `JIRA_EMAIL_KENTICO_JIRA` |\n| **microsoft-docs** | 9105 | custom | `node dist/bundle.js` | `microsoft_docs_search` | (Public API, no auth required) |\n| **playwright** | 9103 | npm | `playwright-mcp` | **8 tools**: `browser_navigate`, `browser_navigate_back`, `browser_take_screenshot`, `browser_network_requests`, `browser_click`, `browser_fill_form`, `browser_evaluate`, `browser_press_key` | None |\n| **ralphchives-read** | 9107 | custom | `node dist/bundle.js` | `search_ralphchives`, `get_topic`, `list_recent_topics` | `NODEBB_API_TOKEN`, `NODEBB_CATEGORY_NAME`; Env: `NODEBB_API_URL` |\n| **ralphchives-write** | 9106 | custom | `node dist/bundle.js` | `post_task_report`, `post_observation`, `reply_to_thread` | `NODEBB_API_TOKEN`, `NODEBB_CATEGORY_NAME`; Env: `NODEBB_API_URL` |\n| **web-fetch** | 9104 | custom | `node dist/bundle.js` | `web_fetch` | None |\n\n### MCP Server Descriptions\n\n- **ado** — Azure DevOps operations: create/list PRs, manage PR threads, reply to comments, push progress updates\n- **codegraphcontext** — Code graph intelligence: indexes code into graph DB for structural queries, call chains, dead code detection, complexity analysis\n- **discord-hitl** — Human-in-the-loop via Discord: blocking questions, approvals, notifications through Discord threads\n- **jira-kentico** — JIRA Cloud: add comments and attachments to issues (Kentico JIRA instance)\n- **microsoft-docs** — Search Microsoft Learn documentation via public search API\n- **playwright** — Browser automation: navigate, screenshot, interact with web pages, evaluate JavaScript, press keys\n- **ralphchives-read** — Knowledge base read path: search topics, retrieve topic content, list recent activity (scoped by profile category)\n- **ralphchives-write** — Knowledge base write path: post task reports, observations, thread replies (NodeBB forum backend)\n- **web-fetch** — Generic HTTP: fetch content from any URL and return as text\n\n---\n\n## 3. PROFILES & AGENT CONFIGURATIONS\n\n### Ralph-Docs Profile\n\n**File:** `profiles/ralph-docs/profile.json` (228 lines)\n\n- **Repo:** `~/repositories/ralph-repositories/kentico-docs-jekyll`\n- **Data Source:** `kentico-jira` | **VCS:** `ado` | **CLI:** `copilot`\n- **Timeout:** 36 seconds | **Max Continuations:** 3\n- **Allowlist Domains:** `.aka.ms`, `.dev.azure.com`, `.artifacts.visualstudio.com`, `.blob.core.windows.net`, `.npmjs.org`, `.rubygems.org`, `.nuget.org`, `.pypi.org`, `.pythonhosted.org`\n\n#### MCP Servers Enabled\n- `jira-kentico` (JIRA_ISSUE_KEY = $task.id)\n- `ado` (ADO_PROJECT: CustomerEducation; ADO_REPO: kentico-docs-jekyll)\n- `web-fetch`, `microsoft-docs`\n- `ralphchives-write` (NODEBB_CATEGORY_NAME: ralph-docs)\n- `ralphchives-read` (NODEBB_CATEGORY_NAME: ralph-docs)\n- GitHub MCP: `get_file_contents`\n\n#### Variants (3 configurations)\n\n**Variant 1: Ralph Documentation Primary**\n- Match: projects `DOC`, `DF`; statuses `To Do`, `Defect Found`; trigger `@Ralph`\n- Before Agent: Set status → \"In Progress\" | After Agent: → \"Ready for Review\"\n- Agent: `ralph.ralph` with 15+ skills (codesamples, workflows, documentation, verification, release notes, research, build, Xperience)\n\n**Variant 2: Malph Documentation Review**\n- Match: projects `DOC`, `DF`; status `Ready for Review`; trigger `@Malph`\n- Agent: `ralph.malph` with review workflow skills\n\n**Variant 3: RalphDev Infrastructure (Ruby, Gulp, Frontend, Jekyll)**\n- Match: projects `DOC`, `DF`; statuses `To Do`, `Defect Found`; trigger `@RalphDev`\n- Agent: `ralph.stacky` with dev-specific skills (gems, pipeline, frontend, jekyll, build verification)\n\n### Ralph-VSCode Profile\n\n**File:** `profiles/ralph-vscode/profile.json` (146 lines)\n\n- **Repo:** `~/repositories/ralph-repositories/kentico-docs-autocomplete-vscode`\n- **Data Source:** `kentico-jira` | **VCS:** `ado` | **CLI:** `copilot`\n- **Timeout:** 36 seconds\n- **Allowlist Domains:** `.npmjs.org`, `dev.azure.com`, `pkgs.dev.azure.com`, `vsblob.dev.azure.com`, `.artifacts.visualstudio.com`\n\n#### MCP Servers Enabled\n- `jira-kentico` (JIRA_ISSUE_KEY = $task.id)\n- `ado` (ADO_PROJECT: CustomerEducation; ADO_REPO: kentico-docs-autocomplete-vscode)\n- `ralphchives-write` & `ralphchives-read` (NODEBB_CATEGORY_NAME: ralph-vscode)\n- GitHub MCP: `get_file_contents`\n\n#### Variants (2 configurations)\n\n**Variant 1: Ralph VS Code Development**\n- Match: project `DOC`; statuses `To Do`, `Defect Found`; trigger `@RalphAutocomplete`\n- Agent: `ralph.ralph` with 9 skills (PR workflow, ralphchives, vscode-workflow, testing, TypeScript, grammar/scopes)\n\n**Variant 2: Malph VS Code Review**\n- Match: project `DOC`; status `Ready for Review`; trigger `@MalphAutocomplete`\n- Agent: `ralph.malph` with 8 review workflow skills\n\n---\n\n## 4. HOOKS & AUDIT SYSTEM\n\n### Hook Scripts\n\n**Location:** `shared/hooks/` (6 scripts + audit config)\n\n| Hook | Event | Purpose |\n|------|-------|---------|\n| **log-session-start.sh** | `sessionStart` | Initializes session, generates SESSION_ID, records timestamp & initial prompt, creates log directory |\n| **log-prompt.sh** | `userPromptSubmitted` | Logs user prompt to audit.jsonl |\n| **log-pre-tool.sh** | `preToolUse` | Logs every tool invocation: timestamp, tool name, args to both pre-tool.log and audit.jsonl (optimized for 200-500 calls/task) |\n| **log-post-tool.sh** | `postToolUse` | Logs tool results: success/failure, LLM-visible output; writes untruncated output to readable log |\n| **log-error.sh** | `errorOccurred` | Logs error events: error name, message, stack trace |\n| **log-session-end.sh** | `sessionEnd` | Records session end: timestamp, exit reason, working directory |\n\n**Audit Config:** `shared/hooks/ralph-audit.json` (v1)\n\nDefines 6 hook event handlers:\n- `sessionStart` → `log-session-start.sh` (5 sec timeout)\n- `userPromptSubmitted` → `log-prompt.sh` (5 sec timeout)\n- `preToolUse` → `log-pre-tool.sh` (5 sec timeout)\n- `postToolUse` → `log-post-tool.sh` (5 sec timeout)\n- `errorOccurred` → `log-error.sh` (5 sec timeout)\n- `sessionEnd` → `log-session-end.sh` (5 sec timeout)\n\nOutput: `/workspace/.ralph/logs/`\n- `audit.jsonl` — timestamped audit trail (all events)\n- `pre-tool.log` — compact tool call invocations\n- `.current-session-id` — session identifier file\n\n---\n\n## 5. SUMMARY TABLE: Shared Resources Overview\n\n| Category | Count | Key Components |\n|----------|-------|-----------------|\n| **Agent Includes (Core)** | 7 files | Contract, Rules, Security, References, Ralphchives, ADO API, PR Format |\n| **Personality Profiles** | 2 files | Malph (🦇 reviewer), Ralph (🔧 builder) |\n| **Post-Task Hooks** | 4 files | Agent Improver, Run Analyzer, Run Synthesizer, Subagent Mapper |\n| **Ralph-Docs Workflows** | 14 files | 2 standard/revision workflows, 1 Malph review, 6 codesamples files |\n| **Ralph-VSCode Workflows** | 4 files | 2 standard/revision, 1 Malph review, 1 detailed checklist |\n| **MCP Servers** | 9 servers | 9101–9108 ports; ~60 total tools |\n| **Profiles** | 2 configs | ralph-docs (3 variants), ralph-vscode (2 variants) |\n| **Hook Scripts** | 6 scripts | Session, Prompt, Pre-Tool, Post-Tool, Error, Session-End; 5s each |\n\n---\n\n## 6. DATA FLOW RELATIONSHIPS\n\n```\n┌─ TASK EXECUTION ─────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                                                           │\n│  Profile (ralph-docs or ralph-vscode)                   │\n│    ├─ Selects MCP Servers & Skills                      │\n│    ├─ Triggers Agent Variant                            │\n│    └─ Configures beforeAgent/afterAgent status          │\n│                                                           │\n│  Agent (ralph.ralph or ralph.malph or ralph.stacky)     │\n│    ├─ Uses Agent Includes (rules, security, contracts)  │\n│    ├─ Applies Personality (malph.md or ralph.md)        │\n│    ├─ Calls MCP Tools (ado, jira, ralphchives, etc.)    │\n│    └─ Produces status.json + artifacts                  │\n│                                                           │\n│  POST-TASK HOOKS (Post-Execution Analysis)              │\n│    ├─ Subagent Mapper: Extract telemetry from logs      │\n│    ├─ Run Analyzer: Per-subagent quality analysis       │\n│    ├─ Agent Improver: Apply findings to templates       │\n│    └─ Run Synthesizer: Cross-subagent assessment        │\n│                                                           │\n│  AUDIT SYSTEM (Real-Time Logging)                       │\n│    ├─ Session hooks log lifecycle events                │\n│    ├─ Tool hooks log pre/post invocation                │\n│    ├─ Error hooks capture failures                      │\n│    └─ Output: audit.jsonl, pre-tool.log, session ID     │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\nThis inventory provides a complete map of Ralph-Orchestrator's shared infrastructure for agent includes, MCP servers, profiles, and audit systems.",
