              "arguments": "{\"command\": \"cat > /tmp/fractal_inventory.md << 'EOF'\\n# Ralph Orchestrator - Fractal Factory Infrastructure Inventory\\n\\n## 1. FRACTAL FACTORY AGENTS (.fractals/fractal-factory/agents/)\\n\\n28 agent files totaling 3,881 lines. These are the exemplar patterns that produced systems should learn from.\\n\\n### Core Orchestration\\n- **fractal-factory.agent.md** (136 lines)\\n  - Session orchestrator for the 7-pass pipeline\\n  - Routes between coordinators, handles re-entry from gap hunting\\n  - Pure router pattern — reads progress.json and status.json files\\n\\n### Pass 1: Discovery (4 agents)\\nCoordinators by discovery specialists to understand the domain:\\n\\n1. **fractal-factory-discovery-coordinator.agent.md** (83 lines)\\n   - Coordinates Pass 1 discovery\\n   - Dispatches 4 specialists sequentially: domain-scanner, invariant-extractor, asset-auditor, exemplar-analyzer\\n   - Pure router pattern\\n\\n2. **fractal-factory-domain-scanner.agent.md** (150 lines)\\n   - Reads domain-brief.md and domain-docs/\\n   - Produces initial domain model with subdomains\\n   - Writes to domain-model.json\\n\\n3. **fractal-factory-invariant-extractor.agent.md** (142 lines)\\n   - Extracts behavioral, structural, quality, and workflow invariants\\n   - Reads from invariants.md and domain materials\\n   - Adds extracted rules to domain-model.json with confidence scores\\n\\n4. **fractal-factory-asset-auditor.agent.md** (131 lines)\\n   - Scans workspace for reusable assets (skills, templates, MCP servers, agent includes)\\n   - Audits for relevance to produced system subdomains\\n   - Marks reusability level: direct, adaptable, reference-only\\n\\n5. **fractal-factory-exemplar-analyzer.agent.md** (153 lines)\\n   - Analyzes exemplar agent families (existing multi-agent systems in inputs.exemplars)\\n   - Extracts reusable patterns: hierarchy, naming conventions, routing idioms, artifacts\\n   - Categorizes patterns: hierarchy, naming, artifact, routing, anti-laziness, convergence\\n\\n### Pass 2: Analysis (3 agents)\\nArchitecture design specialists:\\n\\n1. **fractal-factory-analysis-coordinator.agent.md** (78 lines)\\n   - Coordinates Pass 2 analysis\\n   - Dispatches 3 specialists: pipeline-architect, artifact-designer, depth-analyzer\\n   - Pure router pattern\\n\\n2. **fractal-factory-pipeline-architect.agent.md** (182 lines)\\n   - Designs the 7-pass pipeline for produced system\\n   - Decides which passes to enable, entry/exit conditions, re-entry rules\\n   - Writes architecture.json with pass definitions and cross-cutting concerns\\n\\n3. **fractal-factory-artifact-designer.agent.md** (167 lines)\\n   - Designs shared artifact schemas (JSON schemas, read-modify-write contracts)\\n   - Maps complete data flow between agents\\n   - Identifies universal artifacts (context.json, progress.json, manifest.json, status.json)\\n   - And domain-specific artifacts based on pipeline\\n\\n4. **fractal-factory-depth-analyzer.agent.md** (152 lines)\\n   - Analyzes domain complexity per coordinator\\n   - Decides depth-2 (coordinator→specialists) or depth-3 (coordinator→sub-coordinators→specialists)\\n   - Considers subdomain count, invariant complexity, exemplar patterns\\n\\n### Pass 3: Planning (3 agents)\\nRoster and routing design specialists:\\n\\n1. **fractal-factory-planning-coordinator.agent.md** (78 lines)\\n   - Coordinates Pass 3 planning\\n   - Dispatches 3 specialists: roster-planner, routing-planner, test-planner\\n   - Pure router pattern\\n\\n2. **fractal-factory-roster-planner.agent.md** (191 lines)\\n   - Plans complete agent roster: names, levels, parents, children, result codes\\n   - Assigns agents to subdomains and artifacts\\n   - Names coordinators per pass, specialists per subdomain\\n   - Writes roster.json with initial status\\n\\n3. **fractal-factory-routing-planner.agent.md** (158 lines)\\n   - Designs routing tables for every coordinator and orchestrator\\n   - Maps result codes to next actions, defines re-entry rules\\n   - Sets convergence bounds based on maxGapCycles, maxWriterReviewerRetries\\n   - Writes to roster.json routing section\\n\\n4. **fractal-factory-test-planner.agent.md** (159 lines)\\n   - Creates golden test scenarios covering agent types, edge cases, re-entry paths\\n   - Designs verification test scenarios from domain invariants\\n   - Writes test-plan.json with structured test cases\\n\\n### Pass 4: Execution (3 agents)\\nPrompt and infrastructure writers:\\n\\n1. **fractal-factory-execution-coordinator.agent.md** (103 lines)\\n   - Coordinates Pass 4 execution\\n   - Runs prompt-writer → prompt-reviewer loop with retries\\n   - Dispatches infra-writer after loop completes\\n   - Pure router, tracks retry counts\\n\\n2. **fractal-factory-prompt-writer.agent.md** (209 lines) ⭐ LARGEST SPECIALIST\\n   - Writes .agent.md prompt files for every agent in produced system\\n   - Follows universal agent prompt template\\n   - Uses roster, architecture, domain-model, and test-plan as specifications\\n   - Writes to produced-output/agents/\\n\\n3. **fractal-factory-prompt-reviewer.agent.md** (157 lines)\\n   - Reviews every .agent.md for structural compliance and content quality\\n   - Validates routing completeness and anti-laziness enforcement\\n   - Approves or rejects with specific feedback\\n   - Implements retry loop with prompt-writer\\n\\n4. **fractal-factory-infra-writer.agent.md** (129 lines)\\n   - Writes non-prompt infrastructure: bootstrap script, artifact schemas, skill stubs, test files\\n   - Generates schema documentation from architecture.json\\n   - Writes produced-output/bootstrap.sh, produced-output/schemas/, produced-output/skills/, produced-output/tests/\\n\\n### Pass 5: Verification (2 agents)\\n\\n1. **fractal-factory-verification-coordinator.agent.md** (78 lines)\\n   - Coordinates Pass 5 verification\\n   - Dispatches checklist-validator and audit-oracle\\n   - Pure router pattern\\n\\n2. **fractal-factory-checklist-validator.agent.md** (184 lines)\\n   - Exhaustively validates every produced agent against structural/behavioral checklist\\n   - Ground-truth checks: agent files match roster, references match architecture, invariants are enforceable\\n   - Writes verification-report.json with detailed validation results\\n\\n3. **fractal-factory-audit-oracle.agent.md** (177 lines)\\n   - Independent oracle audit of produced system\\n   - Validates architectural consistency, gap coverage, anti-laziness patterns\\n   - Writes audit-report.json with findings\\n\\n### Pass 6: Gap Hunting (1 agent + coordinator)\\n\\n1. **fractal-factory-gap-hunting-coordinator.agent.md** (73 lines)\\n   - Coordinates Pass 6 gap hunting\\n   - Dispatches gap-hunter\\n   - Reports convergence or dirty state to orchestrator\\n   - Pure router, tracks cycle count\\n\\n2. **fractal-factory-gap-hunter.agent.md** (203 lines) ⭐ LARGEST COORDINATOR CHILD\\n   - Hunts for gaps: missing coverage, orphaned references, incomplete patterns\\n   - Searches 8 categories: coverage gaps, broken references, pattern incompleteness, edge cases, invariant violations, anti-laziness violations, artifact issues, orchestration issues\\n   - Reports clean (converged) or dirty (needs re-entry)\\n   - Writes gap-report.json with findings\\n\\n### Pass 7: Delivery (3 agents)\\n\\n1. **fractal-factory-delivery-coordinator.agent.md** (79 lines)\\n   - Coordinates Pass 7 delivery\\n   - Dispatches packager, documentation-writer, report-writer sequentially\\n   - Pure router pattern\\n\\n2. **fractal-factory-packager.agent.md** (137 lines)\\n   - Packages produced artifacts into target output directory\\n   - Validates completeness against roster and architecture checklists\\n   - Produces packaging-report.json\\n\\n3. **fractal-factory-documentation-writer.agent.md** (125 lines)\\n   - Writes architecture guide, user guide, and roster reference\\n   - Uses domain-model, architecture, test-plan as inputs\\n   - Writes produced-output/docs/\\n\\n4. **fractal-factory-report-writer.agent.md** (155 lines)\\n   - Produces final delivery report: coverage statistics, quality metrics, outstanding items\\n   - Reads manifest.json (audit trail) and all progress artifacts\\n   - Writes final-report.json\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. FRACTAL FACTORY SHARED INFRASTRUCTURE\\n\\n### Bootstrap Script\\n- **fractal-factory-bootstrap.sh** (creates .fractal-factory/ artifact directory structure)\\n  - Creates progress.json with 7-pass pipeline state\\n  - Creates manifest.json (empty audit log)\\n  - Creates agent/ subdirectories for session orchestrator and all coordinators\\n  - Creates produced-output/ with agents/, schemas/, skills/, tests/, docs/ subdirectories\\n\\n### Configuration Schemas (4 files in .fractals/fractal-factory/schemas/)\\n\\n1. **context.schema.md** (50+ lines)\\n   - User-provided configuration for fractal factory run\\n   - Fields: version, domain (name, description), target (outputDirectory, namingPrefix), inputs (domainBrief, domainDocs, exemplars, invariants, constraints), options (maxDepth, maxAgents, maxGapCycles, maxWriterReviewerRetries, pipelinePasses)\\n\\n2. **domain-model.schema.md** (60+ lines)\\n   - Shared artifact populated by discovery specialists (Pass 1)\\n   - Sections: subdomains (id, name, description, complexity, estimatedAgentCount), invariants (classification, confidence, verificationStrategy), existingAssets (type, reusability, relevantSubdomains), exemplarPatterns (category, applicability)\\n\\n3. **progress.schema.md**\\n   - Tracks pipeline state across 7-pass execution\\n   - Owned exclusively by session orchestrator\\n   - Sections: currentPass, passes (per-pass status and agent counts), gapHunting (cycle tracking, convergence flag)\\n\\n4. **produced-agent.schema.md**\\n   - Structural requirements for every .agent.md file\\n   - Follows universal agent prompt template\\n   - Validates by prompt-reviewer and checklist-validator\\n\\n### README\\n- **fractal-factory/README.md** (50 lines shown)\\n  - Quick start guide (bootstrap, fill context, prepare inputs, invoke guide)\\n  - Architecture overview (user → guide → orchestrator → 7 coordinators → 16 specialists)\\n  - Describes 7-pass pipeline structure\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. SOURCE CODE ARCHITECTURE (src/)\\n\\n### Core Orchestrator\\n- **orchestrator.ts** (18,574 bytes)\\n  - Main Ralph orchestrator implementation\\n  - Polls JIRA, triggers agents, manages task lifecycle\\n\\n### Services Layer (16 files)\\n**Location**: src/services/\\n\\n| Service | Purpose |\\n|---------|---------|\\n| **activity-log.ts** | Logs agent/task activity for audit trail |\\n| **agent-pipeline-executor.ts** | Executes prompt-writer→reviewer loops |\\n| **dashboard-server.ts** | Serves INK dashboard to CLI |\\n| **heartbeat.ts** | Sends heartbeat to JIRA Cloud |\\n| **issue-manager.ts** | JIRA issue lifecycle management |\\n| **operation-ledger.ts** | Tracks operations and state transitions (13KB) |\\n| **orchestrator-comments.ts** | Posts status updates to JIRA comments |\\n| **preflight.ts** | Pre-execution validation |\\n| **profile-router.ts** | Routes to Claude Copilot or Copilot CLI |\\n| **profile-setup-service.ts** | Sets up execution profiles |\\n| **task-context.ts** | Builds task execution context |\\n| **task-resource-manager.ts** | Manages task docker containers, resource limits |\\n| **task-result-writer.ts** | Writes task results back to JIRA |\\n| **task-runner.ts** | Main task execution loop (12KB) |\\n| **trigger-scanner.ts** | Scans JIRA for trigger keywords (10KB) |\\n| **vcs-source-client.ts** | Git/VCS source operations (5.7KB) |\\n\\n### Container Management (12 files)\\n**Location**: src/container/\\n\\n| Module | Purpose |\\n|--------|---------|\\n| **agent-session-runner.ts** | Runs agents in isolated sessions |\\n| **cli-executor-factory.ts** | Factory for CLI executors (Copilot/Claude) |\\n| **compose-client.ts** | Docker Compose orchestration |\\n| **continuation-runner.ts** | Handles multi-turn agent sessions |\\n| **lifecycle.ts** | Container lifecycle management |\\n| **log-collector.ts** | Collects logs from containers |\\n| **log-source-registry.ts** | Registry for log sources |\\n| **manager.ts** | Container manager |\\n| **result-parser.ts** | Parses agent output |\\n| **stream-capture.ts** | Captures container streams |\\n| **types.ts** | Container type definitions |\\n| **workspace-cleaner.ts** | Cleans up workspace after execution |\\n\\n**Subdirectories**:\\n- **cli-executors/** — CLI-specific executors\\n- **setup/** — Container setup routines\\n\\n### Data Source/Connectors (2 levels)\\n**Location**: src/datasource/\\n\\n- **connectors/jira/** — JIRA API integration\\n  - JIRA Cloud client for polling, issue management\\n\\n### Configuration\\n**Location**: src/config/\\n\\n- Configuration management for orchestrator\\n\\n### UI/Dashboard\\n**Location**: src/cli-dashboard/\\n\\n- INK-based CLI dashboard (React terminal UI)\\n- Shows status, queue, history, logs\\n\\n### Prompt & Templating\\n**Location**: src/prompt/\\n\\n- Agent prompt templates\\n- Template rendering\\n\\n### Utilities & Validation\\n**Locations**:\\n- **src/util/** — Utility functions\\n- **src/validate/** — Input/output validation (Zod schemas)\\n\\n### Log Management\\n**Location**: src/logs/\\n\\n- Log aggregation and storage\\n\\n### Core Files\\n- **app-startup.ts** (4.8KB) — Application startup\\n- **awilix-cradle.ts** (8.9KB) — Dependency injection container setup\\n- **awilix-cradle-types.ts** (3.7KB) — DI container type definitions\\n- **orchestrator-types.ts** (3.1KB) — Type definitions\\n- **index.tsx** (2.1KB) — Entry point\\n- **logger.ts** — Logging setup\\n- **retry.ts** (1.3KB) — Retry logic\\n- **orchestrator-observer.ts** (3.8KB) — Event observation\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. SCRIPTS (scripts/)\\n\\n| Script | Purpose |\\n|--------|---------|\\n| **audit-log-hierarchy.py** | Python audit for log hierarchy |\\n| **audit-parallel-and-tokens.py** | Audit parallel execution and token usage |\\n| **audit-parallel-deep.py** | Deep parallel execution audit |\\n| **audit-verify-fix.py** | Verify fixes |\\n| **lookup-users.ts** | Look up JIRA users |\\n| **reset-issue.ts** | Reset test environment (5.9KB) |\\n| **reset-testenv/** | Test environment reset helpers |\\n| **run-agent.ts** | Run individual agents (5.9KB) |\\n| **run-hooks.ts** | Run lifecycle hooks (6.6KB) |\\n| **validate.ts** | Validation script (202 bytes) |\\n| **visualize-agent-graph.ts** | Visualize agent dependency graph (23KB) |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. SHARED INFRASTRUCTURE\\n\\n### Skills (src/shared/skills/)\\nDomain-specific and workflow skills:\\n- **domain/** — Domain-specific skills\\n- **integrations/** — Integration skills (JIRA, ADO, etc)\\n- **tasks/** — Task management skills\\n- **workflow/** — Workflow automation skills\\n- **xperience/** — Experience/documentation skills\\n- **xperience-documentation/** — Documentation generation skills\\n\\n### Agent Includes (src/shared/agent-includes/)\\nReusable Liquid partials for agents:\\n- **ado-api.md** — ADO API interface\\n- **ado-pr-format.md** — ADO PR formatting\\n- **agent-as-function-contract.md** — Agent-as-function pattern\\n- **personality/** — Agent personality templates\\n- **post-hooks/** — Post-execution hooks\\n- **prompt-security.md** — Security patterns\\n- **ralph-docs/** — Ralph documentation\\n- **ralph-vscode/** — VSCode integration\\n- **ralphchives.md** — NodeBB archive references\\n- **rules.md** — Common rules/patterns\\n- **source-references.md** — Source reference patterns\\n\\n### MCP Servers (src/shared/mcp-servers/)\\nModel Context Protocol server integrations:\\n- **ado/** — Azure DevOps\\n- **codegraphcontext/** — Code graph context\\n- **discord-hitl/** — Discord human-in-the-loop\\n- **jira-kentico/** — JIRA and Kentico integration\\n- **microsoft-docs/** — Microsoft documentation\\n- **playwright/** — Browser automation\\n- **ralphchives-read/** — NodeBB archive read\\n- **ralphchives-write/** — NodeBB archive write\\n- **web-fetch/** — Web fetching\\n\\n### MCP Sidecar\\n**Location**: src/shared/mcp-sidecar/\\n\\n- Gateway for MCP tool registration\\n- Runs isolated from main orchestrator\\n\\n### Security\\n**Location**: src/shared/security/\\n\\n- Security policies and validation\\n\\n### Hooks\\n**Location**: src/shared/hooks/\\n\\n- Lifecycle hooks (pre-execution, post-execution)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. ARCHITECTURE DOCUMENTATION\\n\\n### Root-Level Architecture Docs\\n\\n| File | Purpose | Lines |\\n|------|---------|-------|\\n| **ARCHITECTURE.md** | Ralph orchestrator system architecture (36KB) | 50+ |\\n| **AGENT-AS-FUNCTION.md** | Subagent-as-function pattern with filesystem artifact handoff (12KB) | 50+ |\\n| **CLAUDE.md** | Guidance for Claude Code (15KB) | 30 |\\n| **CONFIGURATION.md** | Configuration guide (31KB) | N/A |\\n| **MCP.md** | MCP servers and tools (17KB) | N/A |\\n| **SECURITY.md** | Security hardening (17KB) | N/A |\\n| **AUTH-PRISMA.md** | Authentication and Prisma integration (21KB) | N/A |\\n| **CODEGRAPH-STRATEGY.md** | CodeGraph context strategy (7KB) | N/A |\\n| **DEPENDENCY-INJECTION.md** | DI container design (3.3KB) | N/A |\\n| **TEMPLATE-INSPECTOR.md** | Template inspection (1.2KB) | N/A |\\n| **README.md** | Project overview (11KB) | N/A |\\n| **copilot-cli-internals.md** | Copilot CLI internals (15KB) | N/A |\\n| **refactoring-instr.md** | Refactoring instructions (5KB) | N/A |\\n\\n### Documentation Directory (docs/)\\n\\n#### User Guide (docs/user-guide/)\\n- **README.md** — User guide index\\n- **configuration.md** — Configuration guide\\n- **environment-variables.md** — Env var reference\\n- **profiles.md** — Execution profiles\\n- **runtime-macros.md** — Runtime macro reference\\n- **skills.md** — Skills system\\n- **template-variables.md** — Template variable reference\\n- **trigger-parameters.md** — Trigger parameter reference\\n- **mcp-servers.md** — MCP server reference\\n- **deploying-mcp-servers.md** — MCP deployment guide\\n- **codegraphcontext.md** — CodeGraph context setup\\n\\n#### Developer Documentation (docs/dev-doc/)\\n- **agent-templates.md** — Agent template patterns\\n- **compose-layering.md** — Docker Compose layering\\n- **cradle-refac.md** — DI container refactoring\\n- **data-source-registration.md** — Data source registration\\n- **local-testing.md** — Local testing guide\\n- **mcp-sidecar-design.md** — MCP sidecar architecture\\n- **mcp-tool-naming.md** — Tool naming conventions\\n- **multistage-pipelines.md** — Multi-stage pipeline design\\n- **prompt-injection-hardening.md** — Security hardening\\n- **ralphchives.md** — Archive integration\\n\\n#### Past Issues (docs/past-issues/)\\n- **001-ado-server-crash-session-loss.md** — Incident notes\\n\\n#### Research (docs/research/)\\n- **oh-my-opencode-analysis.md** — Analysis of OpenCode patterns\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. EXISTING FACTORY OUTPUT / PRODUCED SYSTEMS\\n\\n### Configuration State\\n**Location**: .fractal-factory/\\n\\n| File | Contents |\\n|------|----------|\\n| **context.json** | Current run configuration: domain name (fantasy-writer), target output (.fractal-factory/output/romantic-fantasy-writer), naming prefix (romantic-fantasy-writer), input paths (domain-brief.md, invariants.md, exemplars pointing to .fractals/fractal-factory/agents) |\\n| **progress.json** | 7-pass pipeline state: currently on Pass 1 (discovery active), tracks completed agents per pass, gap-hunting cycle count (0/3, not converged yet) |\\n| **domain-brief.md** | 32KB narrative description of the romantic fantasy writer domain |\\n| **invariants.md** | 18KB behavioral rules and constraints for produced system |\\n| **domain-model.json** | 67KB result of discovery pass — subdomains, invariants with confidence scores, existing assets, exemplar patterns extracted |\\n| **roster.json** | Currently minimal (82 bytes) — will be populated by roster-planner |\\n| **architecture.json** | Currently minimal (100 bytes) — will be populated by pipeline-architect |\\n| **test-plan.json** | Currently minimal (61 bytes) — will be populated by test-planner |\\n| **manifest.json** | Audit log with 568 bytes — tracks agent dispatch history |\\n\\n### Produced Output Structure\\n**Location**: .fractal-factory/produced-output/\\n\\n- **agents/** — Will contain .agent.md files for romantic-fantasy-writer agents\\n- **schemas/** — Will contain JSON schema documentation\\n- **skills/** — Will contain skill stub directories\\n- **tests/** — Will contain golden test scenario files\\n- **docs/** — Will contain architecture guide, user guide, roster reference\\n\\n### Current Status\\nThe factory is in the middle of a production run for the \\\"romantic-fantasy-writer\\\" domain:\\n- Pass 1 (Discovery) is currently active\\n- Configured for maxDepth=4, maxAgents=80, maxGapCycles=10, maxWriterReviewerRetries=10\\n- All 7 passes enabled: discovery, analysis, planning, execution, verification, gapHunting, delivery\\n- Has analyzed exemplars from .fractals/fractal-factory/agents (itself as exemplar!)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. PATTERN SUMMARY\\n\\n### Core Patterns Exemplified\\n\\n#### 1. **Purity Rule (Pure Router Pattern)**\\nUsed by all coordinators and the session orchestrator. Key principle:\\n- Read status.json from children\\n- Dispatch children by invoking them\\n- Update own status.json\\n- Prepend to manifest.json\\n- **Never do substantive work yourself** — that's a specialist's job\\n\\n#### 2. **Agent-as-Function with Filesystem Artifact Handoff**\\nData flows horizontally between specialists via the filesystem, not through orchestrator:\\n- Orchestrator reads only status.json at each step\\n- Specialists write artifacts to their subdirectories\\n- Downstream specialists read upstream artifacts directly\\n- Prevents context window bloat and maintains specialist independence\\n\\n#### 3. **Universal Agent Prompt Template**\\nEvery produced agent follows the same structure:\\n- YAML frontmatter (name, description, model)\\n- Overview section\\n- Context section (what to read from .fractal-factory/)\\n- Inputs section (what files to process)\\n- Process section (step-by-step algorithm)\\n- Write Rules section (what to produce)\\n- Anti-Laziness Rules section (quality gates)\\n\\n#### 4. **Anti-Laziness Enforcement**\\nSpecialists and reviewers actively prevent shortcuts:\\n- Prompt-reviewer validates every agent prompt for completeness\\n- Checklist-validator exhaustively validates produced artifacts\\n- Audit-oracle conducts independent verification\\n- Gap-hunter adversarially searches for missed coverage\\n\\n#### 5. **Convergence via Gap Hunting**\\nIterative refinement until stability:\\n- Gap-hunter searches 8 categories for issues\\n- Reports clean (converged) or dirty (needs re-entry)\\n- Orchestrator can re-run earlier passes if dirty\\n- Bounded by maxGapCycles to prevent infinite loops\\n\\n#### 6. **Specialist Classification**\\nAgents organized into categories with clear responsibilities:\\n- **Coordinators**: pure routers, one per pass\\n- **Discovery Specialists**: understand the domain\\n- **Planning Specialists**: design the system\\n- **Execution Specialists**: produce artifacts\\n- **Verification Specialists**: validate quality\\n\\n#### 7. **Routing Tables**\\nEvery coordinator and orchestrator has a routing table mapping:\\n- Input (which child's status.json)\\n- Condition (what the status indicates)\\n- Action (dispatch which specialist, or what decision)\\n\\n#### 8. **Result Codes and Status.json**\\nStructured communication between agents:\\n- Each agent writes status.json with result codes\\n- Parent reads status.json to decide next action\\n- Prevents parsing unstructured output\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Key Statistics\\n\\n- **28 agent files** totaling **3,881 lines**\\n- **1 session orchestrator** routing the 7-pass pipeline\\n- **7 coordinators** (one per pass, pure routers)\\n- **16+ specialists** implementing actual work\\n- **4 schemas** defining the artifact format\\n- **16 services** in the orchestrator codebase\\n- **6 shared infrastructure** directories (skills, MCP, includes, sidecar, security, hooks)\\n- **13 root-level documentation** files\\n- **23 docs/** subdirectory files\\n- **12+ scripts** for automation and debugging\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Next Steps for Production\\n\\nThe romantic-fantasy-writer domain production is currently active. Once complete, it will demonstrate:\\n1. A fully-specified romance/fantasy fiction generation system\\n2. Multi-agent hierarchy with up to depth-4 nesting\\n3. Up to 80 agents organized by the fractal factory\\n4. Complete artifact schemas, routing tables, test plans\\n5. Documentation, bootstrap script, and golden tests\\n6. All patterns and exemplars from the fractal factory itself\\n\\nThis produced system then becomes an exemplar that can be studied and reused for similar domains.\\nEOF\\ncat /tmp/fractal_inventory.md\\n\", \"description\": \"Create comprehensive inventory report\"}"
            }
