ification | integrations/ | Testing | Functional verification using playwright-cli for ASP.NET Core codesamples application |\n| 4 | ralph-ralphchives | integrations/ | Knowledge Base | Persistent knowledge base access: search prior work, post observations, record task reports |\n| 5 | ralph-screenshots | integrations/ | Visual Documentation | Capture clean admin UI screenshots with playwright-cli, highlight elements, attach to JIRA |\n| 6 | ralph-source-references | integrations/ | Code Reference | URL formatting for citing Xperience source code in JIRA with navigable browser links |\n\n---\n\n### **TASK SKILLS (6 skills)**\nHigh-level task execution and project workflows:\n\n| # | Name | Path | Domain | Description |\n|---|------|------|--------|-------------|\n| 1 | ralph-codesamples | tasks/ | Code Samples | .NET project structure, feature folders, code_link integration, build workflow |\n| 2 | ralph-codesamples-adminui | tasks/ | UI Testing | Playwright automation for admin UI: creating promotions, taxonomies, shipping, orders |\n| 3 | ralph-codesamples-bootstrap | tasks/ | Project Setup | Bootstrap codesamples project: version install, NuGet restore, database, CI, verification |\n| 4 | ralph-task-planning | tasks/ | Planning | Convert research/feedback into ordered, headless task files for writers |\n| 5 | ralph-training-modules | tasks/ | Learning Content | YAML schema for training modules and learning paths with persona and sequence support |\n| 6 | ralph-write-release-notes | tasks/ | Documentation | User-focused release notes: capabilities, structure, categorization, examples |\n\n---\n\n### **DOCUMENTATION WORKFLOW SKILLS (8 skills)**\nPhase-based orchestration for the Ralph documentation workflow:\n\n| Phase | Name | Description |\n|-------|------|-------------|\n| Router | ralph-workflow | Entry point routing to standard (8 phases) or revision (7 phases) workflows |\n| Phase 1 | 1-setup.md | Branch setup, scratchpad creation, ralphchives search (referenced by ralph-workflow) |\n| Phase 2 | 2-research.md | Dispatch ralph-researcher → ralph-planner for implementation plan |\n| Phase 3 | 3-write.md | Dispatch ralph-writer per active task from tasks.json |\n| Phase 4-5 | 4-review.md | Review, revise if needed, advance to next task |\n| Phase 6 | 6-commit.md | Pre-commit checks, commit, push |\n| Phase 7 | 7-pr.md | Create ADO pull request |\n| Phase 8 | 8-handoff.md | Dispatch ralph-scribe, deliver to JIRA, print exit block |\n\n**Revision workflow (7 phases):** r1-setup → r3-fix → 4-review → r5-commit → r6-handoff\n\n---\n\n### **FULLSTACK DEVELOPMENT WORKFLOW SKILLS (Stacky)**\nPhase-based orchestration for fullstack (backend) development:\n\n| Workflow | Name | Description |\n|----------|------|-------------|\n| Router | devralph-workflow | Routes to standard (9 phases) or revision (4 phases) Stacky workflow |\n| Std 1 | 1-setup.md | Branch, scratchpad, component identification |\n| Std 2 | 2-research.md | Dispatch stacky-analyst for implementation plan |\n| Std 3 | 3-implement.md | Dispatch stacky-coder for changes and build validation |\n| Std 4 | 4-test.md | Write unit/integration tests (stacky-test-writer) |\n| Std 5 | 5-e2e.md | Write Playwright E2E tests for UI changes |\n| Std 6 | 6-review.md | Code review gate (stacky-reviewer + stacky-bug-auditor) |\n| Std 7 | 7-commit.md | Pre-commit, commit, push |\n| Std 8 | 8-pr.md | Create ADO PR |\n| Std 9 | 9-handoff.md | Write handoff, report to JIRA, exit |\n| Rev 1 | r1-setup.md | Review previous handoff, extract defects, plan fixes |\n| Rev 2 | r2-fix.md | Dispatch stacky-coder for fixes, verification |\n| Rev 3 | r3-commit.md | Commit with fix(TASKID) prefix, push |\n| Rev 4 | r4-handoff.md | Update handoff, report, exit |\n\n---\n\n### **DOCUMENTATION REVIEW WORKFLOW SKILLS — Malph (8 phases)**\nReview orchestrator for documentation PRs:\n\n| Phase | Name | Description |\n|-------|------|-------------|\n| Router | malph-workflow-* (6 phases) | Routes to phase-