rtifact, routing, anti-laziness, convergence\\n\\n### Pass 2: Analysis (3 agents)\\nArchitecture design specialists:\\n\\n1. **fractal-factory-analysis-coordinator.agent.md** (78 lines)\\n   - Coordinates Pass 2 analysis\\n   - Dispatches 3 specialists: pipeline-architect, artifact-designer, depth-analyzer\\n   - Pure router pattern\\n\\n2. **fractal-factory-pipeline-architect.agent.md** (182 lines)\\n   - Designs the 7-pass pipeline for produced system\\n   - Decides which passes to enable, entry/exit conditions, re-entry rules\\n   - Writes architecture.json with pass definitions and cross-cutting concerns\\n\\n3. **fractal-factory-artifact-designer.agent.md** (167 lines)\\n   - Designs shared artifact schemas (JSON schemas, read-modify-write contracts)\\n   - Maps complete data flow between agents\\n   - Identifies universal artifacts (context.json, progress.json, manifest.json, status.json)\\n   - And domain-specific artifacts based on pipeline\\n\\n4. **fractal-factory-depth-analyzer.agent.md** (152 lines)\\n   - Analyzes domain complexity per coordinator\\n   - Decides depth-2 (coordinator→specialists) or depth-3 (coordinator→sub-coordinators→specialists)\\n   - Considers subdomain count, invariant complexity, exemplar patterns\\n\\n### Pass 3: Planning (3 agents)\\nRoster and routing design specialists:\\n\\n1. **fractal-factory-planning-coordinator.agent.md** (78 lines)\\n   - Coordinates Pass 3 planning\\n   - Dispatches 3 specialists: roster-planner, routing-planner, test-planner\\n   - Pure router pattern\\n\\n2. **fractal-factory-roster-planner.agent.md** (191 lines)\\n   - Plans complete agent roster: names, levels, parents, children, result codes\\n   - Assigns agents to subdomains and artifacts\\n   - Names coordinators per pass, specialists per subdomain\\n   - Writes roster.json with initial status\\n\\n3. **fractal-factory-routing-planner.agent.md** (158 lines)\\n   - Designs routing tables for every coordinator and orchestrator\\n   - Maps result 