        "role": "assistant",
        "content": "Perfect! Now let me create a concise summary document for you:\n\n---\n\n# **COMPREHENSIVE INVENTORY: Ralph Orchestrator Fractal Factory Infrastructure**\n\n## **Executive Summary**\n\nThe Ralph Orchestrator repository contains a **meta-level fractal orchestrator** that produces validated fractal agent families. The system consists of:\n\n- **28 exemplar agent files** (3,881 lines) implementing a 7-pass production pipeline\n- **16+ service modules** managing task orchestration, Docker containers, and JIRA integration\n- **6 shared infrastructure directories** (skills, MCP servers, agent includes, security, hooks)\n- **1 active production run** for the \"romantic-fantasy-writer\" domain (Pass 1 currently active)\n\n---\n\n## **1. FRACTAL FACTORY AGENTS** (28 files, organized by pipeline pass)\n\n### **Orchestration Backbone**\n- **fractal-factory.agent.md** (136L) — Session orchestrator routing 7-pass pipeline\n\n### **Pass 1: Discovery (4 agents, 1 coordinator)**\n1. **discovery-coordinator.agent.md** — Routes discovery specialists\n2. **domain-scanner.agent.md** (150L) — Scans domain-brief.md → produces subdomains\n3. **invariant-extractor.agent.md** (142L) — Extracts behavioral rules → confidence-scored invariants\n4. **asset-auditor.agent.md** (131L) — Audits existing skills/MCP/templates for reuse\n5. **exemplar-analyzer.agent.md** (153L) — Extracts patterns from exemplar agent families\n\n### **Pass 2: Analysis (3 agents, 1 coordinator)**\n1. **analysis-coordinator.agent.md** — Routes analysis specialists\n2. **pipeline-architect.agent.md** (182L) — Designs which of 7 passes to enable, entry/exit conditions\n3. **artifact-designer.agent.md** (167L) — Designs artifact schemas, data flow, read-modify-write contracts\n4. **depth-analyzer.agent.md** (152L) — Decides depth-2 vs depth-3 hierarchy per coordinator\n\n### **Pass 3: Planning (3 agents, 1 coordinator)**\n1. **planning-coordinator.agent.md** — Routes planning specialists\n2. **roster-planner.agent.md** (191L) — Names all agents, assigns to subdomains/artifacts\n3. **routing-planner.agent.md** (158L) — Designs routing tables (result code → next action)\n4. **test-planner.agent.md** (159L) — Creates golden test scenarios for verification\n\n### **Pass 4: Execution (3 agents, 1 coordinator)** \n1. **execution-coordinator.agent.md** — Routes execution specialists, manages retry loop\n2. **prompt-writer.agent.md** (209L) ⭐ **LARGEST** — Writes .agent.md files for all produced agents\n3. **prompt-reviewer.agent.md** (157L) — Validates prompts, enforces anti-laziness, manages retry\n4. **infra-writer.agent.md** (129L) — Writes bootstrap script, schemas, skill stubs, test files\n\n### **Pass 5: Verification (2 agents, 1 coordinator)**\n1. **verification-coordinator.agent.md** — Routes verification specialists\n2. **checklist-validator.agent.md** (184L) — Exhaustively validates against structural/behavioral checklist\n3. **audit-oracle.agent.md** (177L) — Independent oracle audit of architecture consistency\n\n### **Pass 6: Gap Hunting (1 agent, 1 coordinator)**\n1. **gap-hunting-coordinator.agent.md** — Routes gap hunter\n2. **gap-hunter.agent.md** (203L) ⭐ **2ND LARGEST** — Hunts 8 categories of gaps, reports convergence or dirty state\n\n### **Pass 7: Delivery (3 agents, 1 coordinator)**\n1. **delivery-coordinator.agent.md** — Routes delivery specialists\n2. **packager.agent.md** (137L) — Packages artifacts to target output directory\n3. **documentation-writer.agent.md** (125L) — Writes architecture/user guide/roster reference\n4. **report-writer.agent.md** (155L) — Produces final delivery report with metrics\n\n---\n\n## **2. FRACTAL FACTORY SHARED INFRASTRUCTURE**\n\n### **Artifact Directory Structure** (bootstrap script creates this)\n```\n.fractal-factory/\n├── progress.json          # Pipeline state (orchestrator-owned)\n├── manifest.json          # Audit trail (agent dispatch history)\n├── context.json           # User configuration\n├── domain-model.json      # Discovered domain structure\n├── roster.json            # Planned agent roster\n├── architecture.json      # Pipeline & artifact design\n├── test-plan.json         # Golden test scenarios\n├── agents/                # Agent subdirectories\n└── produced-output/       # Output location\n    ├── agents/            # .agent.md files\n    ├── schemas/           # Artifact JSON schemas\n    ├── skills/            # Skill stubs\n    ├── tests/             # Test fixture files\n    └── docs/              # Documentation\n```\n\n### **Configuration Schemas** (4 files in `.fractals/fractal-factory/schemas/`)\n1. **context.schema.md** — User config (domain, target, inputs, options)\n2. **domain-model.schema.md** — Discovery results (subdomains, invariants, assets, patterns)\n3. **progress.schema.md** — Pipeline state tracking\n4. **produced-agent.schema.md** — Universal agent prompt template requirements\n\n### **Bootstrap Script**\n- **fractal-factory-bootstrap.sh** — Initializes `.fractal-factory/` directory structure with seeded progress.json\n\n---\n\n## **3. SOURCE CODE ARCHITECTURE** (Node.js/TypeScript)\n\n### **Core Entry Points**\n- **orchestrator.ts** (18.5KB) — Main orchestrator polling JIRA and dispatching tasks\n- **app-startup.ts** — Application initialization\n- **index.tsx** — Ink terminal UI entry point\n\n### **Services Layer** (16 files, `src/services/`)\n| Service | Role |\n|---------|------|\n| **task-runner.ts** (12KB) | Main execution loop |\n| **operation-ledger.ts** (13KB) | State transitions tracking |\n| **trigger-scanner.ts** (10KB) | JIRA trigger detection |\n| **issue-manager.ts** | JIRA issue lifecycle |\n| **agent-pipeline-executor.ts** | Prompt writer→reviewer loops |\n| **task-resource-manager.ts** | Docker/resource management |\n| **profile-router.ts** | Claude vs Copilot CLI routing |\n| **vcs-source-client.ts** (5.7KB) | Git operations |\n| **preflight.ts** | Pre-execution validation |\n| **heartbeat.ts** | JIRA Cloud heartbeat |\n| **orchestrator-comments.ts** | Status posting to JIRA |\n| **activity-log.ts** | Audit trail logging |\n| **dashboard-server.ts** | INK dashboard serving |\n| **task-context.ts** | Task execution context |\n| **task-result-writer.ts** | Result writing |\n| **profile-setup-service.ts** | Profile initialization |\n\n### **Container Management** (12 files, `src/container/`)\n- **agent-session-runner.ts** — Isolated agent session execution\n- **compose-client.ts** — Docker Compose orchestration\n- **cli-executor-factory.ts** — CLI executor factory (Copilot/Claude)\n- **lifecycle.ts** — Container startup/shutdown\n- **log-collector.ts** — Log aggregation from containers\n- **result-parser.ts** — Output parsing\n- **workspace-cleaner.ts** — Cleanup on completion\n- Plus: continuation-runner, manager, stream-capture, types, and subdirs (cli-executors/, setup/)\n\n### **Data Sources** (`src/datasource/`)\n- **connectors/jira/** — JIRA Cloud API integration\n\n### **Other Core Modules**\n- **src/config/** — Configuration management\n- **src/prompt/** — Agent prompt templates\n- **src/cli-dashboard/** — INK-based terminal UI (React)\n- **src/validate/** — Zod validation schemas\n- **src/util/** — Utilities\n- **src/logs/** — Log aggregation\n\n### **Dependency Injection**\n- **awilix-cradle.ts** (8.9KB) — DI container setup\n- **awilix-cradle-types.ts** (3.7KB) — Type definitions\n\n---\n\n## **4. SHARED INFRASTRUCTURE DIRECTORIES**\n\n### **Skills** (`src/shared/skills/`)\n- **domain/** — Domain-specific agent skills\n- **integrations/** — JIRA, ADO, external integrations\n- **tasks/** — Task management utilities\n- **workflow/** — Workflow automation\n- **xperience/** — Experience/documentation generation\n- **xperience-documentation/** — Doc-specific skills\n\n### **Agent Includes** (`src/shared/agent-includes/`)\nReusable Liquid template partials:\n- ado-api.md, ado-pr-format.md, agent-as-function-contract.md\n- personality/, post-hooks/, prompt-security.md\n- ralph-docs/, ralph-vscode/, ralphchives.md\n- rules.md, source-references.md\n\n### **MCP Servers** (`src/shared/mcp-servers/`)\n- **ado/** — Azure DevOps integration\n- **jira-kentico/** — JIRA & Kentico\n- **codegraphcontext/** — Code context\n- **playwright/** — Browser automation\n- **discord-hitl/** — Human-in-the-loop\n- **ralphchives-read/**, **ralphchives-write/** — Archive access\n- **microsoft-docs/**, **web-fetch/** — Data sources\n\n### **MCP Sidecar** (`src/shared/mcp-sidecar/`)\n- Isolated MCP tool gateway, runs separately from main orchestrator\n\n### **Security** (`src/shared/security/`)\n- Security policies and validation\n\n### **Hooks** (`src/shared/hooks/`)\n- Lifecycle hooks (pre-execution, post-execution)\n\n---\n\n## **5. SCRIPTS** (`scripts/`)\n\n| Script | Purpose |\n|--------|---------|\n| **visualize-agent-graph.ts** (23KB) | Visualizes agent dependency graph |\n| **run-agent.ts** (5.9KB) | Run individual agents |\n| **run-hooks.ts** (6.6KB) | Execute lifecycle hooks |\n| **reset-issue.ts** (5.9KB) | Reset test environment |\n| **lookup-users.ts** | JIRA user lookup |\n| **audit-log-hierarchy.py** | Log hierarchy auditing |\n| **audit-parallel-and-tokens.py** | Parallel execution audit |\n| **audit-parallel-deep.py** | Deep parallel audit |\n| **audit-verify-fix.py** | Validation checks |\n| **validate.ts** | Input/output validation |\n\n---\n\n## **6. DOCUMENTATION**\n\n### **Root-Level Architectural Docs** (13 files)\n| File | Size | Purpose |\n|------|------|---------|\n| **ARCHITECTURE.md** | 36KB | Ralph orchestrator architecture |\n| **AGENT-AS-FUNCTION.md** | 12KB | Subagent-as-function pattern |\n| **CLAUDE.md** | 15KB | Claude Code guidance |\n| **CONFIGURATION.md** | 31KB | Configuration reference |\n| **MCP.md** | 17KB | MCP servers & tools |\n| **SECURITY.md** | 17KB | Security hardening |\n| **AUTH-PRISMA.md** | 21KB | Auth & Prisma integration |\n| **CODEGRAPH-STRATEGY.md** | 7KB | CodeGraph context |\n| **DEPENDENCY-INJECTION.md** | 3.3KB | DI design |\n| **README.md** | 11KB | Project overview |\n| **copilot-cli-internals.md** | 15KB | CLI internals |\n| **refactoring-instr.md** | 5KB | Refactoring guide |\n| **TEMPLATE-INSPECTOR.md** | 1.2KB | Template inspection |\n\n### **User Guide** (`docs/user-guide/`, 11 files)\n- README, configuration, environment-variables, profiles, runtime-macros\n- skills, template-variables, trigger-parameters, mcp-servers\n- deploying-mcp-servers, codegraphcontext\n\n### **Developer Documentation** (`docs/dev-doc/`, 10 files)\n- agent-templates, compose-layering, cradle-refac, data-source-registration\n- local-testing, mcp-sidecar-design, mcp-tool-naming, multistage-pipelines\n- prompt-injection-hardening, ralphchives\n\n### **Research & Issues** (`docs/research/`, `docs/past-issues/`)\n- oh-my-opencode-analysis.md, 001-ado-server-crash-session-loss.md\n\n---\n\n## **7. CURRENT PRODUCTION RUN STATE**\n\n### **Domain: Romantic Fantasy Writer**\n**Location**: `.fractal-factory/`\n\n| File | Size | Status |\n|------|------|--------|\n| **context.json** | 1.7KB | ✅ Configured (target: .fractal-factory/output/romantic-fantasy-writer) |\n| **domain-brief.md** | 32KB | ✅ Provided |\n| **invariants.md** | 18KB | ✅ Provided |\n| **domain-model.json** | 67KB | ✅ Populated (subdomains, invariants with confidence scores, assets, patterns) |\n| **progress.json** | 1.6KB | 🔄 Pass 1 (Discovery) ACTIVE |\n| **roster.json** | 82B | ⏳ Pending (roster-planner will populate) |\n| **architecture.json** | 100B | ⏳ Pending (pipeline-architect will populate) |\n| **test-plan.json** | 61B | ⏳ Pending (test-planner will populate) |\n| **manifest.json** | 568B | ✅ Audit log (agent dispatch history) |\n\n### **Configuration**\n- **maxDepth**: 4 (allows coordinator→sub-coordinator→specialists hierarchy)\n- **maxAgents**: 80 (planning budget)\n- **maxGapCycles**: 10 (convergence iterations)\n- **maxWriterReviewerRetries**: 10 (prompt loop retries)\n- **Exemplars**: `.fractals/fractal-factory/agents` (learning from the factory itself!)\n- **All 7 passes enabled**: discovery, analysis, planning, execution, verification, gapHunting, delivery\n\n### **Produced Output Structure** (will be created in Pass 4)\n```\n.fractal-factory/produced-output/\n├── agents/                    # .agent.md files\n├── schemas/                   # JSON schema documentation\n├── skills/                    # Skill stub directories\n├── tests/                     # Golden test fixture files\n└── docs/                      # Architecture guide, user guide, roster reference\n```\n\n---\n\n## **8. CORE PATTERNS & PRINCIPLES**\n\n### **Pure Router Pattern**\nAll coordinators and the session orchestrator follow a strict purity rule:\n- ✅ Read status.json from children\n- ✅ Dispatch children via invocation\n- ✅ Update own status.json and manifest.json\n- ❌ **Never** do substantive work (that's a specialist's job)\n\n### **Agent-as-Function with Filesystem Artifact Handoff**\n- Orchestrator reads only status.json (single-line signal)\n- All detail flows horizontally between specialists via filesystem\n- Specialists read upstream artifacts directly, never through orchestrator\n- Prevents context window bloat and maintains independence\n\n### **Universal Agent Prompt Template**\nEvery produced agent follows:\n```yaml\n---\nname: agent-name\ndescription: short description\nmodel: claude-opus-4.6\nuser-invocable: false\n---\n\n# Overview\n\n## Context\n(what to read from .fractal-factory/)\n\n## Inputs\n(what files to process)\n\n## Process\n(step-by-step algorithm)\n\n## Write Rules\n(what artifacts to produce)\n\n## Anti-Laziness Rules\n(quality gates and validation)\n```\n\n### **Convergence via Gap Hunting**\n- Gap-hunter searches 8 categories for issues\n- Reports convergence (clean) or dirty state\n- Orchestrator can re-run earlier passes if dirty\n- Bounded by maxGapCycles\n\n### **Anti-Laziness Enforcement**\nFour-layer validation:\n1. **Prompt-Reviewer** — Validates prompt completeness\n2. **Checklist-Validator** — Exhaustive structural validation\n3. **Audit-Oracle** — Independent consistency audit\n4. **Gap-Hunter** — Adversarial coverage search\n\n---\n\n## **KEY STATISTICS**\n\n| Metric | Count |\n|--------|-------|\n| Agent files (exemplars) | 28 |\n| Total agent lines | 3,881 |\n| Service modules | 16 |\n| Container modules | 12 |\n| Shared skill categories | 6 |\n| MCP servers | 9 |\n| Agent include partials | 10+ |\n| Root-level docs | 13 |\n| User guide docs | 11 |\n| Dev docs | 10 |\n| Scripts | 12+ |\n| 7-pass pipeline stages | 7 |\n| Coordinators | 7 |\n| Specialists | 16+ |\n| Verification agents | 3 |\n\n---\n\n## **SUMMARY: LEARNING EXEMPLARS**\n\nThe Fractal Factory is a meta-learning system:\n\n1. **Discovery agents** learn domain structure from user inputs\n2. **Analysis agents** design architecture for the produced system\n3. **Planning agents** create detailed specifications (roster, routing, tests)\n4. **Execution agents** write agent prompts and infrastructure\n5. **Verification agents** validate quality and coverage\n6. **Gap hunters** iteratively refine until convergence\n7. **Delivery agents** package and document the result\n\n**The romantic-fantasy-writer production run is currently learning from the factory's own exemplar agents, creating a meta-circular loop of production and learning.**",
