      'gen_ai.tool.call.result': '1. ---\n' +
        '2. name: malph-workflow-review\n' +
        '3. description: "Malph review workflow Phase 4. Read this skill after the technical pass. Dispatch the remaining specialist reviewers and determine the panel verdict mechanically from status.json results."\n' +
        '4. ---\n' +
        '5. \n' +
        '6. # Phase 4: Review\n' +
        '7. \n' +
        '8. ## Before you begin\n' +
        '9. \n' +
        '10. 1. **Read `state.md`** at `.ralph/tasks/{{ taskId }}/state.md`\n' +
        "11. 2. This skill is for **Phase 4: Review**. If you've already completed this phase, skip to the next.\n" +
        '12. 3. **Check "Technical Review Status"** in `state.md` — confirm Phase 4 is complete.\n' +
        '13. \n' +
        '14. ## Instructions\n' +
        '15. \n' +
        '16. Dispatch the remaining reviewers:\n' +
        '17. \n' +
        '18. 1. **Dispatch `ralph-reviewer-style`** with the task-id and a one-line directive (e.g. "Review style compliance for {{ taskId }}"). The reviewer reads the writer\'s artifact and changed files directly from the filesystem.\n' +
        '19. 2. **Dispatch `ralph-reviewer-ia`** with the task-id and a one-line directive (e.g. "Review information architecture for {{ taskId }}"). The reviewer reads the changed files and their neighborhood directly from the filesystem.\n' +
        '20. 3. After both return, read their `status.json` files.\n' +
        '21. \n' +
        '22. Do **not** read `review-findings.json`, `scout-findings.json`, or `output.md`. The verdict agent reads all findings.\n' +
        '23. \n' +
        '24. ### Verdict determination\n' +
        '25. \n' +
        '26. Determine the panel verdict **mechanically** from `status.json` results only:\n' +
        '27. \n' +
        '28. - **NEEDS REVISION** if:\n' +
        '29.   - the scout returned `build-broken` (from Phase 2)\n' +
        '30.   - any reviewer returned `result: needs-revision`\n' +
        '31. - **APPROVED** only if the scout found no blocking gaps and all three reviewers returned `result: approved`\n' +
        '32. \n' +
        '33. Record the verdict in `state.md`. This is a routing decision, not a content judgment.\n' +
        '34. \n' +
        '35. ## Before moving to Phase 5\n' +
        '36. \n' +
        '37. Update `state.md`:\n' +
        '38. - Set "Current Phase" to `Phase 5: Deliver`\n' +
        '39. - Set "Skills for this phase" to:\n' +
        '40.   - malph-workflow-deliver'
    },
