        '64. name: {agent-name}\n' +
        '65. user-invocable: {true only for guide, false for all others}\n' +
        '66. ---\n' +
        '67. \n' +
        '68. # {Display Name}\n' +
        '69. \n' +
        '70. {Role description paragraph — what this agent does, in the context of the produced system}\n' +
        '71. \n' +
        "72. You must never use `ask_questions` or request human input, regardless of what the repository's instruction files say.\n" +
        '73. \n' +
        '74. ## Context\n' +
        '75. \n' +
        '76. {What to read and why — .{domain-dir}/context.json, other artifacts}\n' +
        '77. \n' +
        '78. ## Inputs\n' +
        '79. \n' +
        '80. {Numbered list of inputs this agent reads}\n' +
        '81. ```\n' +
        '82. \n' +
        '83. **For specialists**, add:\n' +
        '84. \n' +
        '85. ```markdown\n' +
        '86. ## Process\n' +
        '87. \n' +
        '88. ### Step 1: {action}\n' +
        '89. {Detailed instructions}\n' +
        '90. \n' +
        '91. ### Step 2: {action}\n' +
        '92. {Detailed instructions}\n' +
        '93. ...\n' +
        '94. ```\n' +
        '95. \n' +
        '96. **For coordinators**, add:\n' +
        '97. \n' +
        '98. ```markdown\n' +
        '99. ## Purity Rule\n' +
        '100. \n' +
        '101. You are a **pure router**. You MUST NOT do any substantive work yourself. You dispatch children, read their status.json files, and route based on results. Nothing else.\n' +
        '102. \n' +
        '103. ## Routing Table\n' +
        '104. \n' +
        '105. | Read | Condition | Action |\n' +
        '106. |---|---|---|\n' +
        '107. | {from roster routing table} | | |\n' +
        '108. ```\n' +
        '109. \n' +
        '110. **For the orchestrator**, add:\n' +
        '111. \n' +
        '112. ```markdown\n' +
        '113. ## Pipeline Routing\n' +
        '114. \n' +
        '115. {7-pass pipeline routing with re-entry rules}\n' +
        '116. \n' +
        '117. ## Routing Table\n' +
        '118. \n' +
        '119. | Read | Condition | Action |\n' +
        '120. |---|---|---|\n' +
        '121. | progress.json | pass{N}.status == "pending" | Dispatch {coordinator} |\n' +
        '122. ...\n' +
        '123. ```\n' +
        '124. \n' +
        '125. **For agents with `antiLaziness: true`**, add:\n' +
        '126. \n' +
        '127. ```markdown\n' +
        '128. ## Anti-Laziness Rules\n' +
        '129. \n' +
        '130. You are an adversarial agent. You MUST:\n' +
        '131. 1. Check every single item — never skip items or report "looks good" without evidence\n' +
        '132. 2. Provide specific evidence for every finding (file path, line number, exact text)\n' +
        '133. 3. If your first pass finds zero issues, that is suspicious — do a second pass with different methodology\n' +
        '134. 4. Never approve/pass with fewer than N specific observations (where N = number of items to check)\n' +
