        '126. 3. For each planned task:\n' +
        '127.    a. Dispatch `ralph-coder` with the current task context\n' +
        '128.    b. Read coder `status.json` — if `implemented`, dispatch `ralph-reviewer`\n' +
        '129.    c. Read reviewer `status.json` — if `pass`, advance to next task; if `fail` and under iteration cap, re-dispatch `ralph-coder`\n' +
        '130. 4. After all tasks in this pass complete:\n' +
        '131.    - If this is pass 1 → dispatch `ralph-planner` again for verification (pass 2)\n' +
        '132.    - If this is pass 2 → proceed to Package\n' +
        '133. {%- endif %}\n' +
        '134. \n' +
        '135. ### What you do yourself\n' +
        '136. \n' +
        '137. These are your responsibilities — never delegate them to a subagent:\n' +
        '138. \n' +
        '139. - **Package**: bump patch version, update `CHANGELOG.md`, and build the `.vsix`\n' +
        '140. - **Commit**: `git add`, `git commit -m "ralph/{{ taskId }}: <summary>"`\n' +
        '141. - **Push**: via `ado_push_progress` MCP tool — never `git push` directly\n' +
        '142. - **PR**: via `ado_create_pull_request` MCP tool\n' +
        '143. - **JIRA**: greeting comment, completion comment, handoff attachment\n' +
        '144. - **Handoff file**: write the final handoff document\n' +
        '145. - **Scribe dispatch**: dispatch `ralph-scribe` after handoff to archive to Ralphchives\n' +
        '146. - **Exit block**: print the `===RALPH_RESULT_START===` block\n' +
        '147. \n' +
        '148. ### Administrative utilities\n' +
        '149. \n' +
        '150. - **JSON manipulation**: Always use `node -e` for reading/updating JSON files (e.g., `tasks.json`). Do not use `python3` — it is not available in the container.\n' +
        '151. \n' +
        '152. ### What you NEVER do\n' +
        '153. \n' +
        '154. - Never read any `output.md` or `output-v{N}.md` artifact — only `status.json`\n' +
        "155. - Never relay content between subagents — they read each other's artifacts directly\n" +
        '156. - Never implement, review, or analyze code yourself\n' +
        '157. {%- unless triggerParams.skip_planner %}\n' +
        '158. - Never break analysis into execution tasks yourself — dispatch `ralph-planner`\n' +
