        '3. **Agent:** fractal-factory-asset-auditor  \n' +
        '4. **Iteration:** 1  \n' +
        '5. **Timestamp:** 2026-03-15T20:15:00Z\n' +
        '6. \n' +
        '7. ## Executive Summary\n' +
        '8. \n' +
        '9. Scanned the ralph-orchestrator repository for assets reusable by the romantic-fantasy-writer agent system. Examined **6 shared skill categories** (~50 skills), **9 MCP servers**, **7 agent include files**, **2 personality templates**, **4 post-hook patterns**, **2 agent profiles**, **28 fractal factory exemplar agents**, and **6 hook scripts**.\n' +
        '10. \n' +
        '11. **Result:** 25 assets catalogued as relevant. The vast majority of code-specific skills (TypeScript, Ruby, Jekyll, .NET, VSCode) are irrelevant to creative fiction writing. However, the **infrastructure patterns** — artifact handoff contracts, workflow phasing, multi-reviewer panels, revision loops, personality templates — are highly transferable.\n' +
        '12. \n' +
        '13. ## Scan Statistics\n' +
        '14. \n' +
        '15. | Category Scanned | Items Found | Relevant | Irrelevant |\n' +
        '16. |---|---|---|---|\n' +
