        '18. | Shared Skills (integrations/) | 6 | 0 | 6 |\n' +
        '19. | Shared Skills (tasks/) | 6 | 3 | 3 |\n' +
        '20. | Shared Skills (workflow/) | 15 | 5 | 10 |\n' +
        '21. | Shared Skills (xperience/) | 2 | 0 | 2 |\n' +
        '22. | Agent Includes (core) | 7 | 3 | 4 |\n' +
        '23. | Agent Includes (personality/) | 2 | 2 | 0 |\n' +
        '24. | Agent Includes (post-hooks/) | 4 | 3 | 1 |\n' +
        '25. | Agent Includes (ralph-docs/) | 14 | 2 | 12 |\n' +
        '26. | MCP Servers | 9 | 3 | 6 |\n' +
        '27. | Profiles | 2 | 1 | 1 |\n' +
        '28. | Fractal Factory Agents | 28 | 2 | 26 |\n' +
        '29. | Hook Scripts | 7 | 1 | 6 |\n' +
        '30. | **Total** | **122** | **28 assessed → 25 catalogued** | **94** |\n' +
        '31. \n' +
        '32. ## Reusability Classification\n' +
        '33. \n' +
        '34. ### Direct Reuse (3 assets) — Mount as-is\n' +
        '35. \n' +
        '36. | ID | Asset | Why Direct |\n' +
        '37. |---|---|---|\n' +
        '38. | ASSET-001 | agent-as-function-contract | Universal artifact handoff pattern — status.json, output.md versioning, manifest.json audit trail. Every agent in the fiction system needs this. |\n' +
        '39. | ASSET-002 | operational-rules | Routing constraints (read only status.json, wait for subagents, block correctly). Domain-agnostic. |\n' +
        '40. | ASSET-003 | prompt-security | Prompt injection defense, data exfiltration prevention. User-provided story prompts are untrusted input — same security model applies. |\n' +
        '41. \n' +
        '42. ### Adaptable (8 assets) — Useful with domain-specific modifications\n' +
        '43. \n' +
        '44. | ID | Asset | Adaptation Needed |\n' +
