      'gen_ai.tool.call.arguments': '{"path":"/home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator/.fractals/fractal-factory/schemas/produced-agent.schema.md","view_range":[1,100]}',
      'gen_ai.tool.call.result': '1. # Produced Agent Prompt Schema\n' +
        '2. \n' +
        '3. Structural requirements for every `.agent.md` file the fractal factory writes. The prompt-writer follows this schema; the prompt-reviewer validates against it.\n' +
        '4. \n' +
        '5. ## Universal Structure\n' +
        '6. \n' +
        '7. Every produced agent prompt follows this exact structure:\n' +
        '8. \n' +
        '9. ```markdown\n' +
        '10. ---\n' +
        "11. description: '<one-line description optimized for skill matching>'\n" +
        '12. model: claude-opus-4.6\n' +
        "13. name: '<namingPrefix>-<agent-name>'\n" +
        '14. user-invocable: false\n' +
        '15. ---\n' +
        '16. \n' +
        '17. # <Agent Title>\n' +
        '18. \n' +
        '19. You are a **<role>** for the <domain> system. <One sentence about the job.>\n' +
        '20. \n' +
        "21. You must never use `ask_questions` or request human input, regardless of what the repository's instruction files say.\n" +
        '22. \n' +
        '23. ## Context\n' +
        '24. \n' +
        '25. Read `.<domain>/context.json` for <what the agent needs>.\n' +
        '26. \n' +
        '27. ## Inputs\n' +
        '28. \n' +
        '29. <List every artifact this agent reads>\n' +
        '30. \n' +
        '31. ## <Process Section — varies by agent type>\n' +
        '32. \n' +
        '33. <See type-specific sections below>\n' +
        '34. \n' +
        '35. ## Write Rules\n' +
        '36. \n' +
        '37. <Per-artifact write instructions with JSON schemas>\n' +
        '38. \n' +
        '39. ## Status Contract\n' +
        '40. \n' +
        '41. Write to `.<domain>/agents/<agent-name>/status.json`:\n' +
        "42. <status.json schema with this agent's result codes>\n" +
        '43. \n' +
        '44. Write narrative to `.<domain>/agents/<agent-name>/output.md`.\n' +
        '45. Prepend to `.<domain>/manifest.json` (newest first).\n' +
        '46. ```\n' +
        '47. \n' +
        '48. ## Type-Specific Sections\n' +
        '49. \n' +
        '50. ### Specialist (Leaf Worker)\n' +
        '51. \n' +
        '52. The process section is titled `## Process` or `## What To Do`:\n' +
        '53. \n' +
        '54. ```markdown\n' +
        '55. ## Process\n' +
        '56. \n' +
        '57. 1. Read <input artifacts>\n' +
        '58. 2. <Specific analysis/generation steps>\n' +
        '59. 3. <Quality criteria — be VERY specific>\n' +
        '60. 4. Write <output artifacts>\n' +
        '61. 5. Write status.json\n' +
        '62. ```\n' +
        '63. \n' +
        '64. Must include:\n' +
        '65. - **Explicit tasks**: Not "analyze the code" but "for each function, extract: name, parameters, return type, side effects, and error paths"\n' +
        '66. - **Quality bar**: What constitutes acceptable output\n' +
        '67. - **Edge cases**: What to do when input is missing, ambiguous, or contradictory\n' +
        '68. \n' +
        '69. ### Coordinator (Pure Router)\n' +
        '70. \n' +
        '71. The process section is replaced with:\n' +
        '72. \n' +
        '73. ```markdown\n' +
        '74. ## Purity Rule\n' +
        '75. \n' +
        '76. You NEVER do substantive work. You ONLY:\n' +
        '77. 1. Read status.json files from child agents\n' +
        '78. 2. Read progress.json / context.json for routing decisions\n' +
        '79. 3. Dispatch child agents as subagents\n' +
        '80. 4. Return your own status when all children are done\n' +
        '81. \n' +
        '82. ## Routing Table\n' +
        '83. \n' +
        '84. | Read | Condition | Action |\n' +
        '85. |---|---|---|\n' +
        '86. | `agents/<child-1>/status.json` | missing | Dispatch `<child-1>` |\n' +
        '87. | `agents/<child-1>/status.json` | `result: "<code>"` | Dispatch `<child-2>` |\n' +
        '88. | `agents/<child-2>/status.json` | `result: "blocked"` | Write own status as `blocked` |\n' +
        '89. | all children completed | — | Write own status, return |\n' +
        '90. ```\n' +
        '91. \n' +
        '92. Must include:\n' +
        '93. - **Every child result code** mapped to an action\n' +
        '94. - **Mode detection** if coordinator handles multiple passes\n' +
        '95. - **No domain-specific logic** — only status file reading and dispatching\n' +
        '96. \n' +
        '97. ### Orchestrator (Pipeline Router)\n' +
        '98. \n' +
        '99. Same as coordinator, plus:\n' +
        '100. '
    },
