est Pattern:**\n- Prepend entry (same structure as Domain Scanner)\n\n---\n\n### **3. FRACTAL-FACTORY-PROMPT-REVIEWER** (Reviewer/Verification Specialist)\n\n**Main Sections:**\n```\n# Prompt Reviewer\n  ## Context\n  ## Inputs\n  ## Anti-Laziness Rules\n  ## Process\n    ### Step 1: Enumerate Files to Review\n    ### Step 2: Structural Review (Per Agent)\n      {Frontmatter subsection}\n      {Required Sections subsection}\n      {Type-Specific Sections subsection}\n      {Universal Sections subsection}\n    ### Step 3: Content Review (Per Agent)\n      {Domain specificity subsection}\n      {Routing completeness subsection}\n      {Result code consistency subsection}\n    ### Step 4: Write Review Results\n    ### Step 5: Update Roster Status\n  ## Write Rules\n    ### roster.json\n  ## Status Contract\n```\n\n**Inputs:**\n1. Numbered list in `## Inputs`\n2. Reads: `context.json`, `roster.json`, `architecture.json`, `domain-model.json`, `produced-output/agents/*.agent.md`\n\n**Outputs (Write Rules):**\n- Update `roster.json` setting `status` to `\"reviewed\"` (for approved) or keep as `\"written\"` (for rejected)\n\n**Status Contract:**\n```json\n{\n  \"agent\": \"fractal-factory-prompt-reviewer\",\n  \"task_id\": \"pass4/prompt-review\",\n  \"status\": \"completed\",\n  \"result\": \"approved | rejected\",\n  \"summary\": \"Reviewed N agents: A approved, R rejected. Total findings: B blockers, W warnings, I info.\",\n  \"artifacts\": [\"roster.json\", \"agents/fractal-factory-prompt-reviewer/output.md\"],\n  \"next_hint\": \"fractal-factory-prompt-writer (if rejected) | fractal-factory-infra-writer (if all approved)\",\n  \"iteration\": 1\n}\n```\n**Result Codes:** `approved`, `rejected`\n\n**Anti-Laziness Rules:** **YES** — explicit section with 7 adversarial rules:\n1. Read every prompt file cover-to-cover; never skim\n2. Check every structural checklist item for every agent\n3. Provide specific evidence for every finding\n4. Never approve with fewer observation