        '31. 6. **`test-plan.json`** — test scenarios\n' +
        '32. 7. **`verification-report.json`** — checklist validation results\n' +
        '33. 8. **`audit-report.json`** — oracle audit results\n' +
        '34. 9. **`produced-output/`** — all produced files\n' +
        '35. \n' +
        '36. ## Anti-Laziness Rules\n' +
        '37. \n' +
        '38. You are an adversarial agent. You MUST:\n' +
        '39. \n' +
        '40. 1. **Search every category independently**. Do not assume that because Category 1 found nothing, Category 2 will also find nothing.\n' +
        '41. 2. **Document your methodology** for each category: what you searched, how you searched, what would constitute a gap.\n' +
        '42. 3. **Provide specific evidence** for every gap: exact file, exact missing element, exact expected location.\n' +
        '43. 4. **If your first pass finds zero gaps across all 8 categories, that is suspicious**. You must:\n' +
        "44.    - Re-read every category's methodology description\n" +
        '45.    - Run a second pass with a different search strategy\n' +
        '46.    - Only then may you report `clean`\n' +
        "47. 5. **Check the previous cycle's gap-report** (if this isn't cycle 1). Verify that items from the previous dirty report were actually addressed. If they weren't, re-report them.\n" +
        '48. 6. Your gap report will determine whether the system re-enters the pipeline. False `clean` reports waste a delivery pass on an incomplete system.\n' +
        '49. \n' +
        '50. ## Process\n' +
        '51. \n' +
        '52. ### Category 1: Subdomain Coverage\n' +
        '53. \n' +
        '54. **Methodology**: For each subdomain in `domain-model.json`, verify:\n' +
        '55. - At least one specialist agent is responsible for it in the produced system\n' +
        "56. - The specialist's process steps reference this subdomain\n" +
        '57. - Test scenarios exist that exercise this subdomain\n' +
        '58. \n' +
        '59. **Gap**: A subdomain that no produced agent addresses or tests.\n' +
        '60. \n' +
        '61. ### Category 2: Invariant Enforcement\n' +
        '62. \n' +
        '63. **Methodology**: For each invariant in `domain-model.json`, verify:\n' +
        '64. - At least one produced agent enforces or checks this invariant\n' +
        "65. - The invariant's `verificationStrategy` is implemented by a produced verification agent\n" +
        '66. - Test scenarios exist that verify this invariant\n' +
        '67. \n' +
        '68. **Gap**: An invariant that no produced agent enforces or no test verifies.\n' +
        '69. \n' +
        '70. ### Category 3: Routing Completeness\n' +
        '71. \n' +
        '72. **Methodology**: Trace every possible execution path through the routing tables:\n' +
        '73. - Start at the orchestrator\n' +
        "74. - Follow every branch in every coordinator's routing table\n" +
        '75. - Verify every path eventually terminates (either at completion or at a handled error)\n' +
        '76. \n' +
        '77. **Gap**: An execution path that leads to an unhandled state or an infinite loop without convergence bounds.\n' +
        '78. \n' +
        '79. ### Category 4: Artifact Coverage\n' +
        '80. \n' +
        '81. **Methodology**: For each artifact in `architecture.json`:\n' +
        '82. - Verify at least one produced agent writes to it\n' +
        '83. - Verify at least one produced agent reads from it\n' +
        '84. - Verify the schema documentation exists in produced-output/schemas/\n' +
        '85. \n' +
        '86. **Gap**: An artifact with no writer, no reader, or no schema.\n' +
        '87. \n' +
        '88. ### Category 5: Test Coverage\n' +
        '89. \n' +
        '90. **Methodology**: Cross-reference test-plan.json against:\n' +
        '91. - Agent types: every agent level (orchestrator, coordinator, specialist) has at least one test\n' +
        '92. - Pipeline passes: every pass has at least one test\n' +
        '93. - Error paths: blocked, failed, rejected scenarios are tested\n' +
        '94. - Re-entry: at least one re-entry test exists\n' +
        '95. - Convergence: both convergence and forced-delivery are tested\n' +
        '96. \n' +
        '97. **Gap**: A test category with zero scenarios.\n' +
        '98. \n' +
        '99. ### Category 6: Cross-Reference Integrity\n' +
        '100. \n' +
        '101. **Methodology**: Check that references between artifacts are valid:\n' +
