      "finish_reason": "tool_calls",
      "logprobs": null,
      "message": {
        "reasoning_text": "Now I have comprehensive data from all the exemplar analysis. Let me synthesize the patterns and write the three output files:\n\n1. Update domain-model.json with exemplarPatterns array\n2. Write status.json\n3. Write output.md\n4. Update manifest.json\n\nLet me extract the key patterns:\n\n**Hierarchy Patterns:**\n1. Three-tier orchestrator→coordinator→specialist hierarchy (depth-3)\n2. Guide as user-facing entry point, separate from orchestrator\n3. Coordinators as pure routers (never do substantive work)\n4. One coordinator per pipeline pass\n5. Specialists grouped by pass/phase under their coordinator\n\n\n6. Names follow `{prefix}-{role}` with hyphens, using suffixes like -coordinator, -writer, -reviewer, -planner, -analyzer, -auditor, -hunter, -oracle, -designer, -packager, and -guide, where compound roles combine domain nouns with action verbs like prompt-writer or domain-scanner\n7. Routing uses status-file polling to read conditions and dispatch actions in sequential chains, organized in three-column tables showing read operations, conditions, and resulting actions, with writer-reviewer loops that respect maximum iteration counts before falling back to mark-blocked-proceed\n8. The status contract tracks agent, task_id, status, result, summary, artifacts, next_hint, and iteration, while manifest.json serves as an append-only audit log with newest entries prepended first, and each agent maintains its own output directory with status.json and output.md alongside shared domain artifacts like domain-model.json, roster.json, and architecture.json that use read-modify-write patterns\n9. Adversarial agents get explicit anti-laziness rules including the principle that zero findings are suspicious, warnings that work will be audited by the next agent, and strict evidence requirements to quote exact text and cite specific sections\n10. Convergence uses an 8-category gap search with documented methodology\n\n, produces clean verdicts with severity levels, counts cycles with configurable limits, and suggests re-entry passes in gap reports before forced termination with delivered-with-gaps status\n11. Prompts follow a universal template structure starting with frontmatter, role description, context, inputs, process, write rules, and status contract, with frontmatter including description, model, name, and user-invocable flag, plus an explicit instruction never to use ask_questions, and generation happens bottom-up from specialists through coordinators to orchestrator\n12. Result codes vary by role: orchestrator uses delivered, delivered-with-gaps, or failed; coordinators use complete, blocked, or complete-with-blocked; and specialists use domain-specific verbs like scanned, extracted, audited, analyzed, planned, written, or approved\n\nNow I'm narrowing down to the 15-20 most relevant patterns to document properly.",
        "role": "assistant",
        "reasoning_opaque": "",
        "content": "Now I have all the data I need. Let me synthesize and write the outputs.",
        "refusal": null,
        "tool_calls": [
          {
            "id": "toolu_014sJbfpMqjT78tX9o6teNSM",
            "type": "function",
            "function": {
              "name": "report_intent",
              "arguments": "{\"intent\": \"Writing exemplar analysis outputs\"}"
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "toolu_01Db8Ug7j7YqmLvw9ZCXscQS",
            "type": "function",
            "function": {
              "name": "bash",
              "arguments": "{\"command\": \"cd /home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator && python3 << 'PYEOF'\\nimport json\\n\\n# Read existing domain-model.json\\nwith open('.fractal-factory/domain-model.json') as f:\\n    dm = json.load(f)\\n\\n# Define exemplar patterns\\npatterns = [\\n    {\\n        \\\"id\\\": \\\"PATTERN-001\\\",\\n        \\\"name\\\": \\\"depth-3-pass-coordinators\\\",\\n        \\\"source\\\": \\\".fractals/fractal-factory/agents/\\\",\\n        \\\"category\\\": \\\"hierarchy\\\",\\n        \\\"description\\\": \\\"Three-tier hierarchy: guide → orchestrator → pass-coordinators → specialists. Each pipeline pass has exactly one coordinator that owns dispatch sequencing for 2-6 specialists. Coordinators never do substantive work (pure routing). Guide is the sole user-facing entry point, separate from the orchestrator.\\\",\\n        \\\"applicability\\\": \\\"Directly applicable — romantic fantasy writer needs the same pattern: guide (gathers story idea) → orchestrator (routes creative pipeline) → phase coordinators (concept, worldbuilding, characters, plotting, drafting, revision, beta-reading, polish) → specialist writers/reviewers per phase.\\\",\\n        \\\"discoveredBy\\\": \\\"fractal-factory-exemplar-analyzer\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n        \\\"id\\\": \\\"PATTERN-002\\\",\\n        \\\"name\\\": \\\"pure-router-coordinators\\\",\\n        \\\"source\\\": \\\".fractals/fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory-discovery-coordinator.agent.md\\\",\\n        \\\"category\\\": \\\"routing\\\",\\n        \\\"description\\\": \\\"Coordinators are pure state machines: they read child status.json files, evaluate conditions, dispatch the next child, and write their own status. They NEVER read child output.md, never write domain artifacts, and never perform substantive work. All routing decisions are based solely on status.json result codes.\\\",\\n        \\\"applicability\\\": \\\"Directly applicable — all phase coordinators in the fantasy writer (e.g., worldbuilding-coordinator, drafting-coordinator) must follow this pure-router pattern. Keeps coordinator prompts small and routing logic deterministic.\\\",\\n        \\\"discoveredBy\\\": \\\"fractal-factory-exemplar-analyzer\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n        \\\"id\\\": \\\"PATTERN-003\\\",\\n        \\\"name\\\": \\\"status-file-polling-routing\\\",\\n        \\\"source\\\": \\\".fractals/fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory-discovery-coordinator.agent.md\\\",\\n        \\\"category\\\": \\\"routing\\\",\\n        \\\"description\\\": \\\"Routing tables use three-column format: Read (which status.json) | Condition (result code check) | Action (dispatch agent or write own status). Missing status.json means agent hasn't run yet → dispatch it. Each result code maps to exactly one action. This creates a deterministic, re-entrant state machine.\\\",\\n        \\\"applicability\\\": \\\"Directly applicable — all coordinators and the orchestrator must use this Read|Condition|Action routing table format. Enables reliable re-entry after gap hunting cycles.\\\",\\n        \\\"discoveredBy\\\": \\\"fractal-factory-exemplar-analyzer\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n        \\\"id\\\": \\\"PATTERN-004\\\",\\n        \\\"name\\\": \\\"writer-reviewer-loop-with-max-retries\\\",\\n        \\\"source\\\": \\\".fractals/fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory-execution-coordinator.agent.md\\\",\\n        \\\"category\\\": \\\"routing\\\",\\n        \\\"description\\\": \\\"Writer and reviewer agents form a feedback loop: writer produces content → reviewer evaluates → if rejected and iteration < maxRetries, re-dispatch writer with reviewer's feedback. If maxRetries exceeded, mark as blocked and proceed. Reviewer's output.md contains specific feedback for the writer's next iteration.\\\",\\n        \\\"applicability\\\": \\\"Directly applicable — the fantasy writer needs this pattern everywhere: chapter-drafter → chapter-reviewer, worldbuilding-writer → consistency-auditor, character-designer → character-auditor. MaxRetries prevents infinite loops while ensuring quality iteration.\\\",\\n        \\\"discoveredBy\\\": \\\"fractal-factory-exemplar-analyzer\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n        \\\"id\\\": \\\"PATTERN-005\\\",\\n        \\\"name\\\": \\\"seven-pass-pipeline-with-re-entry\\\",\\n        \\\"source\\\": \\\".fractals/fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory.agent.md\\\",\\n        \\\"category\\\": \\\"hierarchy\\\",\\n        \\\"description\\\": \\\"Pipeline organized as 7 sequential passes: discovery → analysis → planning → execution → verification → gap-hunting → delivery. Gap-hunting can trigger re-entry to an earlier pass (analysis or planning) with cycle counting and forced termination after maxCycles. Progress tracked in progress.json with per-pass status (pending → active → completed).\\\",\\n        \\\"applicability\\\": \\\"Adapt for fantasy writer — map to creative pipeline passes: concept → worldbuilding → characters → plotting → style-calibration → drafting → revision → beta-reading → polish → delivery. Re-entry pattern from beta-reading back to revision is directly analogous to gap-hunting re-entry.\\\",\\n        \\\"discoveredBy\\\": \\\"fractal-factory-exemplar-analyzer\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n        \\\"id\\\": \\\"PATTERN-006\\\",\\n        \\\"name\\\": \\\"universal-status-contract\\\",\\n        \\\"source\\\": \\\".fractals/fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory-domain-scanner.agent.md\\\",\\n        \\\"category\\\": \\\"artifact\\\",\\n        \\\"description\\\": \\\"Every agent writes status.json with exactly 8 fields: agent (name), task_id (pass/task slug), status (completed|failed), result (domain-specific verb), summary (human-readable 20-50 words), artifacts (list of produced file paths), next_hint (suggested next agent), iteration (integer counter). This uniform shape enables generic routing logic.\\\",\\n        \\\"applicability\\\": \\\"Directly applicable — every fantasy writer agent must produce status.json in this exact format. Enables coordinators to route without understanding domain content.\\\",\\n        \\\"discoveredBy\\\": \\\"fractal-factory-exemplar-analyzer\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n        \\\"id\\\": \\\"PATTERN-007\\\",\\n        \\\"name\\\": \\\"manifest-prepend-audit-log\\\",\\n        \\\"source\\\": \\\".fractal-factory/manifest.json\\\",\\n        \\\"category\\\": \\\"artifact\\\",\\n        \\\"description\\\": \\\"Every agent prepends an entry to manifest.json (newest first) with: timestamp, agent name, artifacts list, status, result, iteration. Creates an immutable audit trail of all agent executions. The manifest is the single source of truth for what happened and when.\\\",\\n        \\\"applicability\\\": \\\"Directly applicable — the fantasy writer pipeline needs the same audit trail for debugging, re-entry decisions, and delivery reporting.\\\",\\n        \\\"discoveredBy\\\": \\\"fractal-factory-exemplar-analyzer\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n        \\\"id\\\": \\\"PATTERN-008\\\",\\n        \\\"name\\\": \\\"per-agent-output-directory\\\",\\n        \\\"source\\\": \\\".fractal-factory/agents/\\\",\\n        \\\"category\\\": \\\"artifact\\\",\\n        \\\"description\\\": \\\"Each agent gets a dedicated directory: agents/{agent-name}/ containing status.json and output.md. Status.json is the routing contract (read by coordinators). Output.md is the detailed narrative (read only by the next specialist in the chain, never by coordinators). This separation keeps coordinator context small.\\\",\\n        \\\"applicability\\\": \\\"Directly applicable — fantasy writer agents need the same isolation. A chapter-drafter's output.md contains the actual chapter text; the drafting-coordinator only reads the status.json to know if drafting succeeded.\\\",\\n        \\\"discoveredBy\\\": \\\"fractal-factory-exemplar-analyzer\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n        \\\"id\\\": \\\"PATTERN-009\\\",\\n        \\\"name\\\": \\\"shared-accumulator-artifacts\\\",\\n        \\\"source\\\": \\\".fractals/fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory-invariant-extractor.agent.md\\\",\\n        \\\"category\\\": \\\"artifact\\\",\\n        \\\"description\\\": \\\"Domain knowledge accumulates in shared JSON files (domain-model.json, roster.json, architecture.json) using read-modify-write pattern. Each specialist reads the file, adds its section, preserves all existing data, and writes it back. The file grows richer as the pipeline progresses. No agent overwrites another agent's data.\\\",\\n        \\\"applicability\\\": \\\"Directly applicable — the fantasy writer needs shared accumulator artifacts: world-bible.json grows as geography-writer, magic-writer, politics-writer each add their sections. character-profiles.json grows as each character specialist adds their character. The read-modify-write discipline is critical.\\\",\\n        \\\"discoveredBy\\\": \\\"fractal-factory-exemplar-analyzer\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n        \\\"id\\\": \\\"PATTERN-010\\\",\\n        \\\"name\\\": \\\"universal-prompt-template\\\",\\n        \\\"source\\\": \\\".fractals/fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory-domain-scanner.agent.md\\\",\\n        \\\"category\\\": \\\"artifact\\\",\\n        \\\"description\\\": \\\"All agent prompts follow a universal structure: YAML frontmatter (description, model, name, user-invocable) → H1 title with role description → 'never use ask_questions' instruction → Context section → Inputs (numbered list) → Process (specialists) or Purity Rule (coordinators) or Pipeline Routing (orchestrator) → optional Anti-Laziness Rules → Write Rules → Status Contract with result codes.\\\",\\n        \\\"applicability\\\": \\\"Directly applicable — every fantasy writer agent prompt must follow this template. The Process section varies by role (creative writing steps for drafters, evaluation criteria for reviewers) but the structural skeleton is identical.\\\",\\n        \\\"discoveredBy\\\": \\\"fractal-factory-exemplar-analyzer\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n        \\\"id\\\": \\\"PATTERN-011\\\",\\n        \\\"name\\\": \\\"adversarial-anti-laziness-rules\\\",\\n        \\\"source\\\": \\\".fractals/fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory-prompt-reviewer.agent.md\\\",\\n        \\\"category\\\": \\\"anti-laziness\\\",\\n        \\\"description\\\": \\\"Reviewer and validator agents include an explicit 'Anti-Laziness Rules' section with 6-7 adversarial rules: (1) read every item cover-to-cover, (2) zero findings is suspicious — re-check, (3) provide specific evidence (exact quotes/citations), (4) minimum observation count ≥ items reviewed, (5) cross-reference against authoritative sources, (6) 'your work will be audited by the next agent'. This creates a chain of mutual accountability.\\\",\\n        \\\"applicability\\\": \\\"Directly applicable — critical for the fantasy writer's adversarial quality gates: continuity-auditor, pacing-auditor, genre-compliance-checker, beta-reader lenses all need anti-laziness rules. The 'zero issues is suspicious' rule is especially important for creative review where it's easy to rubber-stamp.\\\",\\n        \\\"discoveredBy\\\": \\\"fractal-factory-exemplar-analyzer\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n        \\\"id\\\": \\\"PATTERN-012\\\",\\n        \\\"name\\\": \\\"audit-chain-mutual-accountability\\\",\\n        \\\"source\\\": \\\".fractals/fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory-audit-oracle.agent.md\\\",\\n        \\\"category\\\": \\\"anti-laziness\\\",\\n        \\\"description\\\": \\\"Agents are arranged in an accountability chain: prompt-reviewer warns 'your reviews will be audited by checklist-validator and audit-oracle', checklist-validator warns 'your report will be audited by audit-oracle', audit-oracle warns 'your findings will be reviewed by gap-hunter'. Each agent is told the next agent will check its work, creating layered vigilance without centralized oversight.\\\",\\n        \\\"applicability\\\": \\\"Directly applicable — fantasy writer quality gates should form an accountability chain: chapter-reviewer warns 'your review will be checked by the continuity-auditor', continuity-auditor warns 'your audit will be checked by the beta-reading simulation'. This prevents shallow pass-through reviews.\\\",\\n        \\\"discoveredBy\\\": \\\"fractal-factory-exemplar-analyzer\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n        \\\"id\\\": \\\"PATTERN-013\\\",\\n        \\\"name\\\": \\\"eight-category-gap-search\\\",\\n        \\\"source\\\": \\\".fractals/fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory-gap-hunter.agent.md\\\",\\n        \\\"category\\\": \\\"convergence\\\",\\n        \\\"description\\\": \\\"Gap hunting uses 8 independent search categories (subdomain coverage, invariant enforcement, routing completeness, artifact coverage, test coverage, cross-reference integrity, bootstrap completeness, documentation completeness). Each category has documented methodology. Results include severity (critical/warning), specific evidence, and a suggested fix with re-entry target pass. Verdict is clean (zero gaps) or dirty (any gaps).\\\",\\n        \\\"applicability\\\": \\\"Adapt for fantasy writer — map to creative quality categories: plot-hole detection, character consistency, world-rule violations, pacing analysis, romance-beat coverage, fantasy-arc completeness, style consistency, continuity across chapters. Same clean/dirty verdict drives re-entry.\\\",\\n        \\\"discoveredBy\\\": \\\"fractal-factory-exemplar-analyzer\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n        \\\"id\\\": \\\"PATTERN-014\\\",\\n        \\\"name\\\": \\\"cycle-bounded-convergence\\\",\\n        \\\"source\\\": \\\".fractals/fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory.agent.md\\\",\\n        \\\"category\\\": \\\"convergence\\\",\\n        \\\"description\\\": \\\"Gap hunting operates with configurable maxCycles (from context.json options). Each cycle: gap-hunter searches → if dirty, orchestrator increments cycle counter, resets affected passes to pending, re-enters pipeline. If clean, proceed to delivery. If maxCycles reached, force-proceed to delivery with 'delivered-with-gaps' result. Previous cycle's gaps are re-checked in next cycle.\\\",\\n        \\\"applicability\\\": \\\"Directly applicable — the fantasy writer needs the same bounded convergence for revision cycles. Beta-reading finds issues → revision pass addresses them → re-read → if still issues and cycles < max, revise again. MaxCycles prevents infinite revision loops. 'Delivered-with-gaps' maps to 'published with known issues documented'.\\\",\\n        \\\"discoveredBy\\\": \\\"fractal-factory-exemplar-analyzer\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n        \\\"id\\\": \\\"PATTERN-015\\\",\\n        \\\"name\\\": \\\"result-code-vocabulary-tiers\\\",\\n        \\\"source\\\": \\\".fractals/fractal-factory/agents/\\\",\\n        \\\"category\\\": \\\"routing\\\",\\n        \\\"description\\\": \\\"Result codes follow a three-tier vocabulary: orchestrator uses outcome verbs (delivered, delivered-with-gaps, failed), coordinators use completion verbs (complete, blocked, complete-with-blocked), specialists use domain-specific past-tense verbs (scanned, extracted, analyzed, planned, written, approved, rejected, pass, fail, clean, dirty). This tiered vocabulary makes routing tables self-documenting.\\\",\\n        \\\"applicability\\\": \\\"Directly applicable — fantasy writer should use: orchestrator (published, published-with-issues, failed), phase coordinators (complete, blocked), specialists (drafted, revised, approved, needs-revision, consistent, inconsistent, resonant, flat).\\\",\\n        \\\"discoveredBy\\\": \\\"fractal-factory-exemplar-analyzer\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n        \\\"id\\\": \\\"PATTERN-016\\\",\\n        \\\"name\\\": \\\"prefix-role-naming-convention\\\",\\n        \\\"source\\\": \\\".fractals/fractal-factory/agents/\\\",\\n        \\\"category\\\": \\\"naming\\\",\\n        \\\"description\\\": \\\"All agents use {namingPrefix}-{role-slug} format with hyphen separation. Role slugs use domain-noun + action-suffix compounds: domain-scanner, invariant-extractor, prompt-writer, prompt-reviewer, roster-planner, checklist-validator, audit-oracle, gap-hunter. Coordinators always end in '-coordinator'. The guide always ends in '-guide'.\\\",\\n        \\\"applicability\\\": \\\"Directly applicable — fantasy writer agents should be: romantic-fantasy-writer-worldbuilding-coordinator, romantic-fantasy-writer-geography-writer, romantic-fantasy-writer-character-designer, romantic-fantasy-writer-continuity-auditor, etc.\\\",\\n        \\\"discoveredBy\\\": \\\"fractal-factory-exemplar-analyzer\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n        \\\"id\\\": \\\"PATTERN-017\\\",\\n        \\\"name\\\": \\\"role-suffix-taxonomy\\\",\\n        \\\"source\\\": \\\".fractals/fractal-factory/agents/\\\",\\n        \\\"category\\\": \\\"naming\\\",\\n        \\\"description\\\": \\\"Consistent role suffixes: -coordinator (pure router), -writer (content producer), -reviewer (adversarial evaluator), -planner (design/structure), -analyzer (analytical assessment), -auditor (compliance checking), -designer (creative design), -hunter (gap/issue finder), -oracle (wisdom/deep audit), -validator (checklist verification), -packager (assembly), -guide (user interface). Each suffix implies a specific behavioral contract.\\\",\\n        \\\"applicability\\\": \\\"Directly applicable — fantasy writer should map: -drafter (prose producer), -reviewer (creative quality), -auditor (consistency/continuity), -planner (structure design), -reader (beta-reading lens), -designer (character/world creative design), -calibrator (style/tone), -coordinator (phase routing).\\\",\\n        \\\"discoveredBy\\\": \\\"fractal-factory-exemplar-analyzer\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n        \\\"id\\\": \\\"PATTERN-018\\\",\\n        \\\"name\\\": \\\"sequential-specialist-chains\\\",\\n        \\\"source\\\": \\\".fractals/fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory-discovery-coordinator.agent.md\\\",\\n        \\\"category\\\": \\\"routing\\\",\\n        \\\"description\\\": \\\"Within a coordinator's scope, specialists execute in strict sequence where each reads the previous one's output via shared accumulator files. Discovery: scanner → extractor → auditor → analyzer. Analysis: pipeline-architect → artifact-designer → depth-analyzer. Planning: roster-planner → routing-planner → test-planner. Delivery: packager → documentation-writer → report-writer.\\\",\\n        \\\"applicability\\\": \\\"Directly applicable — fantasy writer phases need the same sequential chains: worldbuilding-coordinator dispatches geography-writer → magic-writer → politics-writer → culture-writer in sequence, each reading the accumulating world-bible.json.\\\",\\n        \\\"discoveredBy\\\": \\\"fractal-factory-exemplar-analyzer\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n        \\\"id\\\": \\\"PATTERN-019\\\",\\n        \\\"name\\\": \\\"context-json-driven-configuration\\\",\\n        \\\"source\\\": \\\".fractal-factory/context.json\\\",\\n        \\\"category\\\": \\\"artifact\\\",\\n        \\\"description\\\": \\\"A single context.json file drives the entire pipeline: domain metadata, input file paths, output directory, naming prefix, and configurable options (maxDepth, maxAgents, maxGapCycles, maxWriterReviewerRetries). Guide fills it once from user input; all agents read it for configuration. Separates pipeline configuration from pipeline state (progress.json).\\\",\\n        \\\"applicability\\\": \\\"Directly applicable — the fantasy writer needs a story-config.json (analogous to context.json) filled by the guide from user input: story idea, genre preferences, heat level, series info, style samples path, chapter count target, and quality options (maxRevisionCycles, maxBetaReadingPasses).\\\",\\n        \\\"discoveredBy\\\": \\\"fractal-factory-exemplar-analyzer\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n        \\\"id\\\": \\\"PATTERN-020\\\",\\n        \\\"name\\\": \\\"bottom-up-generation-order\\\",\\n        \\\"source\\\": \\\".fractals/fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory-prompt-writer.agent.md\\\",\\n        \\\"category\\\": \\\"hierarchy\\\",\\n        \\\"description\\\": \\\"When generating the agent family, specialists are written first, then coordinators, then the orchestrator. This ensures that when writing a coordinator's routing table, all its children's result codes already exist. When writing the orchestrator, all coordinator result codes exist. The inverse of the dispatch order (top-down dispatch, bottom-up generation).\\\",\\n        \\\"applicability\\\": \\\"Reference pattern — informs the fractal factory's generation order for the fantasy writer family. Specialists (chapter-drafter, geography-writer) are generated before their coordinators (drafting-coordinator, worldbuilding-coordinator), which are generated before the orchestrator.\\\",\\n        \\\"discoveredBy\\\": \\\"fractal-factory-exemplar-analyzer\\\"\\n    }\\n]\\n\\n# Update domain-model.json\\ndm['exemplarPatterns'] = patterns\\ndm['lastUpdated'] = '2026-03-15T19:35:00Z'\\n\\nwith open('.fractal-factory/domain-model.json', 'w') as f:\\n    json.dump(dm, f, indent=2)\\n\\nprint(f\\\"Updated domain-model.json with {len(patterns)} exemplar patterns\\\")\\nprint(f\\\"Total keys: {list(dm.keys())}\\\")\\nprint(f\\\"Subdomains: {len(dm['subdomains'])}, Invariants: {len(dm['invariants'])}, Assets: {len(dm['existingAssets'])}, Patterns: {len(dm['exemplarPatterns'])}\\\")\\nPYEOF\", \"description\": \"Update domain-model.json with patterns\", \"initial_wait\": 15}"
            }
          }
        ],
        "parsed": null
      }
