      traceState: undefined
    },
    kind: 0,
    parentSpanContext: {
      traceId: '4d0edfe3e53e3bed103999709b8eb8dd',
      spanId: 'dd1c612637db9038',
      traceFlags: 1,
      traceState: undefined
    },
    attributes: {
      'gen_ai.operation.name': 'execute_tool',
      'gen_ai.tool.name': 'bash',
      'gen_ai.tool.call.id': 'toolu_01Db8Ug7j7YqmLvw9ZCXscQS',
      'gen_ai.tool.type': 'function',
      'gen_ai.provider.name': 'github',
      'gen_ai.tool.call.arguments': `{"command":"cd /home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator && python3 << 'PYEOF'\\nimport json\\n\\n# Read existing domain-model.json\\nwith open('.fractal-factory/domain-model.json') as f:\\n    dm = json.load(f)\\n\\n# Define exemplar patterns\\npatterns = [\\n    {\\n        \\"id\\": \\"PATTERN-001\\",\\n        \\"name\\": \\"depth-3-pass-coordinators\\",\\n        \\"source\\": \\".fractals/fractal-factory/agents/\\",\\n        \\"category\\": \\"hierarchy\\",\\n        \\"description\\": \\"Three-tier hierarchy: guide → orchestrator → pass-coordinators → specialists. Each pipeline pass has exactly one coordinator that owns dispatch sequencing for 2-6 specialists. Coordinators never do substantive work (pure routing). Guide is the sole user-facing entry point, separate from the orchestrator.\\",\\n        \\"applicability\\": \\"Directly applicable — romantic fantasy writer needs the same pattern: guide (gathers story idea) → orchestrator (routes creative pipeline) → phase coordinators (concept, worldbuilding, characters, plotting, drafting, revision, beta-reading, polish) → specialist writers/reviewers per phase.\\",\\n        \\"discoveredBy\\": \\"fractal-factory-exemplar-analyzer\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n        \\"id\\": \\"PATTERN-002\\",\\n        \\"name\\": \\"pure-router-coordinators\\",\\n        \\"source\\": \\".fractals/fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory-discovery-coordinator.agent.md\\",\\n        \\"category\\": \\"routing\\",\\n        \\"description\\": \\"Coordinators are pure state machines: they read child status.json files, evaluate conditions, dispatch the next child, and write their own status. They NEVER read child output.md, never write domain artifacts, and never perform substantive work. All routing decisions are based solely on status.json result codes.\\",\\n        \\"applicability\\": \\"Directly applicable — all phase coordinators in the fantasy writer (e.g., worldbuilding-coordinator, drafting-coordinator) must follow this pure-router pattern. Keeps coordinator prompts small and routing logic deterministic.\\",\\n        \\"discoveredBy\\": \\"fractal-factory-exemplar-analyzer\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n        \\"id\\": \\"PATTERN-003\\",\\n        \\"name\\": \\"status-file-polling-routing\\",\\n        \\"source\\": \\".fractals/fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory-discovery-coordinator.agent.md\\",\\n        \\"category\\": \\"routing\\",\\n        \\"description\\": \\"Routing tables use three-column format: Read (which status.json) | Condition (result code check) | Action (dispatch agent or write own status). Missing status.json means agent hasn't run yet → dispatch it. Each result code maps to exactly one action. This creates a deterministic, re-entrant state machine.\\",\\n        \\"applicability\\": \\"Directly applicable — all coordinators and the orchestrator must use this Read|Condition|Action routing table format. Enables reliable re-entry after gap hunting cycles.\\",\\n        \\"discoveredBy\\": \\"fractal-factory-exemplar-analyzer\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n        \\"id\\": \\"PATTERN-004\\",\\n        \\"name\\": \\"writer-reviewer-loop-with-max-retries\\",\\n        \\"source\\": \\".fractals/fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory-execution-coordinator.agent.md\\",\\n        \\"category\\": \\"routing\\",\\n        \\"description\\": \\"Writer and reviewer agents form a feedback loop: writer produces content → reviewer evaluates → if rejected and iteration < maxRetries, re-dispatch writer with reviewer's feedback. If maxRetries exceeded, mark as blocked and proceed. Reviewer's output.md contains specific feedback for the writer's next iteration.\\",\\n        \\"applicability\\": \\"Directly applicable — the fantasy writer needs this pattern everywhere: chapter-drafter → chapter-reviewer, worldbuilding-writer → consistency-auditor, character-designer → character-auditor. MaxRetries prevents infinite loops while ensuring quality iteration.\\",\\n        \\"discoveredBy\\": \\"fractal-factory-exemplar-analyzer\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n        \\"id\\": \\"PATTERN-005\\",\\n        \\"name\\": \\"seven-pass-pipeline-with-re-entry\\",\\n        \\"source\\": \\".fractals/fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory.agent.md\\",\\n        \\"category\\": \\"hierarchy\\",\\n        \\"description\\": \\"Pipeline organized as 7 sequential passes: discovery → analysis → planning → execution → verification → gap-hunting → delivery. Gap-hunting can trigger re-entry to an earlier pass (analysis or planning) with cycle counting and forced termination after maxCycles. Progress tracked in progress.json with per-pass status (pending → active → completed).\\",\\n        \\"applicability\\": \\"Adapt for fantasy writer — map to creative pipeline passes: concept → worldbuilding → characters → plotting → style-calibration → drafting → revision → beta-reading → polish → delivery. Re-entry pattern from beta-reading back to revision is directly analogous to gap-hunting re-entry.\\",\\n        \\"discoveredBy\\": \\"fractal-factory-exemplar-analyzer\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n        \\"id\\": \\"PATTERN-006\\",\\n        \\"name\\": \\"universal-status-contract\\",\\n        \\"source\\": \\".fractals/fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory-domain-scanner.agent.md\\",\\n        \\"category\\": \\"artifact\\",\\n        \\"description\\": \\"Every agent writes status.json with exactly 8 fields: agent (name), task_id (pass/task slug), status (completed|failed), result (domain-specific verb), summary (human-readable 20-50 words), artifacts (list of produced file paths), next_hint (suggested next agent), iteration (integer counter). This uniform shape enables generic routing logic.\\",\\n        \\"applicability\\": \\"Directly applicable — every fantasy writer agent must produce status.json in this exact format. Enables coordinators to route without understanding domain content.\\",\\n        \\"discoveredBy\\": \\"fractal-factory-exemplar-analyzer\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n        \\"id\\": \\"PATTERN-007\\",\\n        \\"name\\": \\"manifest-prepend-audit-log\\",\\n        \\"source\\": \\".fractal-factory/manifest.json\\",\\n        \\"category\\": \\"artifact\\",\\n        \\"description\\": \\"Every agent prepends an entry to manifest.json (newest first) with: timestamp, agent name, artifacts list, status, result, iteration. Creates an immutable audit trail of all agent executions. The manifest is the single source of truth for what happened and when.\\",\\n        \\"applicability\\": \\"Directly applicable — the fantasy writer pipeline needs the same audit trail for debugging, re-entry decisions, and delivery reporting.\\",\\n        \\"discoveredBy\\": \\"fractal-factory-exemplar-analyzer\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n        \\"id\\": \\"PATTERN-008\\",\\n        \\"name\\": \\"per-agent-output-directory\\",\\n        \\"source\\": \\".fractal-factory/agents/\\",\\n        \\"category\\": \\"artifact\\",\\n        \\"description\\": \\"Each agent gets a dedicated directory: agents/{agent-name}/ containing status.json and output.md. Status.json is the routing contract (read by coordinators). Output.md is the detailed narrative (read only by the next specialist in the chain, never by coordinators). This separation keeps coordinator context small.\\",\\n        \\"applicability\\": \\"Directly applicable — fantasy writer agents need the same isolation. A chapter-drafter's output.md contains the actual chapter text; the drafting-coordinator only reads the status.json to know if drafting succeeded.\\",\\n        \\"discoveredBy\\": \\"fractal-factory-exemplar-analyzer\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n        \\"id\\": \\"PATTERN-009\\",\\n        \\"name\\": \\"shared-accumulator-artifacts\\",\\n        \\"source\\": \\".fractals/fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory-invariant-extractor.agent.md\\",\\n        \\"category\\": \\"artifact\\",\\n        \\"description\\": \\"Domain knowledge accumulates in shared JSON files (domain-model.json, roster.json, architecture.json) using read-modify-write pattern. Each specialist reads the file, adds its section, preserves all existing data, and writes it back. The file grows richer as the pipeline progresses. No agent overwrites another agent's data.\\",\\n        \\"applicability\\": \\"Directly applicable — the fantasy writer needs shared accumulator artifacts: world-bible.json grows as geography-writer, magic-writer, politics-writer each add their sections. character-profiles.json grows as each character specialist adds their character. The read-modify-write discipline is critical.\\",\\n        \\"discoveredBy\\": \\"fractal-factory-exemplar-analyzer\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n        \\"id\\": \\"PATTERN-010\\",\\n        \\"name\\": \\"universal-prompt-template\\",\\n        \\"source\\": \\".fractals/fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory-domain-scanner.agent.md\\",\\n        \\"category\\": \\"artifact\\",\\n        \\"description\\": \\"All agent prompts follow a universal structure: YAML frontmatter (description, model, name, user-invocable) → H1 title with role description → 'never use ask_questions' instruction → Context section → Inputs (numbered list) → Process (specialists) or Purity Rule (coordinators) or Pipeline Routing (orchestrator) → optional Anti-Laziness Rules → Write Rules → Status Contract with result codes.\\",\\n        \\"applicability\\": \\"Directly applicable — every fantasy writer agent prompt must follow this template. The Process section varies by role (creative writing steps for drafters, evaluation criteria for reviewers) but the structural skeleton is identical.\\",\\n        \\"discoveredBy\\": \\"fractal-factory-exemplar-analyzer\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n        \\"id\\": \\"PATTERN-011\\",\\n        \\"name\\": \\"adversarial-anti-laziness-rules\\",\\n        \\"source\\": \\".fractals/fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory-prompt-reviewer.agent.md\\",\\n        \\"category\\": \\"anti-laziness\\",\\n        \\"description\\": \\"Reviewer and validator agents include an explicit 'Anti-Laziness Rules' section with 6-7 adversarial rules: (1) read every item cover-to-cover, (2) zero findings is suspicious — re-check, (3) provide specific evidence (exact quotes/citations), (4) minimum observation count ≥ items reviewed, (5) cross-reference against authoritative sources, (6) 'your work will be audited by the next agent'. This creates a cha`... 10146 more characters,
