fractal-factory-depth-analyzer\\n      ├── fractal-factory-planning-coordinator\\n      │   ├── fractal-factory-roster-planner\\n      │   ├── fractal-factory-routing-planner\\n      │   └── fractal-factory-test-planner\\n      ├── fractal-factory-execution-coordinator\\n      │   ├── fractal-factory-prompt-writer ↔ fractal-factory-prompt-reviewer (loop)\\n      │   └── fractal-factory-infra-writer\\n      ├── fractal-factory-verification-coordinator\\n      │   ├── fractal-factory-checklist-validator\\n      │   └── fractal-factory-audit-oracle\\n      ├── fractal-factory-gap-hunting-coordinator\\n      │   └── fractal-factory-gap-hunter\\n      └── fractal-factory-delivery-coordinator\\n          ├── fractal-factory-packager\\n          ├── fractal-factory-documentation-writer\\n          └── fractal-factory-report-writer\\n```\\n\\n**Pipeline**: 7 sequential passes with re-entry from gap hunting:\\n```\\nPass 1: Discovery → domain-scanner → invariant-extractor → asset-auditor → exemplar-analyzer\\nPass 2: Analysis → pipeline-architect → artifact-designer → depth-analyzer\\nPass 3: Planning → roster-planner → routing-planner → test-planner\\nPass 4: Execution → prompt-writer ↔ prompt-reviewer (loop, max 3 retries) → infra-writer\\nPass 5: Verification → checklist-validator → audit-oracle\\nPass 6: Gap Hunting → gap-hunter (8-category search → clean/dirty verdict)\\n    └─ if dirty AND cycles < maxCycles → re-enter Pass 2 or 3\\n    └─ if clean → proceed to Pass 7\\n    └─ if cycles >= maxCycles → force-proceed to Pass 7\\nPass 7: Delivery → packager → documentation-writer → report-writer\\n```\\n\\n### Ralph Profiles (Supplementary Exemplar)\\n\\n**Directories**: `profiles/ralph-docs/` (25 agents), `profiles/ralph-vscode/` (16 agents)\\n\\n**Key patterns observed**:\\n- Variant-based routing in `profile.json` (match task metadata → select agent stages)\\n- Parallel multi-model review (6 reviewers dispatched simultaneously in ralph-docs)\\n- Per-task artifact isolation (`.ralph/tasks/{taskId}/artifacts/{agent}/`)\\n- Skill injection (domain skills loaded per-stage from shared skills library)\\n- Pure orchestrator purity (reads only status.json, never output.md)\\n\\n## Extracted Patterns Table\\n\\n| ID | Name | Category | Source | Applicability |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| PATTERN-001 | depth-3-pass-coordinators | hierarchy | fractal-factory | **Direct** — map to creative pipeline phases |\\n| PATTERN-002 | pure-router-coordinators | routing | fractal-factory | **Direct** — all phase coordinators must be pure routers |\\n| PATTERN-003 | status-file-polling-routing | routing | fractal-factory | **Direct** — Read\\\\|Condition\\\\|Action format |\\n| PATTERN-004 | writer-reviewer-loop-with-max-retries | routing | fractal-factory | **Direct** — drafter↔reviewer loops everywhere |\\n| PATTERN-005 | seven-pass-pipeline-with-re-entry | hierarchy | fractal-factory | **Adapt** — map 7 passes to ~10 creative phases |\\n| PATTERN-006 | universal-status-contract | artifact | fractal-factory | **Direct** — 8-field status.json for all agents |\\n| PATTERN-007 | manifest-prepend-audit-log | artifact | fractal-factory | **Direct** — execution audit trail |\\n| PATTERN-008 | per-agent-output-directory | artifact | fractal-factory | **Direct** — agents/{name}/status.json + output.md |\\n| PATTERN-009 | shared-accumulator-artifacts | artifact | fractal-factory | **Direct** — world-bible.json, character-profiles.json |\\n| PATTERN-010 | universal-prompt-template | artifact | fractal-factory | **Direct** — frontmatter → Context → Inputs → Process → Write Rules → Status |\\n| PATTERN-011 | adversarial-anti-laziness-rules | anti-laziness | fractal-factory | **Direct** — critical for quality gate agents |\\n| PATTERN-012 | audit-chain-mutual-accountability | anti-laziness | fractal-factory | **Direct** — chain of reviewer accountability |\\n| PATTERN-013 | eight-category-gap-search | convergence | fractal-factory | **Adapt** — map to creative quality categories |\\n| PATTERN-014 | cycle-bounded-convergence | convergence | fractal-factory | **Direct** — maxRevisionCycles with forced completion |\\n| PATTERN-015 | result-code-vocabulary-tiers | routing | fractal-factory | **Direct** — orchestrator/coordinator/specialist verb tiers |\\n| PATTERN-016 | prefix-role-naming-convention | naming | fractal-factory | **Direct** — {prefix}-{domain-noun}-{action-suffix} |\\n| PATTERN-017 | role-suffix-taxonomy | naming | fractal-factory | **Direct** — -coordinator, -writer, -reviewer, -auditor, etc. |\\n| PATTERN-018 | sequential-specialist-chains | routing | fractal-factory | **Direct** — ordered dispatch within coordinator scope |\\n| PATTERN-019 | context-json-driven-configuration | artifact | fractal-factory | **Direct** — story-config.json analogous to context.json |\\n| PATTERN-020 | bottom-up-generation-order | hierarchy | fractal-factory | **Reference** — informs fractal factory's generation order |\\n\\n## Recommended Patterns for Adoption\\n\\n### Must Adopt (Critical Infrastructure)\\n- **PATTERN-001** (depth-3 hierarchy): The romantic fantasy writer needs coordinators for each creative phase. Without this structure, the orchestrator prompt would be enormous.\\n- **PATTERN-002** (pure-router coordinators): Essential for keeping coordinator prompts small. A drafting-coordinator doesn't need to understand prose — just dispatch and route.\\n- **PATTERN-003** (status-file polling): The routing mechanism that makes the entire system re-entrant and debuggable.\\n- **PATTERN-006** (universal status contract): Uniform 8-field contract enables generic coordinator logic.\\n- **PATTERN-010** (universal prompt template): Consistent prompt structure makes the system maintainable.\\n\\n### Must Adopt (Quality Assurance)\\n- **PATTERN-004** (writer-reviewer loops): Creative writing demands iterative refinement. Chapter drafts must go through reviewer loops with max retries.\\n- **PATTERN-011** (anti-laziness rules): Absolutely critical for creative quality gates. Without these, reviewers will rubber-stamp prose.\\n- **PATTERN-012** (audit chain accountability): The layered \\\"your work will be checked\\\" pattern prevents shallow reviews across the entire quality pipeline.\\n- **PATTERN-014** (cycle-bounded convergence): Revision cycles must have a maximum to prevent infinite rewriting.\\n\\n### Must Adopt (Artifact Management)\\n- **PATTERN-008** (per-agent output directories): Isolates chapter drafts, world bible sections, character profiles.\\n- **PATTERN-009** (shared accumulator artifacts): The world-bible must grow as multiple specialists contribute. Read-modify-write discipline is critical.\\n- **PATTERN-019** (context-driven configuration): Story parameters (genre, heat level, series info) drive the entire pipeline.\\n\\n### Should Adapt\\n- **PATTERN-005** (pipeline passes): The fractal factory's 7 passes map to ~10 creative phases. The re-entry mechanism maps to revision cycles triggered by beta-reading.\\n- **PATTERN-013** (gap search categories): Map the 8 technical categories to creative quality categories: plot holes, character consistency, world-rule violations, pacing, romance beats, fantasy arc, style consistency, continuity.\\n- **PATTERN-015** (result code vocabulary): Orchestrator uses (published, published-with-issues, failed), coordinators use (complete, blocked), specialists use creative verbs (drafted, revised, approved, needs-revision, consistent, inconsistent).\\n- **PATTERN-017** (role suffix taxonomy): Adapt suffixes for creative domain: -drafter, -reader (beta lens), -calibrator (style/tone), alongside standard -reviewer, -auditor, -coordinator.\\n\\n## Patterns Considered but Not Extracted\\n\\n| Pattern | Why Rejected |\\n|---|---|\\n| Docker/compose patterns from ralph-profiles | Infrastructure-specific, not applicable to the produced agent system's prompt design |\\n| JIRA/ADO integration from ralph-profiles | Task management patterns are specific to the development workflow, not creative writing |\\n| MCP server sidecar configuration | Deployment infrastructure, not prompt/workflow design |\\n| Variant-based routing from profile.json | The fantasy writer has a single workflow, not multiple task-type variants |\\n| Parallel multi-model review panel from ralph-docs | Worth noting but the fantasy writer's beta-reading lenses are better modeled as sequential specialized readers than parallel identical reviewers with different models |\\n| Git commit message conventions | Source control patterns not relevant to creative pipeline |\\n\\n## Key Analogies for the Produced System\\n\\nThe fractal factory's pipeline maps to the romantic fantasy writer as follows:\\n\\n| Fractal Factory Phase | Fantasy Writer Analog | Key Similarity |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Discovery (scan domain) | Concept Development (distill story idea) | Both extract structured data from unstructured input |\\n| Analysis (design architecture) | Worldbuilding + Character Design | Both construct structured artifacts from domain knowledge |\\n| Planning (roster + routing) | Plot Architecture | Both create the execution plan for later phases |\\n| Execution (write + review loop) | Chapter Drafting + Revision | Both produce content through iterative writer↔reviewer cycles |\\n| Verification (checklist + audit) | Beta Reading Simulation | Both evaluate output against quality criteria |\\n| Gap Hunting (find issues → re-enter) | Revision from Beta Feedback | Both identify gaps and trigger re-entry to earlier phases |\\n| Delivery (package + document) | Polish + Final Delivery | Both assemble, document, and deliver the final product |\\n\\nThis structural isomorphism means the fractal factory patterns transfer almost directly to the fantasy writer domain, with the main adaptation being domain-specific content in specialist agents.\\n\"}"
