    attributes: {
      'gen_ai.operation.name': 'execute_tool',
      'gen_ai.tool.name': 'bash',
      'gen_ai.tool.call.id': 'toolu_01S1N2r3N5Z2RA3rnE2aX91q',
      'gen_ai.tool.type': 'function',
      'gen_ai.provider.name': 'github',
      'gen_ai.tool.call.arguments': `{"command":"cd /home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator && wc -l .fractal-factory/domain-brief.md && sed -n '300,600p' .fractal-factory/domain-brief.md","description":"Read domain brief middle section","initial_wait":10}`,
      'gen_ai.tool.call.result': '415 .fractal-factory/domain-brief.md\n' +
        '        ch-01.md ... ch-N.md\n' +
        '      final/\n' +
        '        ch-01.md ... ch-N.md\n' +
        '    continuity/\n' +
        '      tracker.md                 ← Running facts, positions, timeline\n' +
        '      knowledge-matrix.md        ← What each character knows at each chapter boundary\n' +
        "      promises.md                ← Reader promises (Chekhov's guns) — planted, status\n" +
        '    revision/\n' +
        '      developmental/\n' +
        '        ch-01.md ... ch-N.md     ← Per-chapter developmental edit findings\n' +
        '      line-edit/\n' +
        '        ch-01.md ... ch-N.md\n' +
        '      copy-edit/\n' +
        '        ch-01.md ... ch-N.md\n' +
        '      revision-log.md            ← Traceability: every change → what finding prompted it\n' +
        '    beta-feedback/\n' +
        '      romance-reader.md\n' +
        '      fantasy-reader.md\n' +
        '      craft-reader.md\n' +
        '      sensitivity-reader.md\n' +
        '      originality-reader.md\n' +
        '      synthesis.md               ← Combined findings, prioritized by severity\n' +
        '    killed-darlings.md           ← Removed-but-saved passages, world details, plot elements\n' +
        '    book-summary.md              ← Post-completion: plot summary, arc outcomes, state changes\n' +
        '  book-2/\n' +
        '    ...\n' +
        '```\n' +
        '\n' +
        '**Subcategory rules:**\n' +
        '- Artifacts with more than ~3 distinct topics MUST be split into subcategory files within a typed directory. A single `world-bible.md` covering geography, magic, politics, culture, and history is too coarse.\n' +
        "- Each subcategory file should be self-contained enough to be loaded independently. An agent checking magic rules shouldn't need to load geography.\n" +
        '- Cross-references between subcategories use relative paths (`../characters/leads/kael.md`), never vague prose references ("see the character bible").\n' +
        '- The series-level directories define the canonical schema. Per-book directories mirror the same structure but contain only new or changed entries for that book.\n' +
        '- At book completion, new per-book entries are **promoted** into the series-level directories (merged, not moved — the book retains its copy for isolation).\n' +
        '\n' +
        '### Sequel Input Contract\n' +
        '\n' +
        'When producing a sequel, the system receives:\n' +
        '1. **All standard inputs** (story idea, optional style samples, etc.) — scoped to the new book\n' +
        '2. **The series knowledge base** (`series/`) — this is the canonical cross-book state. The new book MUST be consistent with everything in it.\n' +
        '3. **Previous book summaries** (`book-N/book-summary.md`) — for narrative context without re-reading full manuscripts\n' +
        '4. **Unresolved threads** (`series/unresolved-threads.md`) — the sequel concept phase MUST decide which threads this book resolves, advances, or deliberately leaves open. No thread may be silently forgotten.\n' +
        '\n' +
        "The sequel does NOT need to re-read prior books' raw chapters — the series knowledge base and summaries are sufficient.\n" +
        '\n' +
        '### Series Knowledge Base Lifecycle\n' +
        '\n' +
        '1. **Book 1 (standalone)**: Per-book artifacts are created as usual. On completion, the book-summary agent extracts canonical facts into the `series/` directory. Even a "standalone" gets this treatment — it\'s cheap insurance.\n' +
        "2. **Book N (sequel)**: The concept phase loads the series knowledge base. All phases cross-reference against it. On completion, the book-summary agent **merges** this book's new facts into the series knowledge base:\n" +
        '   - New characters → added to `character-registry.md`\n' +
        '   - Changed character states (injuries, alliances, deaths) → updated in registry\n' +
        '   - New world facts → merged into `world-bible.md`\n' +
        '   - Magic system expansion → merged into `magic-system.md` (must not contradict existing rules)\n' +
        '   - Resolved threads → moved from `unresolved-threads.md` to the book summary\n' +
        '   - New threads planted → added to `unresolved-threads.md` with the book they were planted in\n' +
        '   - Timeline events → appended to `timeline.md`\n' +
        '\n' +
        '### Cross-Book Consistency Rules\n' +
        '\n' +
        '- The series knowledge base is **append-mostly**. Facts established in book 1 cannot be silently contradicted in book 2. If a retcon is needed, it must be narratively justified (unreliable narrator revealed, new information discovered by characters) and explicitly documented.\n' +
        "- Character voice guides carry across books. A character's voice in book 3 should be recognizably the same person as book 1, with natural evolution (trauma, growth, age) documented.\n" +
        '- The magic system can be *expanded* but not *contradicted*. New abilities must be compatible with established rules.\n' +
        '- The naming convention guide prevents naming collisions (two characters with similar names across books) and ensures consistent use of titles, honorifics, and place names.\n' +
        '\n' +
        '## Craft Toolbox Selection\n' +
        '\n' +
        'During the **Concept** and **Plotting** phases, the system must produce a **Story Craft Profile** (`story-craft-profile.md`) that lists:\n' +
        '- Which tools from the Craft Toolbox (see invariants.md Part 2) are selected for this story\n' +
        '- Why each tool was selected (one sentence)\n' +
        '- Any tools explicitly NOT selected and why (brief)\n' +
        '- Any per-tool adjustments for this story (e.g., "T1 Scene-Sequel: applied to action/plot scenes; relaxed for romantic interludes")\n' +
        '\n' +
        'The adversarial auditors for all subsequent phases verify against the **selected** toolset, not the full toolbox. This ensures craft standards are applied with artistic judgment rather than mechanical rigidity.\n' +
        '\n' +
        '## Output Artifacts\n' +
        '\n' +
        'The system produces per-book and series-level artifacts, each decomposed into subcategory files.\n' +
        '\n' +
        '### Per-Book Artifact Directories\n' +
        '1. **`concept/`** — premise, craft profile, constraints\n' +
        "2. **`world/`** — this book's worldbuilding additions (geography, magic, politics, culture, history, flora/fauna — mirroring series structure)\n" +
        "3. **`characters/`** — this book's character work + per-character arc plans and outcomes\n" +
        '4. **`outline/`** — structural framework, per-chapter outlines, tension map, subplot tracker\n' +
        '5. **`style/`** — prose style guide, tone palette, reference analysis\n' +
        '6. **`chapters/drafts/`** — draft chapters, one file per chapter\n' +
        '7. **`chapters/final/`** — polished final chapters\n' +
        '8. **`continuity/`** — running tracker, character knowledge matrix, reader promises\n' +
        '9. **`revision/`** — per-chapter findings by pass type (developmental, line-edit, copy-edit) + revision log\n' +
        '10. **`beta-feedback/`** — per-lens findings (romance, fantasy, craft, sensitivity, originality) + synthesis\n' +
        '11. **`killed-darlings.md`** — removed-but-saved passages, world details, plot elements\n' +
        '12. **`book-summary.md`** — post-completion: plot summary, arc outcomes, state changes for series knowledge base\n' +
        '\n' +
        '### Series-Level Artifact Directories (accumulated across books)\n' +
        '13. **`series/world/`** — canonical worldbuilding (geography, magic, politics, culture, history, flora/fauna subdirectories)\n' +
        '14. **`series/characters/`** — all characters (leads, supporting, antagonists, voice guides, registry index, relationship map)\n' +
        '15. **`series/magic-system.md`** — high-level magic summary + links to `world/magic/` details\n' +
        '16. **`series/timeline.md`** — cross-book chronological events\n' +
        "17. **`series/unresolved-threads.md`** — planted Chekhov's guns not yet fired, tagged by origin book\n" +
        '18. **`series/naming-conventions.md`** — established names, places, terms, honorifics\n' +
        '19. **`series/style-guide.md`** — prose style continuity across books\n' +
        '\n' +
        '## Quality Expectations\n' +
        '\n' +
        '- **Prose quality**: Publication-ready romantic fantasy prose — lush but not purple, emotionally resonant, genre-appropriate\n' +
        '- **Character depth**: Leads must feel like real people with complex inner lives, not archetypes\n' +
        '- **Romance satisfaction**: The relationship arc must feel earned — genuine tension, genuine vulnerability, genuine payoff\n' +
        '- **Worldbuilding coherence**: Every magical, political, and cultural detail must be internally consistent\n' +
        '- **Pacing**: Chapters should flow naturally with varied tension, avoiding both the "sagging middle" and rushed endings\n' +
        '- **Voice distinctness**: Each POV character must have a recognizably different internal voice\n' +
        '\n' +
        '## Non-Goals\n' +
        '\n' +
        '- The system does NOT need to handle cover design, ISBN assignment, or publishing logistics\n' +
        '- The system does NOT need to market or promote the fiction\n' +
        '- The system does NOT generate illustrations or visual art (textual descriptions only)\n' +
        '- The system does NOT need to handle multiple simultaneous stories — one story at a time\n' +
        '<exited with exit code 0>'
