        '\n' +
        'PATTERN-004:\n' +
        "  Writer and reviewer agents form a feedback loop: writer produces content → reviewer evaluates → if rejected and iteration < maxRetries, re-dispatch writer with reviewer's feedback. If maxRetries exceeded, mark as blocked and proceed. Reviewer's output.md contains specific feedback for the writer's next iteration.\n" +
        '  Source: .fractals/fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory-execution-coordinator.agent.md\n' +
        '\n' +
        'PATTERN-005:\n' +
        '  Pipeline organized as 7 sequential passes: discovery → analysis → planning → execution → verification → gap-hunting → delivery. Gap-hunting can trigger re-entry to an earlier pass (analysis or planning) with cycle counting and forced termination after maxCycles. Progress tracked in progress.json with per-pass status (pending → active → completed).\n' +
        '  Source: .fractals/fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory.agent.md\n' +
        '\n' +
        'PATTERN-006:\n' +
        '  Every agent writes status.json with exactly 8 fields: agent (name), task_id (pass/task slug), status (completed|failed), result (domain-specific verb), summary (human-readable 20-50 words), artifacts (list of produced file paths), next_hint (suggested next agent), iteration (integer counter). This uniform shape enables generic routing logic.\n' +
        '  Source: .fractals/fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory-domain-scanner.agent.md\n' +
        '\n' +
        'PATTERN-007:\n' +
        '  Every agent prepends an entry to manifest.json (newest first) with: timestamp, agent name, artifacts list, status, result, iteration. Creates an immutable audit trail of all agent executions. The manifest is the single source of truth for what happened and when.\n' +
        '  Source: .fractal-factory/manifest.json\n' +
        '\n' +
        'PATTERN-008:\n' +
        '  Each agent gets a dedicated directory: agents/{agent-name}/ containing status.json and output.md. Status.json is the routing contract (read by coordinators). Output.md is the detailed narrative (read only by the next specialist in the chain, never by coordinators). This separation keeps coordinator context small.\n' +
        '  Source: .fractal-factory/agents/\n' +
        '\n' +
        'PATTERN-009:\n' +
        "  Domain knowledge accumulates in shared JSON files (domain-model.json, roster.json, architecture.json) using read-modify-write pattern. Each specialist reads the file, adds its section, preserves all existing data, and writes it back. The file grows richer as the pipeline progresses. No agent overwrites another agent's data.\n" +
        '  Source: .fractals/fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory-invariant-extractor.agent.md\n' +
        '\n' +
        'PATTERN-010:\n' +
        "  All agent prompts follow a universal structure: YAML frontmatter (description, model, name, user-invocable) → H1 title with role description → 'never use ask_questions' instruction → Context section → Inputs (numbered list) → Process (specialists) or Purity Rule (coordinators) or Pipeline Routing (orchestrator) → optional Anti-Laziness Rules → Write Rules → Status Contract with result codes.\n" +
        '  Source: .fractals/fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory-domain-scanner.agent.md\n' +
        '\n' +
        'PATTERN-011:\n' +
        "  Reviewer and validator agents include an explicit 'Anti-Laziness Rules' section with 6-7 adversarial rules: (1) read every item cover-to-cover, (2) zero findings is suspicious — re-check, (3) provide specific evidence (exact quotes/citations), (4) minimum observation count ≥ items reviewed, (5) cross-reference against authoritative sources, (6) 'your work will be audited by the next agent'. This creates a chain of mutual accountability.\n" +
        '  Source: .fractals/fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory-prompt-reviewer.agent.md\n' +
