              "name": "create",
              "arguments": "{\"path\": \"/home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator/.fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory-artifact-designer/output.md\", \"file_text\": \"# Artifact Designer Output — romantic-fantasy-writer\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nDesigned **34 shared artifacts** (4 universal + 30 domain-specific) for the romantic-fantasy-writer agent family. The artifact layer covers all 9 creative pipeline phases plus 2 cross-cutting accumulator systems, with 5 multi-writer contracts and 23 data-flow edges verified acyclic.\\n\\n## Artifact Inventory\\n\\n### Universal Artifacts (4)\\n\\n| # | Artifact | Purpose | Writers | Readers | Protocol |\\n|---|----------|---------|---------|---------|----------|\\n| U1 | `story-config.json` | User inputs, premise, constraints, series position (INV-048, INV-050) | guide | all agents | create-once |\\n| U2 | `progress.json` | Pipeline state: current phase, completion status, cycle counts | orchestrator | orchestrator, coordinators, guide | read-modify-write |\\n| U3 | `manifest.json` | Immutable audit trail, prepend-only (newest first) | all agents | polish-delivery-coordinator, guide | prepend-only |\\n| U4 | `agents/*/status.json` | Per-agent 8-field routing signal (PATTERN-006) | each agent (own) | parent coordinator | create-once-per-iteration |\\n\\n### Phase 1: Concept Development (2 artifacts)\\n\\n| # | Artifact | Purpose | Writers | Protocol |\\n|---|----------|---------|---------|----------|\\n| D1 | `story-concept.json` | Crystallized concept: genre promise, dual-arc, world seed, tone, scope (INV-001, INV-030) | concept-writer | create-once |\\n| D2 | `story-craft-profile.json` | Selected craft tools T1-T14 (5-8 per story), two-tier quality system (INV-032, INV-063) | concept-writer | create-once |\\n\\n### Phase 2: World Building (6 artifacts — subcategorized per INV-031, INV-055)\\n\\n| # | Artifact | Purpose | Writers | Protocol |\\n|---|----------|---------|---------|----------|\\n| D3 | `world-bible/geography.json` | Locations, terrain, climate, travel routes (LOC-NNN) | world-writer | create-once |\\n| D4 | `world-bible/magic-system.json` | Rules, costs, limitations, abilities, Sanderson's Law (MAG-NNN) (INV-009) | world-writer | create-once |\\n| D5 | `world-bible/politics.json` | Factions, governance, conflicts, treaties (FAC-NNN) | world-writer | create-once |\\n| D6 | `world-bible/culture.json` | Customs, religions, naming conventions, social hierarchy (CUL-NNN) (INV-058) | world-writer | create-once |\\n| D7 | `world-bible/history.json` | Timeline, eras, founding myths, historical figures (HIST-NNN) | world-writer | create-once |\\n| D8 | `world-bible/flora-fauna.json` | Creatures, plants, ecosystems (CREAT-NNN, PLANT-NNN) | world-writer | create-once |\\n\\n### Phase 3: Character Design (2 artifact patterns)\\n\\n| # | Artifact | Purpose | Writers | Protocol |\\n|---|----------|---------|---------|----------|\\n| D9 | `characters/cast-index.json` | Master character index, relationships, naming registry, voice matrix (CHAR-NNN) (INV-003, INV-058) | character-writer | create-once |\\n| D10 | `characters/{character-slug}.json` | Individual character profile: backstory, psychology, arc, voice guide, knowledge boundary (INV-003, INV-008, INV-022) | character-writer | create-once |\\n\\n### Phase 4: Plot Architecture (4 artifacts)\\n\\n| # | Artifact | Purpose | Writers | Protocol |\\n|---|----------|---------|---------|----------|\\n| D11 | `plot/structure-framework.json` | Story structure + dual-arc overlay, act breaks, black moment (FBEAT/RBEAT-NNN) (INV-021, T7, T12) | plot-writer | create-once |\\n| D12 | `plot/chapter-outlines.json` | Per-chapter outline: POV, scenes, beats, Chekhov items (CH-NNN, SCN-NNN) (INV-010) | plot-writer | create-once |\\n| D13 | `plot/tension-map.json` | Tension rise-fall per chapter, pacing validation, stakes escalation (INV-020, T6, T13) | plot-writer | create-once |\\n| D14 | `plot/subplot-tracker.json` | All subplots with status, characters, resolution tracking (SUB-NNN) | plot-writer | create-once |\\n\\n### Phase 5: Prose Style Development (1 artifact)\\n\\n| # | Artifact | Purpose | Writers | Protocol |\\n|---|----------|---------|---------|----------|\\n| D15 | `style-guide.json` | Voice, tone, vocabulary, sentence rhythm, POV variations, reference analysis (INV-005, INV-017, INV-018, INV-019, INV-024) | style-analyst | create-once |\\n\\n### Phase 6: Chapter Drafting (2 artifact patterns)\\n\\n| # | Artifact | Purpose | Writers | Protocol |\\n|---|----------|---------|---------|----------|\\n| D16 | `chapters/chapter-{NNN}.md` | Individual chapter prose, one file per chapter (INV-012) | chapter-drafter → revision agents → polish-agent | create-once-then-revise |\\n| D17 | `chapters/chapter-{NNN}-metadata.json` | Chapter metadata: scenes, word count, craft compliance, revision status | chapter-drafter + all editors | **read-modify-write** (multi-writer) |\\n\\n### Cross-Cutting: Continuity Tracking (1 artifact)\\n\\n| # | Artifact | Purpose | Writers | Protocol |\\n|---|----------|---------|---------|----------|\\n| D18 | `continuity-tracker.json` | Running continuity state: timeline, positions, knowledge matrix, Chekhov registry, established facts (INV-011, INV-016) | continuity-tracker | **read-modify-write** (accumulator) |\\n\\n### Cross-Cutting: Series Knowledge Base (1 artifact)\\n\\n| # | Artifact | Purpose | Writers | Protocol |\\n|---|----------|---------|---------|----------|\\n| D19 | `series-knowledge-base.json` | Series-level canon, character evolution, world evolution, naming registry, retcon log (INV-049, INV-051, INV-056, INV-058) | series-kb-manager | **read-modify-write** (accumulator) |\\n\\n### Phase 7: Revision (3 artifacts)\\n\\n| # | Artifact | Purpose | Writers | Protocol |\\n|---|----------|---------|---------|----------|\\n| D20 | `revision/developmental-findings.json` | Plot holes, pacing, character consistency, structural issues (DEV-NNN) (INV-014) | developmental-editor | create-once |\\n| D21 | `revision/line-edit-findings.json` | Prose quality, voice, show-dont-tell, dialogue, clichés (LINE-NNN) (INV-003, INV-005, INV-017) | line-editor | create-once |\\n| D22 | `revision/copy-edit-findings.json` | Grammar, spelling, formatting, proper nouns, factual consistency (COPY-NNN) | copy-editor | create-once |\\n\\n### Phase 8: Beta Reading (6 artifacts — 5 parallel lenses + synthesis)\\n\\n| # | Artifact | Purpose | Writers | Protocol |\\n|---|----------|---------|---------|----------|\\n| D23 | `beta-reading/romance-lens.json` | Romance reader: chemistry, emotional resonance, HFN/HEA (BR-NNN) (INV-053) | romance-beta-reader | create-once |\\n| D24 | `beta-reading/fantasy-lens.json` | Fantasy reader: world immersion, magic coherence, plot engagement (BF-NNN) (INV-053) | fantasy-beta-reader | create-once |\\n| D25 | `beta-reading/craft-lens.json` | Craft reader: prose quality, structure, craft tool compliance (BC-NNN) (INV-053) | craft-beta-reader | create-once |\\n| D26 | `beta-reading/sensitivity-lens.json` | Sensitivity reader: representation, consent, power dynamics (BS-NNN) (INV-053) | sensitivity-beta-reader | create-once |\\n| D27 | `beta-reading/originality-lens.json` | Originality checker: plagiarism, derivative passages, cliché structures (BO-NNN) (INV-023, INV-024, INV-025) | originality-beta-reader | create-once |\\n| D28 | `beta-reading/synthesis.json` | Aggregated findings, cross-lens conflicts, go/no-go verdict (BETA-NNN) (INV-054) | beta-synthesis-agent | create-once |\\n\\n### Phase 9: Polish & Delivery (2 artifacts)\\n\\n| # | Artifact | Purpose | Writers | Protocol |\\n|---|----------|---------|---------|----------|\\n| D29 | `delivery/chapter-summaries.json` | One-paragraph summary per chapter for series KB and reference | polish-agent | create-once |\\n| D30 | `delivery/book-metadata.json` | Final book metadata: title, blurb, word count, quality scores, production metrics | polish-agent | create-once |\\n\\n## Data Flow Diagram\\n\\n```\\n                    ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\\n                    │                  SERIES KB (sequel)                  │\\n                    │           series-knowledge-base.json                 │\\n                    └──────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────┘\\n                                       │ (loaded for sequels)\\n                                       ▼\\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\\n│ PHASE 1: CONCEPT                                                            │\\n│   story-concept.json ──────────────────────────────────────────────────┐    │\\n│   story-craft-profile.json ────────────────────────────────────────┐   │    │\\n└──────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────────────┬──┼───┘    │\\n               │                                                  │  │        │\\n               ▼                                                  │  │        │\\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────┐               │  │        │\\n│ PHASE 2: WORLD BUILDING                         │               │  │        │\\n│   world-bible/geography.json                    │               │  │        │\\n│   world-bible/magic-system.json                 │               │  │        │\\n│   world-bible/politics.json        ─────────────┼───────────┐   │  │        │\\n│   world-bible/culture.json                      │           │   │  │        │\\n│   world-bible/history.json                      │           │   │  │        │\\n│   world-bible/flora-fauna.json                  │           │   │  │        │\\n└──────────────┬──────────────────────────────────┘           │   │  │        │\\n               │                                              │   │  │        │\\n               ▼                                              │   │  │        │\\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────┐           │   │  │        │\\n│ PHASE 3: CHARACTER DESIGN                       │           │   │  │        │\\n│   characters/cast-index.json     ───────────────┼───────┐   │   │  │        │\\n│   characters/{character-slug}.json              │       │   │   │  │        │\\n└──────────────┬──────────────────────────────────┘       │   │   │  │        │\\n               │                                          ▼   ▼   ▼  │        │\\n               │                              ┌───────────────────────┼────┐   │\\n               │                              │ PHASE 4: PLOT ARCH    │    │   │\\n               └──────────────────────────────▶  plot/structure-framework  │   │\\n                                              │  plot/chapter-outlines ───┐│   │\\n                                              │  plot/tension-map ─────┐ ││   │\\n                                              │  plot/subplot-tracker  │ ││   │\\n                                              └────────────────────┬───┘ ││   │\\n                                                                   │     ││   │\\n                                                                   ▼     ▼▼   │\\n                                              ┌───────────────────────────┐   │\\n                                              │ PHASE 5: PROSE STYLE      │   │\\n                                              │   style-guide.json ───┐   │   │\\n                                              └───────────────────────┼───┘   │\\n                                                                      │       │\\n                                    ┌─────────────────────────────────┼───────┘\\n                                    │  All pre-production artifacts   │\\n                                    ▼                                 ▼\\n               ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\\n               │ PHASE 6: CHAPTER DRAFTING (sequential, INV-012)             │\\n               │   chapters/chapter-{NNN}.md (one per chapter)               │\\n               │   chapters/chapter-{NNN}-metadata.json                      │\\n               │   ◄── continuity-tracker.json updated after each chapter ──►│\\n               └──────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────┘\\n                                      │\\n                                      ▼\\n               ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\\n               │ PHASE 7: REVISION (3 sequential passes)                     │\\n               │   revision/developmental-findings.json → fix → v2           │\\n               │   revision/line-edit-findings.json → fix → v3               │\\n               │   revision/copy-edit-findings.json → fix → v4               │\\n               └──────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────┘\\n                                      │\\n                                      ▼\\n               ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\\n               │ PHASE 8: BETA READING (5 parallel lenses)                   │\\n               │   beta-reading/romance-lens.json      ┐                     │\\n               │   beta-reading/fantasy-lens.json      │                     │\\n               │   beta-reading/craft-lens.json        ├──► synthesis.json   │\\n               │   beta-reading/sensitivity-lens.json  │    verdict:         │\\n               │   beta-reading/originality-lens.json  ┘    proceed | re-enter\\n               └──────────┬─────────────────────────┬───────────────────────┘\\n                          │                         │\\n           ┌──────────────┘          (re-entry      │\\n           │  (proceed-to-polish)     if critical/  │\\n           │                          major findings)\\n           │                                │       │\\n           │                                └───────┘ ◄── bounded by maxCycles\\n           ▼\\n               ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\\n               │ PHASE 9: POLISH & DELIVERY                                  │\\n               │   chapters/chapter-{NNN}.md → vFinal                        │\\n               │   delivery/chapter-summaries.json                           │\\n               │   delivery/book-metadata.json                               │\\n               │         │                                                   │\\n               │         └──► series-knowledge-base.json (merge)             │\\n               └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\\n```\\n\\n## Multi-Writer Contracts\\n\\n### 1. `continuity-tracker.json` — Single-Writer Accumulator\\n- **Writer**: `romantic-fantasy-writer-continuity-tracker` (sole writer)\\n- **Protocol**: Read latest chapter → cross-reference world-bible + characters → append/update entries\\n- **Merge rules**: Append-only for timeline, characterKnowledge, establishedFacts. Update-in-place for characterPositions. Chekhov items transition: planted → growing → paid-off.\\n- **Locking**: Sequential — one chapter at a time (INV-012)\\n\\n### 2. `chapters/chapter-{NNN}-metadata.json` — Field-Level Ownership\\n- **Writers**: chapter-drafter, developmental-editor, line-editor, copy-editor, polish-agent\\n- **Protocol**: Each writer modifies only its own `revisionStatus` sub-field and increments `draftVersion`\\n- **Merge rules**: Drafter owns core fields (chapterId, pov, scenes). Each editor owns its revisionStatus entry.\\n- **Locking**: Sequential — revision passes run in strict order\\n\\n### 3. `series-knowledge-base.json` — Single-Writer Accumulator\\n- **Writer**: `romantic-fantasy-writer-series-kb-manager` (sole writer)\\n- **Protocol**: Merges current book's data into series-level record at phase 9\\n- **Merge rules**: Append to arrays, update maps. Prior-book entries immutable (INV-051).\\n- **Locking**: Runs once at pipeline end\\n\\n### 4. `manifest.json` — Prepend-Only Audit Log\\n- **Writers**: All agents\\n- **Protocol**: Each agent prepends its entry after task completion\\n- **Merge rules**: No modifications to existing entries. Newest first.\\n- **Locking**: Sequential within phases; beta readers prepend independently\\n\\n### 5. `progress.json` — Single-Writer\\n- **Writer**: `romantic-fantasy-writer-orchestrator` (sole writer)\\n- **Protocol**: Updates phase status fields\\n- **Locking**: Orchestrator is single-threaded\\n\\n## Acyclicity Validation\\n\\n**Verified: ✅ Acyclic**\\n\\nThe artifact dependency graph follows the 9-phase creative pipeline with strict forward flow:\\n\\n```\\nconcept → world → characters → plot → style → chapters → revision → beta-reading → polish → series-KB\\n```\\n\\n**Controlled backward edge**: `beta-reading/synthesis.json` → `phase7-revision` (re-entry) is bounded by `maxCycles` and is a re-execution, not a circular data dependency.\\n\\n**Cross-book edge**: `series-knowledge-base.json` → `phase1-concept` is only for sequels, across separate production runs, not within a single run.\\n\\n## ID Scheme Summary\\n\\n| Prefix | Domain | Example |\\n|--------|--------|---------|\\n| LOC-NNN | Locations | LOC-001 (Thornhold Castle) |\\n| MAG-NNN | Magic rules | MAG-003 (Healing requires equal pain) |\\n| FAC-NNN | Factions | FAC-002 (Silver Court) |\\n| CUL-NNN | Cultures | CUL-001 (Elvari customs) |\\n| HIST-NNN | Historical events | HIST-005 (The Sundering War) |\\n| CREAT-NNN | Creatures | CREAT-003 (Shadowcat) |\\n| PLANT-NNN | Plants | PLANT-001 (Moonbloom) |\\n| CHAR-NNN | Characters | CHAR-001 (Elara Nightbloom) |\\n| CH-NNN | Chapters | CH-012 |\\n| SCN-NNN | Scenes | SCN-034 |\\n| FBEAT-NNN | Fantasy arc beats | FBEAT-007 (Climax) |\\n| RBEAT-NNN | Romance arc beats | RBEAT-004 (First Vulnerability) |\\n| SUB-NNN | Subplots | SUB-003 (Political conspiracy) |\\n| CK-NNN | Chekhov items | CK-005 (Ancient prophecy) |\\n| TL-NNN | Timeline entries | TL-020 |\\n| FACT-NNN | Established facts | FACT-042 |\\n| CANON-NNN | Series canon | CANON-015 |\\n| DEV-NNN | Developmental findings | DEV-008 |\\n| LINE-NNN | Line edit findings | LINE-023 |\\n| COPY-NNN | Copy edit findings | COPY-011 |\\n| BR-NNN | Romance beta findings | BR-005 |\\n| BF-NNN | Fantasy beta findings | BF-003 |\\n| BC-NNN | Craft beta findings | BC-012 |\\n| BS-NNN | Sensitivity beta findings | BS-002 |\\n| BO-NNN | Originality beta findings | BO-001 |\\n| BETA-NNN | Synthesized beta findings | BETA-007 |\\n\\n## Invariant Coverage by Artifact\\n\\nKey invariants and which artifacts enforce them:\\n\\n| Invariant | Enforcing Artifact(s) |\\n|-----------|----------------------|\\n| INV-001 (Genre Promise) | story-concept.json (genrePromise field) |\\n| INV-002 (Internal Consistency) | continuity-tracker.json, world-bible/*.json |\\n| INV-003 (Voice Distinctness) | characters/{slug}.json (voiceGuide), cast-index.json (voiceDistinctivenessMatrix) |\\n| INV-006 (Chekhov's Gun) | continuity-tracker.json (chekhovRegistry) |\\n| INV-010 (Outline Before Draft) | plot/chapter-outlines.json (must exist before chapter-{NNN}.md) |\\n| INV-011 (Continuity Tracking) | continuity-tracker.json (updated after every chapter) |\\n| INV-012 (Sequential Chapter Production) | chapters/chapter-{NNN}.md (one at a time) |\\n| INV-014 (Revision Traceability) | revision/*.json (status + addressedIn fields) |\\n| INV-023 (No Plagiarism) | beta-reading/originality-lens.json (plagiarismFlags) |\\n| INV-032/063 (Craft Toolbox) | story-craft-profile.json |\\n| INV-049/051 (Series-First) | series-knowledge-base.json |\\n| INV-053 (Five Beta Lenses) | beta-reading/{romance,fantasy,craft,sensitivity,originality}-lens.json |\\n| INV-054 (Beta Findings Addressed) | beta-reading/synthesis.json (verdict field) |\\n| INV-058 (Naming Collisions) | characters/cast-index.json (namingRegistry), series-knowledge-base.json (namingRegistry) |\\n\\n## Design Decisions\\n\\n1. **World-bible split into 6 files** (not monolithic): Follows INV-031/INV-055 subcategory decomposition. Each file is self-contained per INV-064, allowing agents to load only what they need (e.g., chapter-drafter for a political scene loads politics.json, not all world data).\\n\\n2. **Per-character files** (not character-list.json): Each character gets a dedicated JSON file pointed to from cast-index.json. This scales to large casts without loading all characters into context. Voice guides carry across books (INV-057).\\n\\n3. **Continuity tracker as single-writer accumulator**: Despite being read by many agents, only the dedicated continuity-tracker agent writes to it. This prevents merge conflicts and ensures consistent cross-referencing.\\n\\n4. **Beta reading artifacts fully parallel**: Each of the 5 lens files is written by an independent agent with zero dependencies between them. Only synthesis.json aggregates across lenses, after all have completed.\\n\\n5. **Three separate revision finding files** (not one): Matches the three sequential revision passes (developmental → line → copy). Each creates its own findings file with its own ID scheme. This keeps findings traceable to which pass found them.\\n\\n6. **Series KB as append-mostly accumulator**: Prior-book entries are immutable (INV-051). The retconLog field provides an explicit escape hatch for intentional canon changes, ensuring nothing is silently contradicted.\\n\"}"
            }
