          {
            "id": "toolu_01MWGEkdBJHZw4rHiromNdQH",
            "type": "function",
            "function": {
              "name": "bash",
              "arguments": "{\"command\": \"cd /home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator && python3 << 'PYEOF'\\nimport json\\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\\n\\n# Load architecture.json\\nwith open('.fractal-factory/architecture.json') as f:\\n    arch = json.load(f)\\n\\nnow = datetime.now(timezone.utc).strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S.000Z')\\n\\n# Build the depthAnalysis section\\ndepth_analysis = {\\n    \\\"designRationale\\\": (\\n        \\\"The romantic-fantasy-writer system uses a uniform depth-2 hierarchy for all phase coordinators. \\\"\\n        \\\"Despite 17 subdomains and 64 invariants, the creative pipeline naturally decomposes into 9 phases \\\"\\n        \\\"where each phase coordinator manages 2-6 specialists — all well under the 8-specialist threshold \\\"\\n        \\\"for depth-3 escalation. Cross-cutting concerns (adversarial quality gates, continuity tracking, \\\"\\n        \\\"genre compliance, craft toolbox, originality assurance, series knowledge management, artifact management) \\\"\\n        \\\"are enforcement responsibilities embedded into specialist agent prompts rather than separate routing layers. \\\"\\n        \\\"The highest specialist count is beta-reading (6: five parallel lenses + synthesizer), which is still \\\"\\n        \\\"within depth-2 capacity. The overall system depth is 3 levels (guide → orchestrator → coordinator → specialist), \\\"\\n        \\\"well within the maxDepth=4 limit, leaving room for future depth-3 escalation if any phase grows during \\\"\\n        \\\"roster planning.\\\"\\n    ),\\n    \\\"maxAllowedDepth\\\": 4,\\n    \\\"systemDepthLevels\\\": {\\n        \\\"level0\\\": \\\"guide (user-facing entry point)\\\",\\n        \\\"level1\\\": \\\"orchestrator (9-phase sequential pipeline dispatcher)\\\",\\n        \\\"level2\\\": \\\"phase coordinators (one per creative phase, pure routers)\\\",\\n        \\\"level3\\\": \\\"specialists (writers, auditors, editors, lenses, trackers)\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"actualSystemDepth\\\": 3,\\n    \\\"depthThresholds\\\": {\\n        \\\"specialistCountThreshold\\\": 8,\\n        \\\"crossCuttingConcernsThreshold\\\": 3,\\n        \\\"subdomainGroupsThreshold\\\": 3,\\n        \\\"description\\\": \\\"If ANY criterion exceeds its threshold AND maxDepth allows it, coordinator escalates to depth-3 with sub-coordinators grouping specialists by subdomain cluster.\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"decisions\\\": [\\n        {\\n            \\\"coordinator\\\": \\\"romantic-fantasy-writer-orchestrator\\\",\\n            \\\"role\\\": \\\"top-level-orchestrator\\\",\\n            \\\"depth\\\": 2,\\n            \\\"estimatedDirectChildren\\\": 10,\\n            \\\"estimatedSpecialists\\\": 0,\\n            \\\"crossCuttingConcerns\\\": 7,\\n            \\\"subdomainGroups\\\": 9,\\n            \\\"criteria\\\": {\\n                \\\"specialistCount\\\": {\\\"value\\\": 10, \\\"threshold\\\": 8, \\\"exceeds\\\": True},\\n                \\\"crossCuttingConcerns\\\": {\\\"value\\\": 7, \\\"threshold\\\": 3, \\\"exceeds\\\": True},\\n                \\\"subdomainGroups\\\": {\\\"value\\\": 9, \\\"threshold\\\": 3, \\\"exceeds\\\": True},\\n                \\\"exemplarSuggestsDepth3\\\": False\\n            },\\n            \\\"overrideReason\\\": \\\"Despite exceeding numeric thresholds, the orchestrator's children are coordinators, not specialists. The routing pattern is strictly sequential (phase 1 → 2 → ... → 9) with deterministic ordering and no parallel dispatch. The exemplar factory orchestrator follows the same pattern with 7 sequential pass-coordinators at depth-2. Cross-cutting concerns are enforcement responsibilities distributed into phase-level prompts, not separate routing targets. Adding sub-coordinators (e.g., grouping phases 1-5 under 'pre-production' and 6-9 under 'production') would create artificial boundaries that break the natural pipeline flow and complicate the writer-reviewer-to-beta re-entry path.\\\",\\n            \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Sequential pipeline dispatcher. Children are phase coordinators, not specialists. Exemplar pattern (fractal-factory orchestrator with 7 passes) validates depth-2 for sequential coordinators.\\\",\\n            \\\"subCoordinators\\\": None\\n        },\\n        {\\n            \\\"coordinator\\\": \\\"romantic-fantasy-writer-concept-coordinator\\\",\\n            \\\"role\\\": \\\"phase-1-concept-development\\\",\\n            \\\"depth\\\": 2,\\n            \\\"estimatedDirectChildren\\\": 2,\\n            \\\"estimatedSpecialists\\\": 2,\\n            \\\"crossCuttingConcerns\\\": 3,\\n            \\\"subdomainGroups\\\": 1,\\n            \\\"criteria\\\": {\\n                \\\"specialistCount\\\": {\\\"value\\\": 2, \\\"threshold\\\": 8, \\\"exceeds\\\": False},\\n                \\\"crossCuttingConcerns\\\": {\\\"value\\\": 3, \\\"threshold\\\": 3, \\\"exceeds\\\": False},\\n                \\\"subdomainGroups\\\": {\\\"value\\\": 1, \\\"threshold\\\": 3, \\\"exceeds\\\": False},\\n                \\\"exemplarSuggestsDepth3\\\": False\\n            },\\n            \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Minimal phase: concept-writer + concept-auditor in a writer-reviewer loop. Cross-cutting concerns (genre compliance, craft toolbox selection, adversarial gating) are enforcement rules in the auditor's prompt, not separate agents. 2 specialists is the lowest count in the system.\\\",\\n            \\\"subCoordinators\\\": None\\n        },\\n        {\\n            \\\"coordinator\\\": \\\"romantic-fantasy-writer-worldbuilding-coordinator\\\",\\n            \\\"role\\\": \\\"phase-2-world-building\\\",\\n            \\\"depth\\\": 2,\\n            \\\"estimatedDirectChildren\\\": 4,\\n            \\\"estimatedSpecialists\\\": 4,\\n            \\\"crossCuttingConcerns\\\": 4,\\n            \\\"subdomainGroups\\\": 1,\\n            \\\"criteria\\\": {\\n                \\\"specialistCount\\\": {\\\"value\\\": 4, \\\"threshold\\\": 8, \\\"exceeds\\\": False},\\n                \\\"crossCuttingConcerns\\\": {\\\"value\\\": 4, \\\"threshold\\\": 3, \\\"exceeds\\\": True},\\n                \\\"subdomainGroups\\\": {\\\"value\\\": 1, \\\"threshold\\\": 3, \\\"exceeds\\\": False},\\n                \\\"exemplarSuggestsDepth3\\\": False\\n            },\\n            \\\"overrideReason\\\": \\\"Cross-cutting count of 4 exceeds the threshold, but these are enforcement concerns (continuity tracking, series KB, adversarial gating, artifact management) embedded as validation rules in the world-auditor prompt. They do not require separate routing targets. The world-builder agent iterates through 6 subcategory artifacts (geography, magic, politics, culture, history, flora/fauna) sequentially within a single agent, not as separate specialist agents.\\\",\\n            \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"4 specialists: world-builder (produces 6 subcategory files), world-auditor (cross-references all subcategories for consistency), continuity-initializer (seeds the continuity tracker from worldbuilding), series-kb-reader (loads existing series canon for sequels). Only 1 criterion marginally exceeds threshold, and the exceeding concern is enforcement-only.\\\",\\n            \\\"subCoordinators\\\": None\\n        },\\n        {\\n            \\\"coordinator\\\": \\\"romantic-fantasy-writer-character-coordinator\\\",\\n            \\\"role\\\": \\\"phase-3-character-design\\\",\\n            \\\"depth\\\": 2,\\n            \\\"estimatedDirectChildren\\\": 3,\\n            \\\"estimatedSpecialists\\\": 3,\\n            \\\"crossCuttingConcerns\\\": 4,\\n            \\\"subdomainGroups\\\": 1,\\n            \\\"criteria\\\": {\\n                \\\"specialistCount\\\": {\\\"value\\\": 3, \\\"threshold\\\": 8, \\\"exceeds\\\": False},\\n                \\\"crossCuttingConcerns\\\": {\\\"value\\\": 4, \\\"threshold\\\": 3, \\\"exceeds\\\": True},\\n                \\\"subdomainGroups\\\": {\\\"value\\\": 1, \\\"threshold\\\": 3, \\\"exceeds\\\": False},\\n                \\\"exemplarSuggestsDepth3\\\": False\\n            },\\n            \\\"overrideReason\\\": \\\"Cross-cutting count exceeds threshold but all 4 concerns (genre compliance, continuity, adversarial gates, series KB) are validation rules embedded in the character-auditor's prompt. Per-character iteration is handled by the coordinator re-dispatching the same agents, not by adding hierarchy.\\\",\\n            \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"3 specialists: character-designer (creates per-character profiles + cast index), character-auditor (validates voice distinctness, agency, genre conventions), series-character-loader (loads returning characters for sequels). Coordinator iterates per-character through designer-auditor loop.\\\",\\n            \\\"subCoordinators\\\": None\\n        },\\n        {\\n            \\\"coordinator\\\": \\\"romantic-fantasy-writer-plot-coordinator\\\",\\n            \\\"role\\\": \\\"phase-4-plot-architecture\\\",\\n            \\\"depth\\\": 2,\\n            \\\"estimatedDirectChildren\\\": 4,\\n            \\\"estimatedSpecialists\\\": 4,\\n            \\\"crossCuttingConcerns\\\": 4,\\n            \\\"subdomainGroups\\\": 1,\\n            \\\"criteria\\\": {\\n                \\\"specialistCount\\\": {\\\"value\\\": 4, \\\"threshold\\\": 8, \\\"exceeds\\\": False},\\n                \\\"crossCuttingConcerns\\\": {\\\"value\\\": 4, \\\"threshold\\\": 3, \\\"exceeds\\\": True},\\n                \\\"subdomainGroups\\\": {\\\"value\\\": 1, \\\"threshold\\\": 3, \\\"exceeds\\\": False},\\n                \\\"exemplarSuggestsDepth3\\\": False\\n            },\\n            \\\"overrideReason\\\": \\\"Cross-cutting count exceeds threshold, but genre compliance, craft toolbox enforcement, adversarial gating, and continuity are all validation responsibilities in the plot-auditor's prompt. The 4 output artifacts (structure framework, chapter outlines, tension map, subplot tracker) are produced by related specialists in sequence, not as independent subdomain groups.\\\",\\n            \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"4 specialists: plot-architect (structure framework + chapter outlines), tension-mapper (tension-map with dual-arc pacing), subplot-tracker (subplot management), plot-auditor (validates plot completeness, craft tool compliance, dual-arc interleave). Sequential dispatch with auditor reviewing the aggregate.\\\",\\n            \\\"subCoordinators\\\": None\\n        },\\n        {\\n            \\\"coordinator\\\": \\\"romantic-fantasy-writer-style-coordinator\\\",\\n            \\\"role\\\": \\\"phase-5-prose-style\\\",\\n            \\\"depth\\\": 2,\\n            \\\"estimatedDirectChildren\\\": 2,\\n            \\\"estimatedSpecialists\\\": 2,\\n            \\\"crossCuttingConcerns\\\": 3,\\n            \\\"subdomainGroups\\\": 1,\\n            \\\"criteria\\\": {\\n                \\\"specialistCount\\\": {\\\"value\\\": 2, \\\"threshold\\\": 8, \\\"exceeds\\\": False},\\n                \\\"crossCuttingConcerns\\\": {\\\"value\\\": 3, \\\"threshold\\\": 3, \\\"exceeds\\\": False},\\n                \\\"subdomainGroups\\\": {\\\"value\\\": 1, \\\"threshold\\\": 3, \\\"exceeds\\\": False},\\n                \\\"exemplarSuggestsDepth3\\\": False\\n            },\\n            \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Simplest creative phase. 2 specialists: style-analyst (analyzes reference fiction, produces style guide with voice calibration and tone palette), style-auditor (validates originality compliance, completeness, POV-specific variations). No criteria exceed thresholds.\\\",\\n            \\\"subCoordinators\\\": None\\n        },\\n        {\\n            \\\"coordinator\\\": \\\"romantic-fantasy-writer-drafting-coordinator\\\",\\n            \\\"role\\\": \\\"phase-6-chapter-drafting\\\",\\n            \\\"depth\\\": 2,\\n            \\\"estimatedDirectChildren\\\": 4,\\n            \\\"estimatedSpecialists\\\": 4,\\n            \\\"crossCuttingConcerns\\\": 4,\\n            \\\"subdomainGroups\\\": 1,\\n            \\\"criteria\\\": {\\n                \\\"specialistCount\\\": {\\\"value\\\": 4, \\\"threshold\\\": 8, \\\"exceeds\\\": False},\\n                \\\"crossCuttingConcerns\\\": {\\\"value\\\": 4, \\\"threshold\\\": 3, \\\"exceeds\\\": True},\\n                \\\"subdomainGroups\\\": {\\\"value\\\": 1, \\\"threshold\\\": 3, \\\"exceeds\\\": False},\\n                \\\"exemplarSuggestsDepth3\\\": False\\n            },\\n            \\\"overrideReason\\\": \\\"Cross-cutting count exceeds threshold. However, the phase's complexity lies in iteration (sequential per-chapter production), not hierarchy. The same 4 agents are re-dispatched for each chapter. Adding sub-coordinators (e.g., per-chapter sub-coordinator) would multiply agents by chapter count, which is catastrophic for the budget. The coordinator's state machine handles per-chapter iteration natively.\\\",\\n            \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"4 specialists: chapter-drafter (writes chapter prose), chapter-auditor (adversarial review per chapter), continuity-tracker (updates continuity state after each chapter), scene-planner (pre-chapter scene breakdown from outline). The coordinator manages the per-chapter iteration loop: for each chapter → scene-planner → drafter → auditor → continuity-tracker → next chapter. Most complex routing logic in the system but complexity is in iteration, not hierarchy.\\\",\\n            \\\"subCoordinators\\\": None\\n        },\\n        {\\n            \\\"coordinator\\\": \\\"romantic-fantasy-writer-revision-coordinator\\\",\\n            \\\"role\\\": \\\"phase-7-revision-editing\\\",\\n            \\\"depth\\\": 2,\\n            \\\"estimatedDirectChildren\\\": 4,\\n            \\\"estimatedSpecialists\\\": 4,\\n            \\\"crossCuttingConcerns\\\": 3,\\n            \\\"subdomainGroups\\\": 3,\\n            \\\"criteria\\\": {\\n                \\\"specialistCount\\\": {\\\"value\\\": 4, \\\"threshold\\\": 8, \\\"exceeds\\\": False},\\n                \\\"crossCuttingConcerns\\\": {\\\"value\\\": 3, \\\"threshold\\\": 3, \\\"exceeds\\\": False},\\n                \\\"subdomainGroups\\\": {\\\"value\\\": 3, \\\"threshold\\\": 3, \\\"exceeds\\\": False},\\n                \\\"exemplarSuggestsDepth3\\\": False\\n            },\\n            \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"4 specialists across 3 distinct edit passes: developmental-editor (plot holes, pacing, structure), line-editor (prose quality, voice, show-don't-tell), copy-editor (grammar, spelling, consistency), revision-synthesizer (aggregates all findings into prioritized revision list). The 3 subdomain groups (the 3 edit types) each map to exactly 1 specialist, so sub-coordinators would be 1:1 with specialists — pure overhead. Sequential dispatch: developmental → line → copy → synthesize.\\\",\\n            \\\"subCoordinators\\\": None\\n        },\\n        {\\n            \\\"coordinator\\\": \\\"romantic-fantasy-writer-beta-coordinator\\\",\\n            \\\"role\\\": \\\"phase-8-beta-reading\\\",\\n            \\\"depth\\\": 2,\\n            \\\"estimatedDirectChildren\\\": 6,\\n            \\\"estimatedSpecialists\\\": 6,\\n            \\\"crossCuttingConcerns\\\": 3,\\n            \\\"subdomainGroups\\\": 1,\\n            \\\"criteria\\\": {\\n                \\\"specialistCount\\\": {\\\"value\\\": 6, \\\"threshold\\\": 8, \\\"exceeds\\\": False},\\n                \\\"crossCuttingConcerns\\\": {\\\"value\\\": 3, \\\"threshold\\\": 3, \\\"exceeds\\\": False},\\n                \\\"subdomainGroups\\\": {\\\"value\\\": 1, \\\"threshold\\\": 3, \\\"exceeds\\\": False},\\n                \\\"exemplarSuggestsDepth3\\\": False\\n            },\\n            \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"6 specialists — highest count but still under threshold: 5 independent beta-reader lenses (romance-lens, fantasy-lens, craft-lens, sensitivity-lens, originality-lens) + beta-synthesizer. This is the only phase with parallel dispatch: coordinator fans out all 5 lenses simultaneously, waits for all to complete, then dispatches synthesizer. All lenses have identical routing patterns (read full manuscript → produce lens-specific findings), making them a homogeneous group that doesn't benefit from sub-coordinator grouping. INV-053 mandates 5 independent lenses.\\\",\\n            \\\"subCoordinators\\\": None\\n        },\\n        {\\n            \\\"coordinator\\\": \\\"romantic-fantasy-writer-polish-coordinator\\\",\\n            \\\"role\\\": \\\"phase-9-polish-delivery\\\",\\n            \\\"depth\\\": 2,\\n            \\\"estimatedDirectChildren\\\": 3,\\n            \\\"estimatedSpecialists\\\": 3,\\n            \\\"crossCuttingConcerns\\\": 3,\\n            \\\"subdomainGroups\\\": 1,\\n            \\\"criteria\\\": {\\n                \\\"specialistCount\\\": {\\\"value\\\": 3, \\\"threshold\\\": 8, \\\"exceeds\\\": False},\\n                \\\"crossCuttingConcerns\\\": {\\\"value\\\": 3, \\\"threshold\\\": 3, \\\"exceeds\\\": False},\\n                \\\"subdomainGroups\\\": {\\\"value\\\": 1, \\\"threshold\\\": 3, \\\"exceeds\\\": False},\\n                \\\"exemplarSuggestsDepth3\\\": False\\n            },\\n            \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"3 specialists: proofreader (final copy polish incorporating beta/revision findings), series-kb-updater (merges completed book into series knowledge base), delivery-packager (chapter summaries, book metadata, final packaging). Simple sequential dispatch. Terminal phase with no downstream dependencies.\\\",\\n            \\\"subCoordinators\\\": None\\n        }\\n    ],\\n    \\\"budgetAnalysis\\\": {\\n        \\\"guide\\\": 1,\\n        \\\"orchestrator\\\": 1,\\n        \\\"phaseCoordinators\\\": 9,\\n        \\\"totalSpecialists\\\": 32,\\n        \\\"totalEstimatedAgents\\\": 43,\\n        \\\"maxAgents\\\": 80,\\n        \\\"budgetStatus\\\": \\\"within-limit\\\",\\n        \\\"remainingCapacity\\\": 37,\\n        \\\"capacityNotes\\\": (\\n            \\\"43 agents uses 54% of the 80-agent budget, leaving 37 slots for roster planning to: \\\"\\n            \\\"(1) add dedicated cross-cutting utility agents (e.g., shared continuity-verifier, series-canon-validator) \\\"\\n            \\\"if the roster planner determines they shouldn't be embedded in phase auditors, \\\"\\n            \\\"(2) split complex specialists if any single agent's prompt exceeds manageable size, \\\"\\n            \\\"(3) add per-chapter specialist variants if the drafting coordinator needs more granular dispatch. \\\"\\n            \\\"The generous remaining capacity means the roster planner has freedom to expand without triggering \\\"\\n            \\\"depth-3 escalation — any phase that gains specialists above 8 would need re-evaluation.\\\"\\n        )\\n    },\\n    \\\"depth3EscalationWatchList\\\": [\\n        {\\n            \\\"coordinator\\\": \\\"romantic-fantasy-writer-beta-coordinator\\\",\\n            \\\"currentSpecialists\\\": 6,\\n            \\\"headroomToThreshold\\\": 2,\\n            \\\"escalationTrigger\\\": \\\"If the roster planner adds per-genre sub-lenses (e.g., romance-lens splits into tropes-lens + chemistry-lens + pacing-lens), specialist count could exceed 8. Watch for this during roster planning.\\\",\\n            \\\"proposedSubCoordinators\\\": [\\n                {\\\"name\\\": \\\"content-lenses-sub-coordinator\\\", \\\"specialists\\\": [\\\"romance-lens\\\", \\\"fantasy-lens\\\"]},\\n                {\\\"name\\\": \\\"quality-lenses-sub-coordinator\\\", \\\"specialists\\\": [\\\"craft-lens\\\", \\\"sensitivity-lens\\\", \\\"originality-lens\\\"]}\\n            ]\\n        },\\n        {\\n            \\\"coordinator\\\": \\\"romantic-fantasy-writer-drafting-coordinator\\\",\\n            \\\"currentSpecialists\\\": 4,\\n            \\\"headroomToThreshold\\\": 4,\\n            \\\"escalationTrigger\\\": \\\"If the roster planner adds voice-consistency-checker, pacing-validator, or craft-tool-auditor as separate per-chapter agents (rather 