n    \\"depthThresholds\\": {\\n        \\"specialistCountThreshold\\": 8,\\n        \\"crossCuttingConcernsThreshold\\": 3,\\n        \\"subdomainGroupsThreshold\\": 3,\\n        \\"description\\": \\"If ANY criterion exceeds its threshold AND maxDepth allows it, coordinator escalates to depth-3 with sub-coordinators grouping specialists by subdomain cluster.\\"\\n    },\\n    \\"decisions\\": [\\n        {\\n            \\"coordinator\\": \\"romantic-fantasy-writer-orchestrator\\",\\n            \\"role\\": \\"top-level-orchestrator\\",\\n            \\"depth\\": 2,\\n            \\"estimatedDirectChildren\\": 10,\\n            \\"estimatedSpecialists\\": 0,\\n            \\"crossCuttingConcerns\\": 7,\\n            \\"subdomainGroups\\": 9,\\n            \\"criteria\\": {\\n                \\"specialistCount\\": {\\"value\\": 10, \\"threshold\\": 8, \\"exceeds\\": True},\\n                \\"crossCuttingConcerns\\": {\\"value\\": 7, \\"threshold\\": 3, \\"exceeds\\": True},\\n                \\"subdomainGroups\\": {\\"value\\": 9, \\"threshold\\": 3, \\"exceeds\\": True},\\n                \\"exemplarSuggestsDepth3\\": False\\n            },\\n            \\"overrideReason\\": \\"Despite exceeding numeric thresholds, the orchestrator's children are coordinators, not specialists. The routing pattern is strictly sequential (phase 1 → 2 → ... → 9) with deterministic ordering and no parallel dispatch. The exemplar factory orchestrator follows the same pattern with 7 sequential pass-coordinators at depth-2. Cross-cutting concerns are enforcement responsibilities distributed into phase-level prompts, not separate routing targets. Adding sub-coordinators (e.g., grouping phases 1-5 under 'pre-production' and 6-9 under 'production') would create artificial boundaries that break the natural pipeline flow and complicate the writer-reviewer-to-beta re-entry path.\\",\\n            \\"rationale\\": \\"Sequential pipeline dispatcher. Children are phase coordinators, not specialists. Exemplar pattern (fractal-factory orchestrator with 7 passes) validates depth-2 for sequential coordinators.\\",\\n            \\"subCoordinators\\": None\\n        },\\n        {\\n            \\"coordinator\\": \\"romantic-fantasy-writer-concept-coordinator\\",\\n            \\"role\\": \\"phase-1-concept-development\\",\\n            \\"depth\\": 2,\\n            \\"estimatedDirectChildren\\": 2,\\n            \\"estimatedSpecialists\\": 2,\\n            \\"crossCuttingConcerns\\": 3,\\n            \\"subdomainGroups\\": 1,\\n            \\"criteria\\": {\\n                \\"specialistCount\\": {\\"value\\": 2, \\"threshold\\": 8, \\"exceeds\\": False},\\n                \\"crossCuttingConcerns\\": {\\"value\\": 3, \\"threshold\\": 3, \\"exceeds\\": False},\\n                \\"subdomainGroups\\": {\\"value\\": 1, \\"threshold\\": 3, \\"exceeds\\": False},\\n                \\"exemplarSuggestsDepth3\\": False\\n            },\\n            \\"rationale\\": \\"Minimal phase: concept-writer + concept-auditor in a writer-reviewer loop. Cross-cutting concerns (genre compliance, craft toolbox selection, adversarial gating) are enforcement rules in the auditor's prompt, not separate agents. 2 specialists is the lowest count in the system.\\",\\n            \\"subCoordinators\\": None\\n        },\\n        {\\n            \\"coordinator\\": \\"romantic-fantasy-writer-worldbuilding-coordinator\\",\\n            \\"role\\": \\"phase-2-world-building\\",\\n            \\"depth\\": 2,\\n            \\"estimatedDirectChildren\\": 4,\\n            \\"estimatedSpecialists\\": 4,\\n            \\"crossCuttingConcerns\\": 4,\\n            \\"subdomainGroups\\": 1,\\n            \\"criteria\\": {\\n                \\"specialistCount\\": {\\"value\\": 4, \\"threshold\\": 8, \\"exceeds\\": False},\\n                \\"crossCuttingConcerns\\": {\\"value\\": 4, \\"threshold\\": 3, \\"exceeds\\": True},\\n                \\"subdomainGroups\\": {\\"value\\": 1, \\"threshold\\": 3, \\"exceeds\\": False},\\n                \\"exemplarSuggestsDepth3\\": False\\n            },\\n            \\"overrideReason\\": \\"Cross-cutting count of 4 exceeds the threshold, but these are enforcement concerns (continuity tracking, series KB, adversarial gating, artifact management) embedded as validation rules in the world-auditor prompt. They do not require separate routing targets. The world-builder agent iterates through 6 subcategory artifacts (geography, magic, politics, culture, history, flora/fauna) sequentially within a single agent, not as separate specialist agents.\\",\\n            \\"rationale\\": \\"4 specialists: world-builder (produces 6 subcategory files), world-auditor (cross-references all subcategories for consistency), continuity-initializer (seeds the continuity tracker from worldbuilding), series-kb-reader (loads existing series canon for sequels). Only 1 criterion marginally exceeds threshold, and the exceeding concern is enforcement-only.\\",\\n            \\"subCoordinators\\": None\\n        },\\n        {\\n            \\"coordinator\\": \\"romantic-fantasy-writer-character-coordinator\\",\\n            \\"role\\": \\"phase-3-character-design\\",\\n            \\"depth\\": 2,\\n            \\"estimatedDirectChildren\\": 3,\\n            \\"estimatedSpecialists\\": 3,\\n            \\"crossCuttingConcerns\\": 4,\\n            \\"subdomainGroups\\": 1,\\n            \\"criteria\\": {\\n                \\"specialistCount\\": {\\"value\\": 3, \\"threshold\\": 8, \\"exceeds\\": False},\\n                \\"crossCuttingConcerns\\": {\\"value\\": 4, \\"threshold\\": 3, \\"exceeds\\": True},\\n                \\"subdomainGroups\\": {\\"value\\": 1, \\"threshold\\": 3, \\"exceeds\\": False},\\n                \\"exemplarSuggestsDepth3\\": False\\n            },\\n            \\"overrideReason\\": \\"Cross-cutting count exceeds threshold but all 4 concerns (genre compliance, continuity, adversarial gates, series KB) are validation rules