**Working directory**: /home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator
**Factory root**: .fractal-factory/

**Your inputs** (read these files):
- `.fractal-factory/context.json` — config (maxAgents=80, namingPrefix=romantic-fantasy-writer, maxDepth=4)
- `.fractal-factory/domain-model.json` — populated domain model with 17 subdomains, 64 invariants
- `.fractal-factory/architecture.json` — pipeline design, artifact schemas, depth analysis (7-pass pipeline, 34 artifacts, all coordinators at depth-2, 43/80 agent budget)
- `.fractal-factory/domain-brief.md` — domain brief
- `.fractal-factory/invariants.md` — invariants and craft toolbox

**Your task**: Plan the complete agent roster for the romantic-fantasy-writer system. For every agent produce:
- Agent name (using naming prefix from context.json)
- Level (orchestrator / coordinator / specialist)
- Parent agent
- Children agents (if coordinator/orchestrator)
- Result codes (success, failure, etc.)
- Artifact assignments (which artifacts this agent reads/writes)
- Brief description of its responsibility

Stay within the maxAgents budget (80). The architecture.json already suggests ~43 agents, all coordinators at depth-2. Respect the pipeline structure from architecture.json.

**Output**: Write the roster to `.fractal-factory/roster.json` and write your status to `.fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory-roster-planner/status.json` with result "planned" on success.

Status format:
```json
{
  "agent": "fractal-factory-roster-planner",
  "task_id": "pass3/roster",
  "status": "completed",
  "result": "planned",
  "summary": "Roster planned: N agents (X orchestrators, Y coordinators, Z specialists)",
  "artifacts": ["roster.json", "agents/fractal-factory-roster-planner/status.json"],
  "next_hint": "routing-planner",
  "iteration": 1
}
```
