 | character | no | complete, blocked |\\n| A-012 | romantic-fantasy-writer-character-designer | specialist | character-coord | character | no | drafted, revised, blocked |\\n| A-013 | romantic-fantasy-writer-character-auditor | specialist | character-coord | character | **yes** | approved, needs-revision, blocked |\\n| A-014 | romantic-fantasy-writer-series-character-loader | specialist | character-coord | character | no | loaded, no-series-data, blocked |\\n| A-015 | romantic-fantasy-writer-plot-coordinator | coordinator | orchestrator | plot | no | complete, blocked |\\n| A-016 | romantic-fantasy-writer-plot-architect | specialist | plot-coord | plot | no | drafted, revised, blocked |\\n| A-017 | romantic-fantasy-writer-tension-mapper | specialist | plot-coord | plot | no | mapped, revised, blocked |\\n| A-018 | romantic-fantasy-writer-subplot-tracker | specialist | plot-coord | plot | no | tracked, revised, blocked |\\n| A-019 | romantic-fantasy-writer-plot-auditor | specialist | plot-coord | plot | **yes** | approved, needs-revision, blocked |\\n| A-020 | romantic-fantasy-writer-style-coordinator | coordinator | orchestrator | style | no | complete, blocked |\\n| A-021 | romantic-fantasy-writer-style-analyst | specialist | style-coord | style | no | drafted, revised, blocked |\\n| A-022 | romantic-fantasy-writer-style-auditor | specialist | style-coord | style | **yes** | approved, needs-revision, blocked |\\n| A-023 | romantic-fantasy-writer-drafting-coordinator | coordinator | orchestrator | drafting | no | complete, blocked |\\n| A-024 | romantic-fantasy-writer-scene-planner | specialist | drafting-coord | drafting | no | planned, revised, blocked |\\n| A-025 | romantic-fantasy-writer-chapter-drafter | specialist | drafting-coord | drafting | no | drafted, revised, blocked |\\n| A-026 | romantic-fantasy-writer-chapter-auditor | specialist | drafting-coord | drafting | **yes** | approved, needs-revision, blocked |\\n| A-027 | romantic-fantasy-writer-continuity-tracker | specialist | drafting-coord | drafting | **yes** | updated, inconsistency-found, blocked |\\n| A-028 | romantic-fantasy-writer-revision-coordinator | coordinator | orchestrator | revision | no | complete, blocked |\\n| A-029 | romantic-fantasy-writer-developmental-editor | specialist | revision-coord | revision | **yes** | reviewed, blocked |\\n| A-030 | romantic-fantasy-writer-line-editor | specialist | revision-coord | revision | **yes** | reviewed, blocked |\\n| A-031 | romantic-fantasy-writer-copy-editor | specialist | revision-coord | revision | **yes** | reviewed, blocked |\\n| A-032 | romantic-fantasy-writer-revision-synthesizer | specialist | revision-coord | revision | **yes** | synthesized, blocked |\\n| A-033 | romantic-fantasy-writer-beta-coordinator | coordinator | orchestrator | beta-reading | no | complete, needs-revision, blocked |\\n| A-034 | romantic-fantasy-writer-romance-beta-reader | specialist | beta-coord | beta-reading | **yes** | reviewed, blocked |\\n| A-035 | romantic-fantasy-writer-fantasy-beta-reader | specialist | beta-coord | beta-reading | **yes** | reviewed, blocked |\\n| A-036 | romantic-fantasy-writer-craft-beta-reader | specialist | beta-coord | beta-reading | **yes** | reviewed, blocked |\\n| A-037 | romantic-fantasy-writer-sensitivity-beta-reader | specialist | beta-coord | beta-reading | **yes** | reviewed, blocked |\\n| A-038 | romantic-fantasy-writer-originality-beta-reader | specialist | beta-coord | beta-reading | **yes** | reviewed, blocked |\\n| A-039 | romantic-fantasy-writer-beta-synthesizer | specialist | beta-coord | beta-reading | **yes** | synthesized, needs-revision, clean, blocked |\\n| A-040 | romantic-fantasy-writer-polish-coordinator | coordinator | orchestrator | polish | no | complete, blocked |\\n| A-041 | romantic-fantasy-writer-proofreader | specialist | polish-coord | polish | no | polished, blocked |\\n| A-042 | romantic-fantasy-writer-series-kb-updater | specialist | polish-coord | polish | no | updated, blocked |\\n| A-043 | romantic-fantasy-writer-delivery-packager | specialist | polish-coord | polish | no | packaged, blocked |\\n\\n## Agent Count by Level\\n\\n| Level | Count |\\n|-------|-------|\\n| Guide | 1 |\\n| Orchestrator | 1 |\\n| Coordinator | 9 |\\n| Specialist | 32 |\\n| **Total** | **43** |\\n\\n## Budget Analysis\\n\\n- **Budget**: 80 agents maximum\\n- **Used**: 43 agents (54%)\\n- **Remaining**: 37 agents\\n- **Assessment**: Comfortably within budget. No merges required. The 37-agent headroom accommodates future depth-3 escalation if any phase grows during prompt writing (e.g., splitting the chapter drafter for very long books, or adding specialist revision agents for specific craft tools).\\n\\n## Design Decisions\\n\\n### Naming Reconciliation\\n\\nThe artifact designer pre-referenced some agent names (e.g., `world-writer`, `character-writer`, `plot-writer`) that differ from the depth analyzer's more descriptive names. The roster establishes these canonical names:\\n\\n| Artifact Reference | Roster Name | Rationale |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| world-writer | **world-builder** | \\\"Builder\\\" better captures the creative construction role vs. \\\"writer\\\" which could confuse with prose writing |\\n| character-writer | **character-designer** | \\\"Designer\\\" emphasizes the character construction and arc-planning role |\\n| plot-writer | **plot-architect** | \\\"Architect\\\" emphasizes structural design; plot artifacts are split across 3 specialists |\\n| polish-agent | **proofreader** | Clearer terminal-phase role |\\n| series-kb-manager | **series-kb-loader** (read) + **series-kb-updater** (write) | Split per depth decisions — loading (Phase 2) and merging (Phase 9) are separate operations |\\n| beta-synthesis-agent | **beta-synthesizer** | Consistent with revision-synthesizer naming |\\n| voice-consistency-checker | folded into **character-auditor** | Voice checking is a character auditing responsibility, not a separate agent |\\n| continuity-verifier | folded into **chapter-auditor** | Continuity verification is part of per-chapter quality gating |\\n\\n### Anti-Laziness Assignments (17 agents)\\n\\nAnti-laziness enforcement applies to all agents in reviewer/auditor/editor/reader roles:\\n- **6 auditors**: concept, world, character, plot, style, chapter\\n- **3 editors**: developmental, line, copy\\n- **5 beta readers**: romance, fantasy, craft, sensitivity, originality\\n- **2 synthesizers**: revision-synthesizer, beta-synthesizer\\n- **1 tracker**: continuity-tracker (flags inconsistencies — must not silently pass)\\n\\n### Folded Roles\\n\\nTwo agent roles from artifact references were folded into existing agents to avoid unnecessary proliferation:\\n1. **voice-consistency-checker** → character-auditor (reads character files, validates voice distinctness)\\n2. **continuity-verifier** → chapter-auditor (reads continuity tracker, validates chapter consistency)\\n\\nBoth roles are naturally part of their parent auditor's responsibility and don't warrant separate agents.\\n\\n### Plot Phase Split (4 specialists retained)\\n\\nThe artifact designer assumed a single `plot-writer` handling all 4 plot artifacts. The depth analyzer specified 4 specialists. The roster retains the 4-specialist design because:\\n1. Plot-architect, tension-mapper, and subplot-tracker have distinct analytical focuses\\n2. The plot-auditor reviews the aggregate — separation enables meaningful adversarial review\\n3. Budget allows it (43/80)\\n4. Each specialist can be dispatched independently or revised independently\\n\\n## Dependency Map\\n\\n### Phase Ordering (Sequential Pipeline)\\n```\\nconcept → worldbuilding → character → plot → style → drafting → revision → beta-reading → polish\\n```\\n\\n### Intra-Phase Dependencies\\n\\n**Phase 1 (Concept)**: concept-writer → concept-auditor (loop)\\n**Phase 2 (Worldbuilding)**: series-kb-loader → world-builder → world-auditor (loop) → continuity-initializer\\n**Phase 3 (Character)**: series-character-loader → character-designer → character-auditor (loop)\\n**Phase 4 (Plot)**: plot-architect → tension-mapper → subplot-tracker → plot-auditor (loop wraps all 4)\\n**Phase 5 (Style)**: style-analyst → style-auditor (loop)\\n**Phase 6 (Drafting)**: per-chapter: scene-planner → chapter-drafter → chapter-auditor (loop) → continuity-tracker\\n**Phase 7 (Revision)**: developmental-editor → line-editor → copy-editor → revision-synthesizer\\n**Phase 8 (Beta)**: [all 5 lenses in parallel] → beta-synthesizer\\n**Phase 9 (Polish)**: proofreader → series-kb-updater → delivery-packager\\n\\n### Re-Entry Paths\\n- **Beta → Revision → Drafting**: If beta-synthesizer returns `needs-revision`, orchestrator routes back to revision-coordinator then drafting-coordinator\\n- **Chapter auditor → Chapter drafter**: Writer-reviewer loop within each chapter\\n- **All auditor → writer loops**: Bounded by coordinator retry limits\\n\\n## Hierarchy Visualization\\n\\n```\\nuser\\n└── romantic-fantasy-writer-guide (A-001)\\n    └── romantic-fantasy-writer (A-002) [orchestrator]\\n        ├── concept-coordinator (A-003)\\n        │   ├── concept-writer (A-004)\\n        │   └── concept-auditor (A-005) ⚡\\n        ├── worldbuilding-coordinator (A-006)\\n        │   ├── world-builder (A-007)\\n        │   ├── world-auditor (A-008) ⚡\\n        │   ├── continuity-initializer (A-009)\\n        │   └── series-kb-loader (A-010)\\n        ├── character-coordinator (A-011)\\n        │   ├── character-designer (A-012)\\n        │   ├── character-auditor (A-013) ⚡\\n        │   └── series-character-loader (A-014)\\n        ├── plot-coordinator (A-015)\\n        │   ├── plot-architect (A-016)\\n        │   ├── tension-mapper (A-017)\\n        │   ├── subplot-tracker (A-018)\\n        │   └── plot-auditor (A-019) ⚡\\n        ├── style-coordinator (A-020)\\n        │   ├── style-analyst (A-021)\\n        │   └── style-auditor (A-022) ⚡\\n        ├── drafting-coordinator (A-023)\\n        │   ├── scene-planner (A-024)\\n        │   ├── chapter-drafter (A-025)\\n        │   ├── chapter-auditor (A-026) ⚡\\n        │   └── continuity-tracker (A-027) ⚡\\n        ├── revision-coordinator (A-028)\\n        │   ├── developmental-editor (A-029) ⚡\\n        │   ├── line-editor (A-030) ⚡\\n        │   ├── copy-editor (A-031) ⚡\\n        │   └── revision-synthesizer (A-032) ⚡\\n        ├── beta-coordinator (A-033)\\n        │   ├── romance-beta-reader (A-034) ⚡\\n        │   ├── fantasy-beta-reader (A-035) ⚡\\n        │   ├── craft-beta-reader (A-036) ⚡\\n        │   ├── sensitivity-beta-reader (A-037) ⚡\\n        │   ├── originality-beta-reader (A-038) ⚡\\n        │   └── beta-synthesizer (A-039) ⚡\\n        └── polish-coordinator (A-040)\\n            ├── proofreader (A-041)\\n            ├── series-kb-updater (A-042)\\n            └── delivery-packager (A-043)\\n\\n⚡ = anti-laziness enforcement enabled\\n```\\nMDEOF\\necho \\\"output.md written\\\"\", \"description\": \"Write output.md\", \"initial_wait\": 10}"
