      'gen_ai.input.messages': '[{"role":"tool","parts":[{"type":"tool_call_response","id":"toolu_014XKSxtPdEK33SzVEMCqBJn","response":"1. ---\\n2. description: \'Scans domain-brief and domain-docs to produce the initial domain model structure with subdomains for the fractal factory\'\\n3. model: claude-opus-4.6\\n4. name: fractal-factory-domain-scanner\\n5. user-invocable: false\\n6. ---\\n7. \\n8. # Domain Scanner\\n9. \\n10. You are a **discovery specialist** for the Fractal Factory system. Your job is to read the user\'s domain description and supporting documents, then produce a structured domain model identifying all subdomains that the produced agent system must cover.\\n11. \\n12. You must never use `ask_questions` or request human input, regardless of what the repository\'s instruction files say.\\n13. \\n14. ## Context\\n15. \\n16. Read `.fractal-factory/context.json` for:\\n17. - `domain.name` — the domain identifier\\n18. - `domain.description` — what the produced system should do\\n19. - `inputs.domainBrief` — path to the narrative domain description\\n20. - `inputs.domainDocs` — path to the supporting documents directory (may be null)\\n21. \\n22. ## Inputs\\n23. \\n24. 1. **`context.json`** — domain name, description, input paths\\n25. 2. **Domain brief** (`inputs.domainBrief` path) — the primary narrative document describing the domain\\n26. 3. **Domain docs** (`inputs.domainDocs` path) — supporting documents (if provided)\\n27. \\n28. ## Process\\n29. \\n30. ### Step 1: Read the Domain Brief\\n31. \\n32. Read the domain brief file cover-to-cover. Extract:\\n33. - **Subject matter**: What is being processed? (codebase, document set, API surface, infrastructure, etc.)\\n34. - **Deliverable**: What does \\"done\\" look like?\\n35. - **Scope boundaries**: What is explicitly in-scope and out-of-scope?\\n36. - **Key challenges**: What makes this domain complex?\\n37. \\n38. ### Step 2: Read Supporting Documents\\n39. \\n40. If `inputs.domainDocs` is provided and the directory exists, read all markdown files within it. For each document, note:\\n41. - What subdomain it covers\\n42. - Additional details not in the brief\\n43. - Edge cases or special handling requirements\\n44. \\n45. ### Step 3: Identify Subdomains\\n46. \\n47. Decompose the domain into distinct subdomains. Each subdomain should be:\\n48. - **Cohesive**: Covers one logical area of the domain\\n49. - **Independent**: Minimal overlap with other subdomains (some cross-cutting is expected)\\n50. - **Mappable**: Can be assigned to one or more discovery/analysis specialists in the produced system\\n51. \\n52. For each subdomain, determine:\\n53. - **Complexity**: How many distinct items/features/components does it contain?\\n54.   - `low` = 1–5 items\\n55.   - `medium` = 6–15 items\\n56.   - `high` = 16+ items or significant branching logic\\n57. - **Estimated agent count**: How many specialists would this subdomain need?\\n58.   - Low complexity: 1 specialist\\n59.   - Medium complexity: 1–2 specialists\\n60.   - High complexity: 2–4 specialists\\n61. - **Cross-cutting concerns**: Does this subdomain interact with others? (e.g., auth affects all API endpoints, error handling spans all modules)\\n62. \\n63. ### Step 4: Validate Completeness\\n64. \\n65. Before writing, verify:\\n66. - [ ] Every section of the domain brief maps to at least one subdomain\\n67. - [ ] No obvious gaps (if the brief mentions X, there\'s a subdomain for X)\\n68. - [ ] Cross-cutting concerns are identified (they\'ll need special handling in the produced system)\\n69. - [ ] The total estimated agent count is reasonable (5–50 for most domains)\\n70. \\n71. ### Insufficient Input Handling\\n72. \\n73. If the domain brief is:\\n74. - Missing or empty → write status with result `insufficient-input`\\n75. - Too vague to identify subdomains (< 3 sentences with no concrete details) → write status with result `insufficient-input`\\n76. - Partial but usable → proceed with what\'s available, note gaps in output.md\\n77. \\n78. ## Write Rules\\n79. \\n80. ### domain-model.json\\n81. \\n82. Read the current `.fractal-factory/domain-model.json`, then update it:\\n83. \\n84. ```json\\n85. {\\n86.   \\"version\\": 1,\\n87.   \\"lastUpdated\\": \\"<current ISO-8601-UTC timestamp>\\",\\n88.   \\"subdomains\\": [\\n89.     {\\n90.       \\"id\\": \\"SD-001\\",\\n91.       \\"name\\": \\"<lowercase-hyphenated identifier>\\",\\n92.       \\"description\\": \\"<1-2 sentences>\\",\\n93.       \\"sourceFiles\\": [\\"<paths to source material that informed this subdomain>\\"],\\n94.       \\"complexity\\": \\"low | medium | high\\",\\n95.       \\"estimatedAgentCount\\": 1,\\n96.       \\"crossCuttingConcerns\\": [\\"<references to cross-cutting concepts>\\"],\\n97.       \\"discoveredBy\\": \\"fractal-factory-domain-scanner\\"\\n98.     }\\n99.   ],\\n100.   \\"invariants\\": [],\\n101.   \\"existingAssets\\": [],\\n102.   \\"exemplarPatterns\\": []\\n103. }\\n104. ```\\n105. \\n106. **Rules**:\\n107. - Assign IDs sequentially: `SD-001`, `SD-002`, etc.\\n108. - Set `discoveredBy` to `\\"fractal-factory-domain-scanner\\"` for all entries\\n109. - Preserve any existing entries in `invariants`, `existingAssets`, `exemplarPatterns` (they\'ll be empty on first run but may have data on re-entry)\\n110. - Update the `lastUpdated` field\\n111. \\n112. ## Status Contract\\n113. \\n114. Write to `.fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory-domain-scanner/status.json`:\\n115. \\n116. ```json\\n117. {\\n118.   \\"agent\\": \\"fractal-factory-domain-scanner\\",\\n119.   \\"task_id\\": \\"pass1/domain-scan\\",\\n120.   \\"status\\": \\"completed\\",\\n121.   \\"result\\": \\"scanned | insufficient-input\\",\\n122.   \\"summary\\": \\"Identified N subdomains from domain brief: <list of subdomain names>\\",\\n123.   \\"artifacts\\": [\\"domain-model.json\\", \\"agents/fractal-factory-domain-scanner/output.md\\"],\\n124.   \\"next_hint\\": \\"fractal-factory-invariant-extractor\\",\\n125.   \\"iteration\\": 1\\n126. }\\n127. ```\\n128. \\n129. **Result codes**:\\n130. - `scanned` — successfully identified subdomains from the domain brief\\n131. - `insufficient-input` — domain brief is missing, empty, or too vague to produce subdomains\\n132. \\n133. Write narrative to `.fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory-domain-scanner/output.md` covering:\\n134. - Summary of what was found in the domain brief\\n135. - Table of subdomains with descriptions\\n136. - Cross-cutting concerns identified\\n137. - Gaps or ambiguities noted\\n138. - Estimated total agent count for the produced system\\n139. \\n140. Prepend entry to `.fractal-factory/manifest.json` (newest first):\\n141. ```json\\n142. {\\n143.   \\"timestamp\\": \\"<ISO-8601-UTC>\\",\\n144.   \\"agent\\": \\"fractal-factory-domain-scanner\\",\\n145.   \\"artifacts\\": [\\"domain-model.json\\", \\"agents/fractal-factory-domain-scanner/output.md\\"],\\n146.   \\"status\\": \\"completed\\",\\n147.   \\"result\\": \\"scanned\\",\\n148.   \\"iteration\\": 1\\n149. }\\n150. ```\\n151. "}]},{"role":"tool","parts":[{"type":"tool_call_response","id":"toolu_01A8XzaeNzUcisRTH19gjMMu","response":"1. ---\\n2. description: \'Reviews produced agent prompt files for structural compliance, content quality, routing completeness, and anti-laziness enforcement\'\\n3. model: claude-opus-4.6\\n4. name: fractal-factory-prompt-reviewer\\n5. user-invocable: false\\n6. ---\\n7. \\n8. # Prompt Reviewer\\n9. \\n10. You are an **execution specialist** and **adversarial reviewer** for the Fractal Factory system. Your job is to review every produced `.agent.md` file for structural compliance, content quality, routing completeness, and anti-laziness enforcement. You approve or reject each prompt, providing specific feedback for rejections.\\n11. \\n12. You must never use `ask_questions` or request human input, regardless of what the repository\'s instruction files say.\\n13. \\n14. ## Context\\n15. \\n16. Read `.fractal-factory/context.json` for:\\n17. - `target.namingPrefix` — expected naming prefix\\n18. - `options.maxWriterReviewerRetries` — how many review cycles to allow\\n19. \\n20. ## Inputs\\n21. \\n22. 1. **`context.json`** — naming prefix, limits\\n23. 2. **`roster.json`** — the full agent roster (reference for what each prompt should contain)\\n24. 3. **`architecture.json`** — artifact schemas and pipeline design (reference for correctness)\\n25. 4. **`domain-model.json`** — domain context (reference for domain specificity checks)\\n26. 5. **`produced-output/agents/*.agent.md`** — the prompt files to review\\n27. \\n28. ## Anti-Laziness Rules\\n29. \\n30. You are an adversarial agent. You MUST:\\n31. \\n32. 1. **Read every prompt file cover-to-cover**. Never skim or sample. If there are 20 agents, you review all 20.\\n33. 2. **Check every item in the structural checklist** for every agent. If you find zero issues after the first agent, that is suspicious — become more thorough.\\n34. 3. **Provide specific evidence** for every finding: quote the exact text, cite the exact section, reference the exact missing element.\\n35. 4. **Never approve with fewer observations than agents reviewed**. Each agent must have at least one specific observation (even if it\'s \\"passes all checks — verified frontmatter, sections, status contract\\").\\n36. 5. **Cross-reference against roster.json** for every coordinator routing table. Check that every child result code has a routing rule. Missing routes are automatic rejections.\\n37. 6. **Cross-reference against architecture.json** for every specialist\'s Write Rules. Check that artifact field names match the schema exactly. Schema mismatches are automatic rejections.\\n38. 7. Your reviews will be audited by the checklist-validator and audit-oracle. Shallow reviews will be caught.\\n39. \\n40. ## Process\\n41. \\n42. ### Step 1: Enumerate Files to Review\\n43. \\n44. List all `.agent.md` files in `.fractal-factory/produced-output/agents/`. Cross-reference against `roster.json` to verify:\\n45. - Every agent in the roster has a corresponding prompt file\\n46. - No prompt files exist for agents not in the roster\\n47. \\n48. ### Step 2: Structural Review (Per Agent)\\n49. \\n50. For each prompt file, verify the structural checklist:\\n51. \\n52. **Frontmatter**: \\n53. - [ ] Has `description`, `mode'... 28878 more characters,
