ctural and behavioral checklist, then perform deep compliance audit against agent-as-function and domain invariant requirements\\n\\nPass ?: gapHunting - Adversarially search for missing coverage, orphaned references, unenforced invariants, and architectural gaps across the entire produced agent family\\n\\nPass ?: delivery - Package the complete romantic-fantasy-writer agent family into the output directory, write architecture documentation, and produce the final delivery report with quality metrics\\n<exited with exit code 0>"}]},{"role":"tool","parts":[{"type":"tool_call_response","id":"toolu_016q3DJKTHN6xfNmwRQWtpXC","response":"Top-level keys: ['version', 'lastUpdated', 'subdomains', 'invariants', 'existingAssets', 'exemplarPatterns']\\nSubdomains (17):\\n  - user-interaction: Guide agent as sole user-facing entry point: gathers story idea, optional style \\n  - concept-development: Phase 1 of the creative pipeline: distills raw inputs into a crystallized story \\n  - world-building: Phase 2: constructs the complete fictional world in subcategorized artifacts. Co\\n  - character-design: Phase 3: creates full character profiles for romantic leads (backstory, psycholo\\n  - plot-architecture: Phase 4: selects and applies a story structure framework (3-Act, Save the Cat, H\\n  - prose-style-development: Phase 5: if reference stories are provided, analyzes them for abstract stylistic\\n  - chapter-drafting: Phase 6: the core prose production engine. Writes each chapter sequentially foll\\n  - revision-editing: Phase 7: exhaustive multi-pass self-editing. Developmental edit (plot holes, pac\\n  - beta-reading-simulation: Phase 8: deep multi-perspective simulated beta reading through 5 independent rev\\n  - polish-delivery: Phase 9: final proofread for typos/formatting/consistency, generation of one-par\\n  - adversarial-quality-gates: Cross-cutting system of adversarial consistency auditors that gate every creativ\\n  - continuity-tracking: Cross-cutting system for 