ter, elapsed: 474s, total_turns: 1\\n\\n[Turn 0]\\nAll artifacts are clean and validated. Here\'s the roster planning summary:\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Roster Planning Complete ✅\\n\\n### Result: `planned` — 43 agents for the romantic-fantasy-writer system\\n\\n| Level | Count | Description |\\n|-------|-------|-------------|\\n| Guide | 1 | `romantic-fantasy-writer-guide` — user-facing entry point |\\n| Orchestrator | 1 | `romantic-fantasy-writer` — 9-phase sequential pipeline dispatcher |\\n| Coordinator | 9 | One per creative phase (concept → worldbuilding → character → plot → style → drafting → revision → beta-reading → polish) |\\n| Specialist | 32 | Writers, auditors, editors, beta readers, trackers, loaders, packagers |\\n| **Total** | **43** | **54% of 80-agent budget** |\\n\\n### Key Design Decisions\\n\\n1. **All depth-2** — Every coordinator manages 2-6 specialists directly. No sub-coordinators needed (all below the 8-specialist threshold).\\n\\n2. **17 anti-laziness agents** — Every auditor, editor, beta reader, synthesizer, and the continuity tracker have anti-laziness enforcement to prevent rubber-stamping.\\n\\n3. **Naming reconciliation** — Established canonical names that are more descriptive than the artifact designer\'s pre-references (e.g., `world-builder` not `world-writer`, `plot-architect` not `plot-writer`). Two artifact-referenced roles folded into existing agents (`voice-consistency-checker` → `character-auditor`, `continuity-verifier` → `chapter-auditor`).\\n\\n4. **Series KB split** — The single `series-kb-manager` from artifact design was split into `series-kb-loader` (Phase 2, read-only) and `series-kb-updater` (Phase 9, write/merge) per depth analysis.\\n\\n5. **37-agent headroom** — Leaves room for future expansion if any phase needs depth-3 escalation.\\n\\n### Written Artifacts\\n- `.fractal-factory/roster.json` — Full 43-agent roster with hierarchy, result codes, artifact assignments\\n- `.fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory-roster-plan